1
00:00:31,159 --> 00:00:35,147
We only have half a day left.

2
00:00:35,147 --> 00:00:36,949
Everyone keeps asking.

3
00:00:36,949 --> 00:00:39,384
[Did they get the new dish on the menu?]
Did they complete the final mission?

4
00:00:39,384 --> 00:00:41,086
I haven't even told my son.

5
00:00:41,086 --> 00:00:42,992
You really didn't tell him?
Doesn't he get curious?

6
00:00:42,992 --> 00:00:45,959
He goes, "Can't you tell just me?"

7
00:00:45,959 --> 00:00:47,593
So I told him, "Just watch."

8
00:00:47,593 --> 00:00:48,527
Of course!

9
00:00:48,527 --> 00:00:51,096
Developing the menu matters too,

10
00:00:51,096 --> 00:00:53,660
but I was also thinking about
how to reveal my identity at the end.

11
00:00:53,660 --> 00:00:55,426
How to end it dramatically.

12
00:00:55,426 --> 00:00:56,326
[Exactly]
Right.

13
00:00:56,326 --> 00:00:58,760
What Sung Jun is focusing on most right now...

14
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:00,072
This matters most.

15
00:01:00,072 --> 00:01:04,076
is how he'll reveal his identity.

16
00:01:04,076 --> 00:01:05,277
That's what I'm most excited about.

17
00:01:05,277 --> 00:01:09,113
[What will happen after the reveal?]
You'll all find out later.

18
00:01:09,882 --> 00:01:11,483
[Parma's Hee Tae, a former LA farmer]

19
00:01:11,483 --> 00:01:13,452
I'm Sunny from Korea.

20
00:01:13,452 --> 00:01:14,992
[Chengdu's Sunny, a former boxer]

21
00:01:14,992 --> 00:01:18,390
[Swaggering Naples Kwon, ex-ballplayer]

22
00:01:18,390 --> 00:01:22,160
[How will the chefs reveal themselves?]

23
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:24,396
Who is that person?

24
00:01:24,396 --> 00:01:26,365
[The queen of Chinese cuisine?]

25
00:01:26,365 --> 00:01:28,259
[Shock]
[Hee Tae!]

26
00:01:28,259 --> 00:01:29,601
[Oh...]
Kwon Sun Jun...

27
00:01:29,601 --> 00:01:30,802
[A final moment of mixed emotions]

28
00:01:30,802 --> 00:01:33,137
[More from Undercover Chef, coming soon]

29
00:01:34,393 --> 00:01:35,474
[Parma, Italy: Hee Tae, not Sam Kim]
This is it.

30
00:01:35,474 --> 00:01:36,775
I think they'll freak out.

31
00:01:36,775 --> 00:01:38,644
[Day 5, near the end of lunch service]

32
00:01:38,644 --> 00:01:41,780
[Hee Tae agonizes over the final mission]

33
00:01:41,780 --> 00:01:43,248
[He writes something out and shows them]

34
00:01:43,248 --> 00:01:44,716
What I wrote was,

35
00:01:44,716 --> 00:01:47,386
"I'm opening a restaurant in Korea,

36
00:01:47,386 --> 00:01:49,026
and there's a dish I want to make.

37
00:01:49,026 --> 00:01:51,790
Could you give me your opinion?"

38
00:01:51,790 --> 00:01:53,393
[He'll serve the new dish at staff dinner]
Okay.

39
00:01:53,393 --> 00:01:55,593
- Tonight, right?
- Yes, tonight.

40
00:01:55,593 --> 00:01:57,092
[If they like it, he'll pitch the dish]
Okay.

41
00:01:57,092 --> 00:02:00,399
He carefully tested the waters.

42
00:02:00,399 --> 00:02:05,259
Can I start prepping at 6:00 PM?

43
00:02:05,259 --> 00:02:06,572
Of course.

44
00:02:06,572 --> 00:02:09,241
[What will happen to Hee Tae's new dish?]
- Is that okay? - Yes.

45
00:02:09,241 --> 00:02:12,678
[Now, the moment of truth]

46
00:02:12,678 --> 00:02:16,014
[Current time: 6:00 PM]
[A determined walk into the final mission]

47
00:02:16,014 --> 00:02:17,560
[Hee Tae, Final mission ahead]
I started getting nervous.

48
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:19,718
If they knew nothing about me,

49
00:02:19,718 --> 00:02:24,460
would they see me
as someone suited for the kitchen?

50
00:02:24,460 --> 00:02:27,392
[Not just the new dish]
I was worried about the dish,

51
00:02:27,392 --> 00:02:29,428
[The big identity reveal still awaits]
and when I revealed who I was,

52
00:02:29,428 --> 00:02:32,831
I wondered what they'd think.

53
00:02:32,831 --> 00:02:35,200
I have a feeling when he reveals himself,

54
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,302
the other chefs will say, "I knew it."

55
00:02:37,302 --> 00:02:39,671
- For one thing, it doesn't add up.
- His whole story makes no sense.

56
00:02:39,671 --> 00:02:42,259
[The LA farmer's true identity, soon]
I'm really curious how they'll react.

57
00:02:42,259 --> 00:02:45,526
[He bolts straight to the pantry]

58
00:02:45,526 --> 00:02:47,860
What will he get from the pantry?

59
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:49,948
What will he make?

60
00:02:49,948 --> 00:02:52,144
[There's a lot here]

61
00:02:53,259 --> 00:02:56,454
[What ingredients and flavors will he use?]
What will he make?

62
00:02:57,689 --> 00:03:00,792
[Beef]

63
00:03:00,792 --> 00:03:03,662
[Two carrots]

64
00:03:03,662 --> 00:03:05,831
[And...]

65
00:03:05,831 --> 00:03:07,393
[Something brown?]

66
00:03:07,393 --> 00:03:09,167
I'm curious.

67
00:03:10,402 --> 00:03:12,259
[Gianpietro arrives!]

68
00:03:12,259 --> 00:03:14,672
[What we got at the Asian market that morning!]
- So fresh. - Right.

69
00:03:15,326 --> 00:03:17,193
Shiitake mushrooms.

70
00:03:17,193 --> 00:03:18,176
Shiitake.

71
00:03:18,176 --> 00:03:20,111
They're fresh!

72
00:03:21,446 --> 00:03:23,982
[Beef, carrots, and shiitake make... what?]
Let's see what he makes.

73
00:03:23,982 --> 00:03:24,983
[Maybe beef bulgogi?]

74
00:03:24,983 --> 00:03:26,018
Huh?

75
00:03:26,018 --> 00:03:27,986
- It's not bulgogi.
- Bulgogi?

76
00:03:27,986 --> 00:03:29,426
Why bulgogi all of a sudden?

77
00:03:29,426 --> 00:03:31,256
[No more bulgogi!]

78
00:03:31,256 --> 00:03:34,259
[Will he follow Japchae with Korean food?]
But the Japchae went over well.

79
00:03:34,259 --> 00:03:36,495
[Lucrezia spots the shiitake]

80
00:03:36,495 --> 00:03:40,959
I've never seen mushrooms that dark before.

81
00:03:40,959 --> 00:03:42,626
Really?

82
00:03:42,626 --> 00:03:45,437
[Though they use porcini and truffles]

83
00:03:45,437 --> 00:03:48,073
[Shiitake is unfamiliar to Italians]

84
00:03:48,073 --> 00:03:50,426
[And more...]

85
00:03:50,426 --> 00:03:52,410
What's this?

86
00:03:54,046 --> 00:03:55,781
Is that corn syrup?

87
00:03:55,781 --> 00:03:57,849
Sweet cooking wine and cheongju.

88
00:03:57,849 --> 00:03:59,251
- Cooking wine.
- They had some there.

89
00:03:59,251 --> 00:04:00,485
Really?

90
00:04:00,485 --> 00:04:01,793
Dolce Sake.

91
00:04:01,793 --> 00:04:03,288
I'm curious.

92
00:04:03,288 --> 00:04:04,289
Let's see.

93
00:04:04,289 --> 00:04:06,858
[Why these ingredients?]

94
00:04:06,858 --> 00:04:08,727
After five days at this restaurant,

95
00:04:08,727 --> 00:04:12,364
the dishes on the menu are all pretty basic.

96
00:04:12,364 --> 00:04:13,359
[Parma classics dominate the menu]

97
00:04:13,359 --> 00:04:14,800
This is a traditional place.

98
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:19,171
If a foreigner made something
they're already so familiar with,

99
00:04:19,171 --> 00:04:22,726
it'd just look like he was copying them.

100
00:04:22,726 --> 00:04:26,111
[So he adds something fresh]
I needed a new combination

101
00:04:26,111 --> 00:04:29,760
so they'd find it different and fresh.

102
00:04:29,760 --> 00:04:32,617
[At today's staff lunch]
It's so, so good!

103
00:04:32,617 --> 00:04:37,255
[His accidental Japchae earns rave reviews]

104
00:04:37,255 --> 00:04:39,624
[That gives Hee Tae an idea]
They loved that too.

105
00:04:39,624 --> 00:04:41,393
A perfect dish.

106
00:04:41,393 --> 00:04:43,095
[After a lot of thought]
I kept going back and forth,

107
00:04:43,095 --> 00:04:46,164
but if I made what they usually eat...

108
00:04:46,164 --> 00:04:47,793
[If he makes what Italians usually eat]
Well...

109
00:04:47,793 --> 00:04:49,526
They'd say, "He made the same old thing,"

110
00:04:49,526 --> 00:04:52,871
[Too ordinary to become a new menu item]
or, "It's blander than ours."

111
00:04:52,871 --> 00:04:54,860
[Adding something to Italian food]
- Blander? - So I thought about

112
00:04:54,860 --> 00:04:59,444
how they'd react to Asian flavors.

113
00:04:59,444 --> 00:05:03,115
[Italian food with an Asian twist?]
You're adding Korean flavors to it?

114
00:05:03,115 --> 00:05:04,793
For the cooking itself,

115
00:05:04,793 --> 00:05:07,652
[The cooking techniques stay Italian]
I'd follow their methods,

116
00:05:07,652 --> 00:05:09,821
[But he boldly adds Asian flair]
but wherever I could change things,

117
00:05:09,821 --> 00:05:11,923
I'd add my own style

118
00:05:11,923 --> 00:05:16,660
so they'd think, "He has a good palate.

119
00:05:16,660 --> 00:05:19,326
He puts thought into his food.

120
00:05:19,326 --> 00:05:22,300
He understands the basics."

121
00:05:22,300 --> 00:05:25,337
[Will Hee Tae's bold choice work?]
That's what I wanted to show.

122
00:05:25,337 --> 00:05:27,973
Whether to preserve the current menu's style

123
00:05:27,973 --> 00:05:29,092
- Right.
- or

124
00:05:29,092 --> 00:05:30,976
whether to introduce something different

125
00:05:30,976 --> 00:05:34,279
was what I struggled with most
when choosing the dish.

126
00:05:34,279 --> 00:05:37,259
I think a plate needs to show

127
00:05:37,259 --> 00:05:39,226
- who I am.
- It has to come through.

128
00:05:39,226 --> 00:05:41,086
It's not a bad approach.

129
00:05:41,086 --> 00:05:42,354
[What new dish will Hee Tae unveil?]

130
00:05:42,354 --> 00:05:44,490
What could the dish be?

131
00:05:44,490 --> 00:05:46,291
I'm curious.

132
00:05:47,626 --> 00:05:51,126
This is actually the beef left over
from the Japchae at lunch.

133
00:05:51,126 --> 00:05:52,831
Right.

134
00:05:52,831 --> 00:05:56,760
[He starts cutting the carrots]

135
00:05:56,760 --> 00:05:59,471
Cutting them that thick, it must be a braise.

136
00:05:59,471 --> 00:06:01,173
This...

137
00:06:01,173 --> 00:06:02,940
You'll see.

138
00:06:04,209 --> 00:06:07,044
[Sniff]

139
00:06:09,181 --> 00:06:11,183
[Sniff]

140
00:06:11,183 --> 00:06:13,293
[Why is he smelling the shiitake?]
Why is he smelling it?

141
00:06:13,293 --> 00:06:18,123
I need to smell the shiitake first
to decide on the base.

142
00:06:18,123 --> 00:06:20,432
[Shiitake aroma is the key]
They're packed with aroma.

143
00:06:20,432 --> 00:06:21,712
So...

144
00:06:21,712 --> 00:06:25,326
[But moments earlier]
[Sniff]

145
00:06:25,326 --> 00:06:26,331
[Oh, man...]

146
00:06:26,331 --> 00:06:28,065
- What's wrong?
- Huh?

147
00:06:28,900 --> 00:06:31,560
The aroma's too weak.

148
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:35,974
The shiitake barely had any aroma. None at all.

149
00:06:35,974 --> 00:06:38,510
It was too weak.

150
00:06:38,510 --> 00:06:40,712
The shiitake aroma isn't very strong.

151
00:06:40,712 --> 00:06:42,214
- It's not strong?
- Yeah, it's weak.

152
00:06:42,214 --> 00:06:44,216
Isn't shiitake supposed to smell stronger?

153
00:06:44,216 --> 00:06:47,352
- Is it usually stronger?
- Yes.

154
00:06:47,352 --> 00:06:49,855
The mushroom aroma is weak.

155
00:06:49,855 --> 00:06:52,560
[Hee Tae springs into action]

156
00:06:52,560 --> 00:06:57,660
Soaking shiitake in hot water
gives you a deeply aromatic broth.

157
00:06:57,660 --> 00:06:59,326
[Hee Tae's clever fix!]
It turns almost black.

158
00:06:59,326 --> 00:07:04,069
I'm separating the more aromatic ones

159
00:07:04,069 --> 00:07:07,193
and picking out the strongest-smelling stems.

160
00:07:07,193 --> 00:07:08,707
[He separates the stems and caps]

161
00:07:08,707 --> 00:07:11,309
You're using the best, most fragrant ones.

162
00:07:11,309 --> 00:07:12,693
I separated them.

163
00:07:12,693 --> 00:07:15,146
That's incredibly detailed.

164
00:07:15,947 --> 00:07:18,350
I'm making shiitake stock.

165
00:07:18,350 --> 00:07:20,818
[Fascinating]
Okay.

166
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:23,426
[He starts stock with shiitake stems]
I'm curious.

167
00:07:23,426 --> 00:07:25,189
Let's see.

168
00:07:26,858 --> 00:07:30,095
[He catches a strong mushroom aroma]

169
00:07:30,095 --> 00:07:33,793
[A spoon comes out right away]
He must want to check how it's coming along.

170
00:07:33,793 --> 00:07:36,401
[He tastes it right away]

171
00:07:36,401 --> 00:07:40,405
[He silently nods]

172
00:07:40,405 --> 00:07:42,440
If I'd had more time,

173
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:46,544
I would've used only the mushroom stems.

174
00:07:46,544 --> 00:07:49,593
The bottom part is the stem. The stem.

175
00:07:49,593 --> 00:07:50,927
[Hee Tae wishes he had more time]

176
00:07:50,927 --> 00:07:53,827
Thyme, onion, yes.

177
00:07:53,827 --> 00:07:55,987
- Is it beef?
- Yes, it's beef.

178
00:07:55,987 --> 00:07:57,589
[Beef, thyme, shiitake, onion, carrot]
[Everything simmers together]

179
00:07:57,589 --> 00:08:01,293
[Carefully making stock despite the rush]

180
00:08:01,293 --> 00:08:04,262
[Chop]

181
00:08:04,262 --> 00:08:05,263
The shiitake caps.

182
00:08:05,263 --> 00:08:07,265
[He thinly slices the shiitake caps]

183
00:08:07,265 --> 00:08:10,035
[A pile of sliced shiitake caps]

184
00:08:10,035 --> 00:08:12,793
[Next, sniff]

185
00:08:12,793 --> 00:08:15,359
[Now he sniffs the cheongju!]
He keeps checking the aroma.

186
00:08:15,359 --> 00:08:16,374
Cheongju.

187
00:08:16,374 --> 00:08:18,310
[He adds cheongju for depth]

188
00:08:18,310 --> 00:08:19,377
[Boop]

189
00:08:19,377 --> 00:08:21,246
[Yikes!]

190
00:08:21,246 --> 00:08:22,849
[In goes plenty of sweet cooking wine]
[What is he making?]

191
00:08:22,849 --> 00:08:24,916
- What is it?
- Wait...

192
00:08:24,916 --> 00:08:26,351
[Straight to the stove]

193
00:08:26,351 --> 00:08:29,220
[Only cheongju and cooking wine inside]

194
00:08:29,220 --> 00:08:30,493
[Tilt]

195
00:08:30,493 --> 00:08:32,257
Huh?

196
00:08:32,257 --> 00:08:34,526
[He's setting it on fire?]
Huh?

197
00:08:34,526 --> 00:08:36,673
I thought using a technique
they didn't normally use

198
00:08:36,673 --> 00:08:38,964
would get their attention.

199
00:08:38,964 --> 00:08:41,032
[Cheongju and cooking wine flare up]

200
00:08:41,032 --> 00:08:45,903
[Flambe: igniting high-proof alcohol in a dish
to remove off-flavors and intensify aroma]

201
00:08:45,903 --> 00:08:48,606
I boiled it and added a little soy sauce.

202
00:08:48,606 --> 00:08:50,275
I needed to taste it.

203
00:08:50,275 --> 00:08:52,444
[Hee Tae's special sauce]

204
00:08:52,444 --> 00:08:55,065
- You put that much alcohol in a dish?
- Yes.

205
00:08:55,065 --> 00:08:58,817
As the alcohol cooks off,
the sauce gets sweeter.

206
00:08:58,817 --> 00:09:02,721
So the alcohol cooks off,
leaving the sweetness.

207
00:09:02,721 --> 00:09:07,692
There's an umami-packed
braised mushroom dish that's easy to make.

208
00:09:08,727 --> 00:09:10,729
[Not just mushroom stock]

209
00:09:10,729 --> 00:09:12,263
[Now braised mushrooms too?]

210
00:09:12,263 --> 00:09:13,264
Huh?

211
00:09:13,264 --> 00:09:15,500
[Still no idea what it is]

212
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:16,768
[A new Asian aroma fills the kitchen]

213
00:09:16,768 --> 00:09:18,336
[Glances]

214
00:09:18,336 --> 00:09:19,804
[Glances again]

215
00:09:19,804 --> 00:09:21,238
[Glances once more]

216
00:09:22,860 --> 00:09:25,210
What sauces did you add?

217
00:09:25,210 --> 00:09:26,811
- Soy sauce.
- Soy sauce.

218
00:09:26,811 --> 00:09:28,213
Cooking wine and cheongju.

219
00:09:28,213 --> 00:09:29,914
- Sweet sake?
- Yes.

220
00:09:29,914 --> 00:09:31,593
[Interesting...]

221
00:09:31,593 --> 00:09:32,984
It smells amazing!

222
00:09:32,984 --> 00:09:34,919
Thank you.

223
00:09:37,827 --> 00:09:41,092
[The aroma gets a thumbs-up]
Sam Kim kept checking the aroma too.

224
00:09:41,092 --> 00:09:44,095
[Now everyone's curious about the mushrooms]

225
00:09:44,929 --> 00:09:47,460
[Hee Tae gets the first taste]

226
00:09:47,460 --> 00:09:49,267
I added shiitake mushrooms and soy sauce.

227
00:09:49,267 --> 00:09:50,435
Really?

228
00:09:50,435 --> 00:09:52,526
[Give it a try!]

229
00:09:52,526 --> 00:09:54,739
[He says I can try it. Thank you]

230
00:09:54,739 --> 00:09:56,141
- Adorable.
- Adorable.

231
00:09:56,141 --> 00:09:59,026
Try the braised mushrooms.

232
00:09:59,026 --> 00:10:00,259
The braised mushrooms.

233
00:10:00,259 --> 00:10:02,847
- Everyone, come try some.
- Okay.

234
00:10:03,915 --> 00:10:08,086
[Everyone rushes over]

235
00:10:08,086 --> 00:10:09,754
[They were all dying to try it]
- Okay, the sauce. - The sauce.

236
00:10:09,754 --> 00:10:11,655
[They instantly switch to tasting mode]
I'm so curious.

237
00:10:13,059 --> 00:10:14,491
[Nervous...]
Let's see how it tastes.

238
00:10:14,491 --> 00:10:17,462
It should still be sweet
because of the cheongju.

239
00:10:17,462 --> 00:10:23,193
[Chomp goes the braised mushroom]

240
00:10:23,193 --> 00:10:24,235
[It's delicious!]

241
00:10:24,235 --> 00:10:27,005
That umami is just...

242
00:10:27,005 --> 00:10:30,175
[Sweet, salty, and tangy! A brand-new taste]

243
00:10:30,175 --> 00:10:32,560
[Is that the secret?]

244
00:10:32,560 --> 00:10:34,579
What's that?

245
00:10:34,579 --> 00:10:36,426
[The chefs go wild over cooking wine]

246
00:10:36,426 --> 00:10:39,593
- Can I smell it again?
- Cooking wine.

247
00:10:39,593 --> 00:10:42,220
I used equal parts cooking wine and cheongju!

248
00:10:42,220 --> 00:10:44,756
- And this.
- Is this soy sauce?

249
00:10:44,756 --> 00:10:46,793
[Questions pour in about the sauce]
This is soy sauce.

250
00:10:46,793 --> 00:10:48,493
[Busy explaining]
One scoop.

251
00:10:48,493 --> 00:10:50,159
[Eagerly]
What's this?

252
00:10:50,159 --> 00:10:51,963
- Bim.
- Bim?

253
00:10:51,963 --> 00:10:53,665
[Bright-eyed]
They're genuinely curious.

254
00:10:53,665 --> 00:10:57,035
When they even want to know the ingredients,
you know it must be really good.

255
00:10:57,035 --> 00:11:01,059
Honestly, ever since I made Japchae earlier,
they've been paying a lot more attention to me.

256
00:11:01,059 --> 00:11:02,607
[Hee Tae's food is all the buzz]
Exactly.

257
00:11:02,607 --> 00:11:06,226
[The Japchae effect]
The Japchae got a great response too.

258
00:11:06,226 --> 00:11:08,179
Everyone in the kitchen loved it!

259
00:11:08,179 --> 00:11:09,380
They said it was really good.

260
00:11:09,380 --> 00:11:11,226
[Excited]
They kept asking how I made it.

261
00:11:11,226 --> 00:11:13,226
I guess it was a dish they never expected.

262
00:11:13,226 --> 00:11:14,619
It had soy sauce,

263
00:11:14,619 --> 00:11:19,359
but they asked how it could still taste
and smell so much like shiitake.

264
00:11:19,359 --> 00:11:21,159
It made me glad I decided to make it.

265
00:11:21,159 --> 00:11:24,126
They're not used to alcohol without acidity,

266
00:11:24,126 --> 00:11:27,031
- so it probably tasted really fresh to them.
- Right.

267
00:11:27,031 --> 00:11:29,066
[Minced onion]

268
00:11:30,535 --> 00:11:32,859
[Olive oil]

269
00:11:34,339 --> 00:11:37,675
[After the stock and braised mushrooms]

270
00:11:37,675 --> 00:11:39,493
Excuse me.

271
00:11:39,493 --> 00:11:41,379
- Could I have some of this?
- Of course!

272
00:11:41,379 --> 00:11:43,259
[Butter]

273
00:11:43,259 --> 00:11:45,383
[What's he making now?]
Olive oil and butter.

274
00:11:45,383 --> 00:11:46,651
What could he be making?

275
00:11:46,651 --> 00:11:48,820
[Shake]

276
00:11:48,820 --> 00:11:51,856
[Finely chopped shiitake mushrooms?]
What's that?

277
00:11:51,856 --> 00:11:54,492
[Thyme adds another aromatic layer]

278
00:11:54,492 --> 00:11:58,496
[He checks the aroma again]

279
00:11:58,496 --> 00:12:00,393
[Finely sautéed minced mushrooms]

280
00:12:00,393 --> 00:12:01,833
That looks good.

281
00:12:01,833 --> 00:12:02,992
[Now the mushroom stock?]

282
00:12:02,992 --> 00:12:04,802
What?

283
00:12:05,628 --> 00:12:06,938
[Mushroom stock]
What's that?

284
00:12:06,938 --> 00:12:09,641
[Stock over the shiitake caps!]

285
00:12:09,641 --> 00:12:13,711
[The saved caps go into hot mushroom stock]

286
00:12:13,711 --> 00:12:17,582
[Extracting even more shiitake flavor!]

287
00:12:17,582 --> 00:12:20,417
[The minced mushrooms get sautéed again]

288
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:25,923
[In goes the shiitake extract!]

289
00:12:26,958 --> 00:12:30,996
[Something unusual catches his eye]

290
00:12:32,027 --> 00:12:33,464
[Stock, Braise, Sauté]
That looks delicious.

291
00:12:33,464 --> 00:12:35,166
[Maximum shiitake flavor and aroma]

292
00:12:35,166 --> 00:12:37,268
[Carefully building the flavor]
There are so many steps.

293
00:12:37,268 --> 00:12:41,105
I wanted to add a few more layers.

294
00:12:42,574 --> 00:12:43,708
[The three shiitake preparations rest]

295
00:12:43,708 --> 00:12:45,643
I'm most excited about this.

296
00:12:47,178 --> 00:12:49,480
[He picks up something else]

297
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:52,283
[Sprinkling sound]

298
00:12:52,283 --> 00:12:53,585
[A soft sprinkle]

299
00:12:53,585 --> 00:12:55,611
Hold on... No way.

300
00:12:56,421 --> 00:12:58,590
Is he really making that?

301
00:12:58,590 --> 00:12:59,791
Wait.

302
00:12:59,791 --> 00:13:02,360
Honestly, you don't know what it is!

303
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:04,593
[Spoiler alert]
I think he's making...

304
00:13:04,593 --> 00:13:06,831
[Oh]

305
00:13:06,831 --> 00:13:08,933
- Am I right?
- Really?

306
00:13:09,867 --> 00:13:13,626
[Rice]

307
00:13:13,626 --> 00:13:16,641
[Hee Tae's new dish: Shiitake risotto]
Honestly, they seem to...

308
00:13:16,641 --> 00:13:18,476
[Correct!]
really like risotto.

309
00:13:18,476 --> 00:13:20,011
If you steep them in hot water,

310
00:13:20,011 --> 00:13:23,014
you can make a broth
with an incredibly strong aroma.

311
00:13:23,014 --> 00:13:25,283
[Caps and stock together make an aroma booster]
Exactly.

312
00:13:25,283 --> 00:13:28,453
If you pour it in while making risotto,

313
00:13:28,453 --> 00:13:31,189
the rice absorbs all that aroma.

314
00:13:31,189 --> 00:13:34,760
[More shiitake stock as the risotto cooks!]

315
00:13:34,760 --> 00:13:37,726
[Why make the braised mushrooms?]
I have a simple way of braising mushrooms.

316
00:13:37,726 --> 00:13:41,466
[Adding Asian-style umami]
Adding that or fruit gives it sweetness,

317
00:13:41,466 --> 00:13:45,403
so I thought it might be good
to try them together...

318
00:13:45,403 --> 00:13:48,439
[They'll be used as a risotto topping]
So this time, you're going to finish it

319
00:13:48,439 --> 00:13:52,577
- with nothing but mushrooms.
- Exactly.

320
00:13:52,577 --> 00:13:55,680
[Lastly, the sautéed minced shiitake?]
My biggest concern was

321
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:58,560
unless it's a dessert,
even subtle sweetness can make you think,

322
00:13:58,560 --> 00:14:01,259
"Oh, that's a little..."

323
00:14:01,259 --> 00:14:03,726
[Shiitake minced smaller than the rice]
That part was difficult.

324
00:14:03,726 --> 00:14:05,723
[More mushroom flavor balances the sweetness]

325
00:14:05,723 --> 00:14:08,560
- It'll keep tasting good as you chew.
- The texture.

326
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:11,095
I had a lot on my mind while I was cooking.

327
00:14:11,095 --> 00:14:14,232
[All for the mushrooms and Asian flavor]
With so few ingredients, you're trying

328
00:14:14,232 --> 00:14:16,701
[Thinking and struggling every step]
to take it all the way.

329
00:14:16,701 --> 00:14:19,370
Even within that,
there was so much to consider.

330
00:14:19,370 --> 00:14:21,305
[A new dish that's pure Hee Tae]

331
00:14:23,408 --> 00:14:26,477
[The mushroom stock has reduced quite a bit]

332
00:14:27,645 --> 00:14:29,881
[Want me to squeeze out the juices?]

333
00:14:29,881 --> 00:14:31,026
[Perfect]

334
00:14:31,026 --> 00:14:32,850
Thank you.

335
00:14:32,850 --> 00:14:34,393
He stepped in at just the right moment.

336
00:14:34,393 --> 00:14:39,245
[Leaving it to No. 2, Simone]

337
00:14:39,860 --> 00:14:41,592
- Can I take this?
- Of course. Take it.

338
00:14:41,592 --> 00:14:43,361
[Butter]

339
00:14:43,361 --> 00:14:45,196
[Scooping butter with his face?]

340
00:14:45,196 --> 00:14:47,265
Take the butter. Go ahead.

341
00:14:47,265 --> 00:14:49,567
[Italian through and through!]
They love butter.

342
00:14:49,567 --> 00:14:52,226
[A generous helping of butter]

343
00:14:52,226 --> 00:14:54,839
[And then...]

344
00:14:54,839 --> 00:14:56,874
[A mountain of grated cheese]

345
00:14:56,874 --> 00:14:59,243
This has to be good.

346
00:15:00,111 --> 00:15:01,579
[One quick look]

347
00:15:01,579 --> 00:15:03,514
You're basically Italian.

348
00:15:05,460 --> 00:15:07,452
Since this is a staff meal,

349
00:15:07,452 --> 00:15:11,393
[An honorary Italian stirs the risotto]
I need to suit their tastes too.

350
00:15:11,393 --> 00:15:12,560
[Done squeezing!]
Finished.

351
00:15:12,560 --> 00:15:13,460
Thank you.

352
00:15:13,460 --> 00:15:15,594
Finished.

353
00:15:15,594 --> 00:15:17,462
[Simone squeezed out every last drop!]
Thank you.

354
00:15:17,462 --> 00:15:19,163
Thank you.

355
00:15:19,163 --> 00:15:20,198
That looks delicious.

356
00:15:20,198 --> 00:15:23,402
- It needs to be salty too.
- Right.

357
00:15:23,402 --> 00:15:26,070
[Another taste]

358
00:15:26,070 --> 00:15:27,372
I was really worried about it.

359
00:15:27,372 --> 00:15:29,173
Right.

360
00:15:29,173 --> 00:15:31,992
[Now a ladle?]

361
00:15:31,992 --> 00:15:34,526
[Butter refill]
A lot of butter, good.

362
00:15:34,526 --> 00:15:37,649
You're definitely one of us, a butter lover!

363
00:15:37,649 --> 00:15:40,784
[Seasoning like an honorary Italian]
You're definitely one of us, a butter lover!

364
00:15:41,453 --> 00:15:42,687
More?

365
00:15:42,687 --> 00:15:45,323
[Adding only a little at a time]

366
00:15:45,323 --> 00:15:50,728
[Tasting carefully, then adding more]

367
00:15:50,728 --> 00:15:52,563
- More cheese again?
- More cheese.

368
00:15:52,563 --> 00:15:54,198
[Cheese refill]

369
00:15:54,198 --> 00:15:56,768
I found myself adjusting the seasoning
much more carefully.

370
00:15:56,768 --> 00:15:59,503
[Finding the perfect butter-cheese balance]
- Exactly. - It makes me so nervous.

371
00:16:00,272 --> 00:16:03,793
They add as much of it
as we add garlic to kimchi.

372
00:16:03,793 --> 00:16:04,876
Good.

373
00:16:04,876 --> 00:16:06,377
[One more ladle of butter!]
More?

374
00:16:06,377 --> 00:16:08,479
He's really going through the butter.

375
00:16:08,479 --> 00:16:11,115
- Butter!
- Butter!

376
00:16:12,059 --> 00:16:13,317
That seems like too much.

377
00:16:13,317 --> 00:16:16,286
[The butter makes it even creamier]
At this point, aren't you adding rice to butter?

378
00:16:16,959 --> 00:16:18,656
I'm ready now, Chef.

379
00:16:18,656 --> 00:16:21,292
- Finished?
- Finished.

380
00:16:21,292 --> 00:16:23,193
Shall we try it?

381
00:16:23,795 --> 00:16:25,029
Okay, let's go!

382
00:16:25,029 --> 00:16:29,726
[Hee Tae's final mission dish is complete]

383
00:16:29,726 --> 00:16:33,438
[Five undercover days reach their climax!]

384
00:16:33,438 --> 00:16:34,806
You must've been nervous.

385
00:16:34,806 --> 00:16:38,777
So far, the whole process seems
to have gone exactly as intended.

386
00:16:38,777 --> 00:16:40,193
[Creamy Parma-style risotto]

387
00:16:40,193 --> 00:16:41,992
It's simple, but...

388
00:16:41,992 --> 00:16:44,916
- I wanted to make something a little delicate.
- Right.

389
00:16:44,916 --> 00:16:46,095
[Braised shiitake topping]
As long as the seasoning's right,

390
00:16:46,095 --> 00:16:48,118
this has to be a success.

391
00:16:48,953 --> 00:16:53,824
[Will it win over the people of Parma?]

392
00:16:54,492 --> 00:16:56,961
[The result of his all-out effort]

393
00:16:56,961 --> 00:16:58,696
It really looks like a dish
from this restaurant.

394
00:16:58,696 --> 00:17:00,226
- Really?
- Yes.

395
00:17:00,226 --> 00:17:03,860
It really aligns
with what this place stands for.

396
00:17:03,860 --> 00:17:06,126
[Hee Tae's new shiitake risotto]
I kept thinking about not straying too far.

397
00:17:06,126 --> 00:17:07,472
- Exactly.
- From its framework.

398
00:17:07,472 --> 00:17:09,373
That looks delicious.

399
00:17:09,959 --> 00:17:15,313
What worried me most
wasn't whether this dish was perfect.

400
00:17:15,313 --> 00:17:18,049
Would they see it as something
made by a foreigner,

401
00:17:18,049 --> 00:17:21,586
or as a risotto with my own style?

402
00:17:21,586 --> 00:17:23,621
It might stray far from tradition,

403
00:17:23,621 --> 00:17:25,890
but would it still have a clear identity?

404
00:17:25,890 --> 00:17:28,692
[On edge with every plate served]
That was what made me the most nervous.

405
00:17:30,426 --> 00:17:34,065
I know Parma-style risotto well.

406
00:17:34,065 --> 00:17:37,435
It uses onions, shallots,
and Parmigiano Reggiano.

407
00:17:37,435 --> 00:17:40,660
Then it's cooked with meat stock.

408
00:17:40,660 --> 00:17:42,708
But Hee Tae's risotto

409
00:17:42,708 --> 00:17:48,145
is a good idea that strikes a balance

410
00:17:48,145 --> 00:17:51,449
between Asian and Italian cuisine.

411
00:17:51,449 --> 00:17:54,685
[The head chef sees right through it]
He understood exactly what you were going for.

412
00:17:55,286 --> 00:17:57,955
Now it just has to taste good.

413
00:17:57,955 --> 00:18:00,892
If they taste it and just say,
"You tried hard," it's over!

414
00:18:00,892 --> 00:18:04,028
If all they say is,
"You tried hard," it's over.

415
00:18:04,028 --> 00:18:06,326
[What will the kitchen staff think?]
They need to say it's delicious.

416
00:18:06,326 --> 00:18:08,933
Let's see what's in here.

417
00:18:08,933 --> 00:18:09,834
Thank you, Hee Tae.

418
00:18:09,834 --> 00:18:11,168
[Could he even pitch it as a new dish?]
- Thank you. - Thank you.

419
00:18:11,168 --> 00:18:13,092
Thank you.

420
00:18:13,092 --> 00:18:14,772
I'm nervous.

421
00:18:14,772 --> 00:18:16,726
I'm so curious.

422
00:18:16,726 --> 00:18:18,244
Okay.

423
00:18:20,044 --> 00:18:21,426
Did Hee Tae make all of this?

424
00:18:21,426 --> 00:18:22,714
Yes.

425
00:18:23,992 --> 00:18:25,149
Boss!

426
00:18:25,149 --> 00:18:28,018
[They finally try the shiitake risotto]

427
00:18:28,686 --> 00:18:34,393
[Good reviews could lead to a menu pitch]

428
00:18:34,393 --> 00:18:37,159
Huh? Her eyes flickered for a second.

429
00:18:37,159 --> 00:18:39,329
Huh?

430
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:43,259
It's good.

431
00:18:43,259 --> 00:18:44,726
It's good.

432
00:18:44,726 --> 00:18:46,037
It's got to be good, right?

433
00:18:46,037 --> 00:18:49,426
[Nervous...]

434
00:18:49,426 --> 00:18:50,975
Our Gianpi...

435
00:18:50,975 --> 00:18:52,209
Chef Gianpi.

436
00:18:52,209 --> 00:18:54,612
[We trust you, Gianpi!]
How is it? How does it taste?

437
00:18:54,612 --> 00:18:56,446
Boss!

438
00:18:57,460 --> 00:19:00,518
Is it good enough to put on the menu?

439
00:19:00,518 --> 00:19:05,226
[A true master of ceremonies]

440
00:19:07,526 --> 00:19:09,159
It's delicious.

441
00:19:09,159 --> 00:19:10,560
- He says it's good.
- It's good.

442
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:12,296
- First, he says it's good.
- First, it's good.

443
00:19:12,296 --> 00:19:13,393
- First, it's good.
- Hee Tae.

444
00:19:13,393 --> 00:19:15,066
It's delicious.

445
00:19:15,066 --> 00:19:17,435
And Lucrezia even ate mushrooms!

446
00:19:17,435 --> 00:19:20,004
- Oh, really?
- Lu, do you ever eat mushrooms?

447
00:19:20,004 --> 00:19:21,539
Never!

448
00:19:21,539 --> 00:19:24,541
- She doesn't eat mushrooms?
- I didn't know.

449
00:19:25,326 --> 00:19:27,845
[Mushroom-hating Lu cleaned her plate]
She really cleaned her plate, though!

450
00:19:27,845 --> 00:19:31,426
I don't like mushrooms,
but I really enjoyed it!

451
00:19:31,426 --> 00:19:34,218
The flavors were very delicate,

452
00:19:34,218 --> 00:19:37,588
and the technique was excellent.

453
00:19:37,588 --> 00:19:40,257
It tasted great, with nice contrast.

454
00:19:40,257 --> 00:19:43,927
The mushrooms created that contrast,

455
00:19:43,927 --> 00:19:45,760
and the sweet and salty flavors worked well.

456
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:48,942
Italians would love it!

457
00:19:49,533 --> 00:19:52,703
They completely cleaned their plates.

458
00:19:53,337 --> 00:19:56,207
[Top-notch flavor]

459
00:19:56,207 --> 00:19:59,226
[Not a single grain of risotto left]

460
00:19:59,226 --> 00:20:02,259
[So far, so good]

461
00:20:02,259 --> 00:20:04,148
You have a great palate!

462
00:20:04,148 --> 00:20:05,684
[My palate?]
[This?]

463
00:20:05,684 --> 00:20:07,318
- "He has a great palate."
- "Great taste buds."

464
00:20:07,318 --> 00:20:09,959
- "Great taste buds."
- "He's got great taste buds."

465
00:20:09,959 --> 00:20:14,792
That made me think they might say yes.

466
00:20:15,459 --> 00:20:17,092
If that's the case...

467
00:20:17,092 --> 00:20:18,596
- This could actually work.
- Hold on.

468
00:20:18,596 --> 00:20:21,598
[Could it make the menu?]

469
00:20:22,293 --> 00:20:23,293
In Parma...

470
00:20:23,293 --> 00:20:27,204
[Making the menu is another matter]
This place has to put it on the menu.

471
00:20:27,204 --> 00:20:29,306
What's in it?

472
00:20:29,306 --> 00:20:31,408
Shiitake mushrooms.

473
00:20:33,660 --> 00:20:37,214
[Shiitake risotto is unusual in Italy]

474
00:20:37,915 --> 00:20:39,860
[Could it join the menu
at this authentic Parma restaurant?]

475
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:42,760
- That's good.
- Yes.

476
00:20:42,760 --> 00:20:44,655
Thank you.

477
00:20:44,655 --> 00:20:46,827
[Hee Tae finally speaks up]

478
00:20:46,827 --> 00:20:49,426
Do you think this would sell in Korea?

479
00:20:49,426 --> 00:20:53,030
Of course it would!

480
00:20:53,030 --> 00:20:57,092
- In Korea.
- Of course it would!

481
00:20:57,092 --> 00:20:58,736
It needs to sell in Parma!

482
00:20:58,736 --> 00:21:00,404
[The new-menu pitch begins]
Of course it'd work in Seoul.

483
00:21:00,404 --> 00:21:02,339
It'd definitely work in Korea.

484
00:21:02,339 --> 00:21:04,008
But it has to work here.

485
00:21:04,008 --> 00:21:06,226
- It has to.
- Boss.

486
00:21:06,226 --> 00:21:09,122
[If it's truly meant for this restaurant]

487
00:21:09,122 --> 00:21:15,018
[Will Hee Tae's risotto
join this Parma restaurant's menu?]

488
00:21:16,220 --> 00:21:17,860
[Gianpi!]

489
00:21:17,860 --> 00:21:20,791
Then how about...

490
00:21:22,226 --> 00:21:27,964
serving this risotto at your restaurant?

491
00:21:30,534 --> 00:21:33,604
[The introvert boldly pitches his dish!]

492
00:21:33,604 --> 00:21:34,626
[At our restaurant?]

493
00:21:34,626 --> 00:21:36,574
- Boss.
- Huh?

494
00:21:36,574 --> 00:21:39,043
- This dish?
- Let's see.

495
00:21:39,043 --> 00:21:41,511
[Heart pounding]
Here we go!

496
00:21:44,148 --> 00:21:48,018
[The head chef and boss confer at once]

497
00:21:48,018 --> 00:21:50,421
[Their most serious discussion yet]

498
00:21:50,421 --> 00:21:54,725
[Hee Tae waits, trying to stay calm...]

499
00:21:54,725 --> 00:21:58,395
What? What are they saying?
Where are the subtitles?

500
00:21:58,395 --> 00:22:01,232
What is it? Suddenly it's all Italian!

501
00:22:01,232 --> 00:22:03,968
[Why stop translating now?]
I don't speak Italian!

502
00:22:03,968 --> 00:22:05,669
[Even Hee Tae is lost in all that Italian]

503
00:22:05,669 --> 00:22:07,354
Come on...

504
00:22:07,354 --> 00:22:10,608
[I'm dying to know]

505
00:22:10,608 --> 00:22:13,344
[Just nodding for now...]

506
00:22:13,344 --> 00:22:16,913
[Praying again?]
This is so frustrating. What are they saying?

507
00:22:17,782 --> 00:22:21,593
[Let's replay that urgent meeting...]

508
00:22:21,593 --> 00:22:24,989
It's good, but something's missing.

509
00:22:24,989 --> 00:22:27,057
[Anxious] [Restless]
Something's missing?

510
00:22:27,057 --> 00:22:29,593
Yes, it leans a little sweet, but...

511
00:22:29,593 --> 00:22:31,393
that can be adjusted.

512
00:22:31,393 --> 00:22:33,798
I'm still not sure.

513
00:22:33,798 --> 00:22:38,936
[The chef sees hope, but the boss doesn't]

514
00:22:38,936 --> 00:22:42,606
If the mushroom flavor were stronger
and the amount were right,

515
00:22:42,606 --> 00:22:45,927
the aroma would come through more clearly...

516
00:22:45,927 --> 00:22:48,779
Was the mushroom aroma too weak?

517
00:22:48,779 --> 00:22:50,981
[Italian mushrooms have powerful aromas]
They use porcini here.

518
00:22:50,981 --> 00:22:54,827
- Porcini are intense.
- These are mild by comparison.

519
00:22:54,827 --> 00:22:56,053
Right.

520
00:22:56,053 --> 00:22:58,827
[Hee Tae still has no idea...]

521
00:22:58,827 --> 00:23:02,192
[Thank you?]

522
00:23:03,060 --> 00:23:06,197
[The verdict, in English]
This dish...

523
00:23:06,197 --> 00:23:08,766
The taste is...

524
00:23:08,766 --> 00:23:10,134
It doesn't taste Italian.

525
00:23:10,134 --> 00:23:11,769
This mushroom is sweet.

526
00:23:11,769 --> 00:23:13,626
- What?
- What?

527
00:23:13,626 --> 00:23:18,642
It blends Korean and Italian flavors.
It's a good idea!

528
00:23:18,642 --> 00:23:20,110
The idea's good, but...

529
00:23:20,110 --> 00:23:24,393
The sweet aroma of these mushrooms...

530
00:23:24,393 --> 00:23:28,585
isn't typically Italian.

531
00:23:32,724 --> 00:23:36,961
Hee Tae's risotto had a pleasant aroma,

532
00:23:36,961 --> 00:23:41,432
but it didn't fit our restaurant.

533
00:23:41,432 --> 00:23:43,567
[Firm]
It falls outside the restaurant's range.

534
00:23:43,567 --> 00:23:45,804
They have a style to maintain.

535
00:23:45,804 --> 00:23:49,074
[The boss says it lacks authenticity]
They care deeply about tradition.

536
00:23:49,074 --> 00:23:53,959
[All the chefs loved the shiitake risotto]
The owner's vision is very clear,

537
00:23:53,959 --> 00:23:57,248
and guests come here
for traditional Parma food...

538
00:23:57,248 --> 00:23:59,550
- Right.
- I don't think they'd come all this way

539
00:23:59,550 --> 00:24:02,326
- for something different.
- Right.

540
00:24:02,326 --> 00:24:04,560
[His new dish failed the authenticity test]
Right.

541
00:24:04,560 --> 00:24:07,123
That's why getting a dish on the menu is hard.

542
00:24:08,827 --> 00:24:11,830
So it isn't inherently sweet.

543
00:24:11,830 --> 00:24:16,099
It needs a stronger flavor
to bring it together.

544
00:24:16,860 --> 00:24:21,493
Without that, the whole thing tastes sweet.

545
00:24:21,493 --> 00:24:24,241
But that's only a balance issue.

546
00:24:24,241 --> 00:24:25,542
- The idea itself is good.
- It needs a little more...

547
00:24:25,542 --> 00:24:28,059
The seasoning needs more punch...

548
00:24:28,059 --> 00:24:29,974
[He keeps offering advice...]
And the flavor...

549
00:24:31,446 --> 00:24:35,686
[Parma Hee Tae]
[Final mission failed]

550
00:24:35,686 --> 00:24:38,923
[He expected it, but it still hurts]

551
00:24:38,923 --> 00:24:41,959
Is this your first time making it?

552
00:24:41,959 --> 00:24:43,893
Yes.

553
00:24:43,893 --> 00:24:45,095
Then you're fine.

554
00:24:45,095 --> 00:24:47,698
When we create a new dish,

555
00:24:47,698 --> 00:24:49,927
- we test it five, six, even ten times.
- You can't get it right in one try.

556
00:24:49,927 --> 00:24:51,268
Right.

557
00:24:51,268 --> 00:24:54,838
- Make it ten more times.
- "Make it ten more times."

558
00:24:54,838 --> 00:24:57,574
[Hee Tae knows that all too well]

559
00:24:57,574 --> 00:24:59,076
Hold on.

560
00:24:59,076 --> 00:25:00,644
[So disappointing...]

561
00:25:00,644 --> 00:25:03,247
- No!
- Wait, is that really it?

562
00:25:03,247 --> 00:25:05,015
No.

563
00:25:05,015 --> 00:25:06,985
It can't end like this.

564
00:25:06,985 --> 00:25:09,052
[Smiles faintly]
Thank you.

565
00:25:10,793 --> 00:25:12,756
I know that smile.

566
00:25:12,756 --> 00:25:14,426
- An introvert's smile?
- Sam Kim is an introvert.

567
00:25:14,426 --> 00:25:16,527
- Is that the introvert smile again?
- That's not a smile.

568
00:25:16,527 --> 00:25:19,326
- He's crying.
- Oh, he's crying.

569
00:25:19,326 --> 00:25:20,931
First, the rejection...

570
00:25:20,931 --> 00:25:24,026
I knew I could've done better,
so I was disappointed.

571
00:25:24,026 --> 00:25:29,439
I realized there was a wall I couldn't cross.

572
00:25:30,174 --> 00:25:34,593
[Parma Hee Tae fails the final mission]
The mission basically ended in failure.

573
00:25:34,593 --> 00:25:36,580
[Hits close to home]
Oh, this is...

574
00:25:36,580 --> 00:25:40,650
I could replicate
the great local food well enough,

575
00:25:40,650 --> 00:25:46,615
but my urge to show my Asian identity
was too strong back then.

576
00:25:46,615 --> 00:25:48,692
- I wanted it to reflect my identity.
- Deliberately?

577
00:25:48,692 --> 00:25:50,627
- It was intentional.
- So you did that on purpose.

578
00:25:50,627 --> 00:25:53,026
- Okay.
- The mission failed,

579
00:25:53,026 --> 00:25:54,999
and one thing remains.

580
00:25:54,999 --> 00:25:58,168
- There's something more important left.
- The identity reveal is still ahead.

581
00:25:58,168 --> 00:25:59,371
How will he do it?

582
00:25:59,371 --> 00:26:02,206
How will this introvert reveal himself?

583
00:26:02,206 --> 00:26:03,640
Write a letter and run away.

584
00:26:03,640 --> 00:26:05,909
"Write a letter and run away."

585
00:26:07,927 --> 00:26:08,946
[Glances over]

586
00:26:08,946 --> 00:26:10,781
[Fidgets with his hat]
Is he thinking it over right here?

587
00:26:10,781 --> 00:26:12,783
- How to reveal himself.
- He keeps watching them.

588
00:26:12,783 --> 00:26:15,852
[Hee Tae watches everyone]
[Glances one more]

589
00:26:18,822 --> 00:26:20,490
[Glances over]

590
00:26:21,760 --> 00:26:24,161
[Nervous]
Nice.

591
00:26:24,161 --> 00:26:26,263
When I revealed who I was,

592
00:26:26,263 --> 00:26:30,067
I was dying to know what they'd think.

593
00:26:30,067 --> 00:26:32,736
Would they feel hurt?

594
00:26:32,736 --> 00:26:37,741
Or would they say, "How could a chef
be this bad the whole time?"

595
00:26:38,342 --> 00:26:41,678
[Especially after failing the final mission]
That too, since the last dish...

596
00:26:41,678 --> 00:26:44,014
[Nods]
I mean...

597
00:26:44,014 --> 00:26:49,219
So I kept thinking about how to reveal myself,

598
00:26:49,219 --> 00:26:51,560
and then it suddenly hit me.

599
00:26:51,560 --> 00:26:54,157
Huh? You had a plan?

600
00:26:55,359 --> 00:26:58,662
[Giancarlo's star-studded connections]

601
00:26:58,662 --> 00:27:00,532
Giancarlo's thing is...

602
00:27:00,532 --> 00:27:02,092
He loves to brag.

603
00:27:02,092 --> 00:27:04,334
He does.

604
00:27:04,334 --> 00:27:08,064
[He was hearing about culinary legends]

605
00:27:08,064 --> 00:27:10,040
Huh? A question mark?

606
00:27:10,040 --> 00:27:11,475
- Has this person been here too?
- Yes, he has!

607
00:27:11,475 --> 00:27:13,626
Who? Who is it?

608
00:27:13,626 --> 00:27:17,460
[One person catches Hee Tae's eye]

609
00:27:17,460 --> 00:27:19,983
Who is it? Oh! Cracco!

610
00:27:20,827 --> 00:27:21,852
Nice.

611
00:27:21,852 --> 00:27:23,187
Very nice.

612
00:27:23,187 --> 00:27:25,193
[Sung Jun and Hee Tae know Cracco?]

613
00:27:25,193 --> 00:27:27,524
[Who is Cracco?]
Chef Carlo Cracco.

614
00:27:27,524 --> 00:27:30,294
He's huge in Italy!

615
00:27:30,294 --> 00:27:33,997
[Italian Michelin-star chef Carlo Cracco]
Even the general public knows him.

616
00:27:33,997 --> 00:27:36,667
- He was a MasterChef judge too.
- Really?

617
00:27:36,667 --> 00:27:39,026
[Italy's celebrity chef]
He's one of the legends.

618
00:27:39,026 --> 00:27:41,839
[Hee Tae's close friend!]
I thought maybe I could ask my friend

619
00:27:41,839 --> 00:27:44,543
- to call the restaurant.
- Seriously?

620
00:27:44,543 --> 00:27:47,911
- Are you close?
- Seriously? You're close?

621
00:27:47,911 --> 00:27:49,293
It's like Stray Kids and me.

622
00:27:49,293 --> 00:27:51,348
[Not buying it] [Framed!]
How much would he lend you?

623
00:27:51,348 --> 00:27:53,083
Close friends lend each other money.

624
00:27:53,083 --> 00:27:55,219
- You'll see.
- It's obviously like Stray Kids and me.

625
00:27:55,219 --> 00:27:59,656
I thought, "Maybe I could ask him
to call the restaurant."

626
00:28:00,791 --> 00:28:01,992
- Seriously?
- This is huge.

627
00:28:01,992 --> 00:28:04,628
[A friend's help may reveal his identity]
This is amazing!

628
00:28:04,628 --> 00:28:08,126
[Hee Tae! How can I help?]
- Incredible! - I never saw that coming.

629
00:28:08,126 --> 00:28:08,899
This is incredible!

630
00:28:08,899 --> 00:28:11,659
[An introvert's bold reveal plan]
This is incredible. He's really doing this...

631
00:28:11,659 --> 00:28:16,573
[1. Sneak out without the kitchen crew]
- This is incredible. - This is incredible.

632
00:28:16,573 --> 00:28:19,076
[2. Try to reach his friend Cracco]

633
00:28:19,076 --> 00:28:21,278
He's really texting him.

634
00:28:21,278 --> 00:28:22,479
Seriously?

635
00:28:22,479 --> 00:28:25,315
Hello. It's Sam. It's nice to talk again.

636
00:28:25,315 --> 00:28:27,084
Hello. Likewise.

637
00:28:27,084 --> 00:28:29,286
[Contact made immediately]

638
00:28:29,286 --> 00:28:30,687
If he picks up right away...

639
00:28:30,687 --> 00:28:32,442
They must be really close.

640
00:28:32,442 --> 00:28:33,726
[With translation help]
This is going to be so much fun!

641
00:28:33,726 --> 00:28:35,659
[Dopamine rush]
How will he react?

642
00:28:35,659 --> 00:28:37,092
Giancarlo's going to be shocked.

643
00:28:37,092 --> 00:28:38,328
He's going to be shocked.

644
00:28:38,328 --> 00:28:41,665
[We need someone to confirm Hee Tae's identity]

645
00:28:41,665 --> 00:28:44,201
[3. Cracco tells Giancarlo who Hee Tae is!]

646
00:28:44,201 --> 00:28:46,837
This is huge!

647
00:28:46,837 --> 00:28:48,526
- This is amazing.
- I never saw that coming.

648
00:28:48,526 --> 00:28:50,908
[This is going to be epic]
This is just...

649
00:28:50,908 --> 00:28:53,343
This is incredible. He's really doing this?

650
00:28:53,343 --> 00:28:55,026
Doesn't this sound fun? Seriously.

651
00:28:55,026 --> 00:28:56,393
I was shocked.

652
00:28:56,393 --> 00:28:59,215
He's having someone else do it
because he can't.

653
00:29:00,052 --> 00:29:01,618
Because he can't do it himself.

654
00:29:01,618 --> 00:29:04,188
- Introverts can't do this themselves.
- Sung Jun nailed it, as always!

655
00:29:04,188 --> 00:29:05,293
[Brutal truth]
You're right.

656
00:29:05,293 --> 00:29:07,324
You got it exactly right.

657
00:29:07,324 --> 00:29:08,959
[A refreshingly accurate analysis]
Like this...

658
00:29:08,959 --> 00:29:11,697
- Like this...
- Introvert decoded.

659
00:29:11,697 --> 00:29:13,830
Everyone's reactions are so good.

660
00:29:13,830 --> 00:29:16,193
Giancarlo and the chefs, all of them.

661
00:29:16,193 --> 00:29:19,403
Giancarlo always shows off. Guaranteed.

662
00:29:19,403 --> 00:29:20,837
"Hee Tae, you know this chef?

663
00:29:20,837 --> 00:29:23,273
This famous chef is on the phone with me."

664
00:29:23,273 --> 00:29:24,975
You know, that kind of thing.

665
00:29:24,975 --> 00:29:26,677
[Like this?]

666
00:29:26,677 --> 00:29:27,827
Like, "You know him?"

667
00:29:27,827 --> 00:29:30,814
Of course.
Everyone here knows who Chef Cracco is.

668
00:29:30,814 --> 00:29:32,615
Yeah, they all do.

669
00:29:33,217 --> 00:29:37,059
[Will this introvert's careful plan work?]

670
00:29:37,059 --> 00:29:41,057
[Just imagining it makes him laugh]

671
00:29:43,226 --> 00:29:44,695
[Is it time to put the plan into action?]

672
00:29:44,695 --> 00:29:47,660
- Seriously?
- This is my first time seeing this scene.

673
00:29:47,660 --> 00:29:50,159
<i>Hello, Giancarlo.</i>

674
00:29:50,159 --> 00:29:51,426
- Seriously?
- Seriously?

675
00:29:51,426 --> 00:29:53,026
[It's actually Carlo Cracco on the phone!]
Oh, this is huge!

676
00:29:53,026 --> 00:29:55,474
<i>Are you getting ready for dinner service?</i>

677
00:29:57,893 --> 00:30:00,443
- This is huge!
- Seriously?

678
00:30:05,916 --> 00:30:08,785
- I've been ready since the day I was born.
- He's bragging.

679
00:30:08,785 --> 00:30:10,827
He's bragging that Cracco called him.

680
00:30:10,827 --> 00:30:14,393
[He turns on speakerphone]

681
00:30:14,393 --> 00:30:16,026
So he wants everyone to hear?

682
00:30:16,026 --> 00:30:17,328
He wants everyone to hear it.

683
00:30:17,328 --> 00:30:19,529
"See? Cracco and I are this close."

684
00:30:19,529 --> 00:30:22,092
[This owner is quite a character]

685
00:30:22,092 --> 00:30:24,635
Carlo! Carlo!

686
00:30:24,635 --> 00:30:25,669
Carlo!

687
00:30:25,669 --> 00:30:28,071
Cracco, how are you doing?

688
00:30:28,071 --> 00:30:31,460
[He deliberately walks
farther into the kitchen]

689
00:30:31,460 --> 00:30:33,159
[The showing-off never stops]

690
00:30:33,159 --> 00:30:36,860
[Everyone, Carlo Cracco is calling me!]

691
00:30:36,860 --> 00:30:38,448
It's like flashing a royal inspector's badge.

692
00:30:38,448 --> 00:30:40,159
He's a secret royal inspector.

693
00:30:40,159 --> 00:30:41,618
"You know him, right? You know Carlo?"

694
00:30:41,618 --> 00:30:44,159
[It's practically a royal badge]
That's fascinating.

695
00:30:44,159 --> 00:30:46,089
- "He's my friend."
- Carlo.

696
00:30:46,089 --> 00:30:49,359
- He's a secret royal inspector.
- "You know him, right? You know Carlo?"

697
00:30:49,359 --> 00:30:51,726
That's fascinating.

698
00:30:51,726 --> 00:30:54,564
[At the name Carlo] [Eyes lighting up]
"He's my friend."

699
00:30:55,460 --> 00:30:56,566
Carlo.

700
00:30:56,566 --> 00:30:59,202
[Simone is simply amazed]

701
00:30:59,202 --> 00:31:02,359
[And the mastermind Hee Tae...]

702
00:31:02,359 --> 00:31:04,092
[Oh, it's Cracco]

703
00:31:04,092 --> 00:31:06,042
This is incredible.

704
00:31:06,910 --> 00:31:09,413
Oh, right! We have a guest.

705
00:31:09,413 --> 00:31:10,747
Do you know him?

706
00:31:10,747 --> 00:31:12,516
[As expected, he shows off to Hee Tae too]

707
00:31:12,516 --> 00:31:15,092
"Hey, you know Carlo, right?"

708
00:31:15,092 --> 00:31:16,760
He wants to show him and brag.

709
00:31:16,760 --> 00:31:17,827
[Called it]
He read him perfectly.

710
00:31:17,827 --> 00:31:19,660
Oh, man! He read him perfectly.

711
00:31:19,660 --> 00:31:21,159
Oh, man! Sam Kim, you're scary.

712
00:31:21,159 --> 00:31:26,393
He reads people like a book!

713
00:31:26,393 --> 00:31:27,898
Do you know him?

714
00:31:27,898 --> 00:31:31,401
[He knew it]
Oh, perfect.

715
00:31:31,401 --> 00:31:33,003
He had him figured out.

716
00:31:33,003 --> 00:31:35,205
[Strategist Hee Tae read him perfectly]

717
00:31:35,205 --> 00:31:37,574
He's our new hire.

718
00:31:37,574 --> 00:31:40,593
How have you been, Cracco?

719
00:31:40,593 --> 00:31:44,493
[So when will he mention me?]

720
00:31:44,493 --> 00:31:46,860
<i>But what should I call him?</i>

721
00:31:46,860 --> 00:31:47,884
<i>Kim.</i>

722
00:31:47,884 --> 00:31:49,753
[Kim?]

723
00:31:49,753 --> 00:31:52,556
[Finally!]

724
00:31:52,556 --> 00:31:54,491
- Did we change his name...
- Because he's Sam.

725
00:31:54,491 --> 00:31:57,060
We've always called him by his name...

726
00:31:58,028 --> 00:32:01,359
[Kim?]

727
00:32:01,359 --> 00:32:05,168
We've never called him anything but Hee Tae.

728
00:32:05,168 --> 00:32:07,938
No. We've never called him anything else.

729
00:32:07,938 --> 00:32:12,309
[Still talking about Hee Tae]
[Flashes a silent, toothy grin]

730
00:32:12,309 --> 00:32:14,578
[Hahaha!]

731
00:32:14,578 --> 00:32:17,114
[Confused]
But that man...

732
00:32:17,114 --> 00:32:19,549
I want to see how this plays out.

733
00:32:19,549 --> 00:32:22,219
[The owner suddenly steps out to call]

734
00:32:22,219 --> 00:32:23,660
- I want to hear this.
- No, stay inside!

735
00:32:23,660 --> 00:32:25,255
Keep it in there!

736
00:32:25,255 --> 00:32:26,959
[Where did he go?]

737
00:32:26,959 --> 00:32:27,991
What? Where's he going?

738
00:32:27,991 --> 00:32:29,593
Hee Tae, do you know him?

739
00:32:29,593 --> 00:32:32,062
Do you know Carlo Cracco?

740
00:32:32,062 --> 00:32:33,864
- Yes, of course.
- You know him?

741
00:32:33,864 --> 00:32:35,132
Yeah.

742
00:32:35,132 --> 00:32:39,302
Cracco is Italy's most famous chef.

743
00:32:39,302 --> 00:32:43,206
He's telling me, "He's huge in Italy."

744
00:32:43,206 --> 00:32:44,793
He's explaining it to me.

745
00:32:44,793 --> 00:32:47,144
[Of course I know. He's my friend]
He's really...

746
00:32:47,144 --> 00:32:49,112
[He must be famous]
Okay.

747
00:32:49,112 --> 00:32:50,580
He needs to reveal himself.

748
00:32:50,580 --> 00:32:52,249
This introvert, seriously...

749
00:32:52,249 --> 00:32:54,684
[What are you doing, introvert?]
Say something!

750
00:32:54,684 --> 00:32:56,726
What is this?

751
00:32:56,726 --> 00:32:58,955
[How is this reveal supposed to work?]
I need to know.

752
00:32:58,955 --> 00:33:01,658
[After the owner stepped out...]

753
00:33:01,658 --> 00:33:05,262
[The kitchen goes quiet again]

754
00:33:05,262 --> 00:33:08,564
He got the call, then acted totally normal.

755
00:33:09,460 --> 00:33:11,401
I wondered if he hadn't understood.

756
00:33:11,401 --> 00:33:15,521
Then he came back with his face bright red.

757
00:33:15,521 --> 00:33:17,760
[After a long call with Cracco]
What? What is it?

758
00:33:17,760 --> 00:33:19,875
What's going on?

759
00:33:19,875 --> 00:33:22,846
[Rushing back into the kitchen?]
What's going on?

760
00:33:22,846 --> 00:33:26,293
This feels like a hidden-camera prank.

761
00:33:26,293 --> 00:33:27,626
A hidden-camera prank.

762
00:33:27,626 --> 00:33:29,193
- He thinks it's a prank.
- He thinks it's a prank.

763
00:33:29,193 --> 00:33:30,289
I mean...

764
00:33:30,289 --> 00:33:32,589
Cracco said...

765
00:33:32,589 --> 00:33:36,146
What? That "Kim?"

766
00:33:36,146 --> 00:33:38,326
Could you please confirm?
The man standing here...

767
00:33:38,326 --> 00:33:41,092
is Korea's leading authority
on Italian cuisine?

768
00:33:41,092 --> 00:33:42,466
<i>Yes.</i>

769
00:33:42,466 --> 00:33:46,503
Hee Tae is apparently the standard
for Italian cuisine in Korea.

770
00:33:46,503 --> 00:33:51,508
He's highly skilled,
he has great instincts, and he's talented.

771
00:33:51,508 --> 00:33:53,059
He did seem that way...

772
00:33:53,059 --> 00:33:56,193
[Still confused]
He did seem that way...

773
00:33:56,193 --> 00:33:57,916
Look at their faces.

774
00:33:57,916 --> 00:34:00,616
[What is happening?]
Look at them. Look at their faces.

775
00:34:06,289 --> 00:34:07,793
[So much to say... but I won't]

776
00:34:07,793 --> 00:34:10,159
This is fun.

777
00:34:10,159 --> 00:34:15,365
Cracco mentioned "Kim" on the phone tonight,

778
00:34:15,365 --> 00:34:19,269
but there's no "Kim" here, only Hee Tae.

779
00:34:19,269 --> 00:34:22,372
Right. He only knows him as Hee Tae.

780
00:34:22,372 --> 00:34:24,708
But he kept asking, "How's Kim?"

781
00:34:24,708 --> 00:34:27,493
Kim? Kie?

782
00:34:27,493 --> 00:34:29,626
[Who's that?]

783
00:34:29,626 --> 00:34:30,860
Once I collected myself, I asked him.

784
00:34:30,860 --> 00:34:34,593
"How do you know Kim?"

785
00:34:34,593 --> 00:34:36,953
[Cracco's answer follows]
Then he told me,

786
00:34:36,953 --> 00:34:42,358
"He's the face of Italian cuisine in Korea."

787
00:34:45,626 --> 00:34:47,330
Kim is my real last name.

788
00:34:47,330 --> 00:34:48,632
No.

789
00:34:48,632 --> 00:34:51,935
Come to think of it, there were clues.

790
00:34:51,935 --> 00:34:53,870
He spoke some Italian, grew olives...

791
00:34:53,870 --> 00:34:55,860
None of it added up.

792
00:34:55,860 --> 00:34:57,966
Right. It made no sense.

793
00:34:57,966 --> 00:35:00,577
[The truth about the LA farmer]
Nothing he's saying adds up.

794
00:35:00,577 --> 00:35:03,680
Exactly. It was all so vague. We got you.

795
00:35:03,680 --> 00:35:06,259
You had us completely fooled.

796
00:35:06,259 --> 00:35:08,784
Now he's denying it.

797
00:35:09,899 --> 00:35:12,822
[Utterly stunned]

798
00:35:12,822 --> 00:35:16,259
[Hahaha]

799
00:35:16,259 --> 00:35:19,760
[The man I taught was a chef...]

800
00:35:19,760 --> 00:35:21,565
That shocked her.

801
00:35:21,565 --> 00:35:24,526
[A whirlwind of emotions]

802
00:35:24,526 --> 00:35:27,860
[They show them who Hee Tae really is]

803
00:35:27,860 --> 00:35:30,340
Hee Tae, come here.

804
00:35:30,340 --> 00:35:33,393
Come here already!

805
00:35:33,393 --> 00:35:35,193
You're already one of Korea's best!

806
00:35:35,193 --> 00:35:38,317
Look at that mantecare!

807
00:35:38,317 --> 00:35:41,550
[Hee Tae's restaurant sign]
Trattoria Sam Kim?

808
00:35:44,126 --> 00:35:46,756
This can't be real!

809
00:35:51,227 --> 00:35:54,164
[Sam Kim and Gordon Ramsay]

810
00:35:54,164 --> 00:35:55,365
He's my friend.

811
00:35:55,365 --> 00:35:56,760
No.

812
00:35:56,760 --> 00:35:59,660
[Thank you, Cracco]

813
00:35:59,660 --> 00:36:01,460
Thank you.

814
00:36:01,460 --> 00:36:04,274
[Hee Tae's identity, fully revealed]

815
00:36:04,274 --> 00:36:06,726
[Smack on the back]

816
00:36:06,726 --> 00:36:09,112
He fooled us.

817
00:36:09,112 --> 00:36:11,348
[He can't stop laughing]

818
00:36:11,348 --> 00:36:13,984
I never thought he was a chef.

819
00:36:13,984 --> 00:36:16,987
But then he made that fish pasta.

820
00:36:16,987 --> 00:36:19,589
He was so fast and skilled.

821
00:36:19,589 --> 00:36:21,927
- How are they supposed to look at him now?
- It felt awkward.

822
00:36:21,927 --> 00:36:24,260
- Of course it did.
- It had to.

823
00:36:25,395 --> 00:36:28,531
[Awkward]
I mean...

824
00:36:28,531 --> 00:36:30,300
What were we supposed to teach you?

825
00:36:30,300 --> 00:36:33,193
You should've been teaching us.

826
00:36:33,193 --> 00:36:34,471
"You should've been teaching us."

827
00:36:34,471 --> 00:36:37,259
[Tap]

828
00:36:37,259 --> 00:36:39,842
<i>We'll get our revenge tonight.</i>

829
00:36:40,793 --> 00:36:42,359
Please.

830
00:36:42,359 --> 00:36:43,660
[Simone suddenly issues a warning]
"We'll get our revenge tonight."

831
00:36:43,660 --> 00:36:46,159
Tonight, they're getting revenge on him.

832
00:36:46,159 --> 00:36:48,793
<i>We'll get our revenge tonight.</i>

833
00:36:48,793 --> 00:36:51,620
[Watch out, Kim Hee Tae]
No, please, no.

834
00:36:52,489 --> 00:36:53,790
I love you all.

835
00:36:53,790 --> 00:36:55,858
Oh, sure.

836
00:36:57,359 --> 00:36:58,928
Now he says he loves them.

837
00:36:58,928 --> 00:37:00,796
[Love won't save you now]

838
00:37:01,827 --> 00:37:03,766
[Nervous sweat]

839
00:37:04,968 --> 00:37:06,770
He wasn't a farmer trying to become a chef.

840
00:37:06,770 --> 00:37:10,726
He was Korea's most famous Italian chef.

841
00:37:10,726 --> 00:37:13,493
[Word spreads to the dining-room staff]

842
00:37:13,493 --> 00:37:14,560
[Day 5 dinner service begins, 8:00 PM]
And now he has to work.

843
00:37:14,560 --> 00:37:16,579
That must've felt so awkward.

844
00:37:16,579 --> 00:37:18,959
[Back at work as Sam Kim]

845
00:37:18,959 --> 00:37:20,717
Everyone, listen.

846
00:37:20,717 --> 00:37:25,422
We only just found out...

847
00:37:25,422 --> 00:37:29,359
that man in the kitchen came here to learn.

848
00:37:29,359 --> 00:37:30,860
He's explaining it to them.

849
00:37:30,860 --> 00:37:32,793
But he's actually

850
00:37:32,793 --> 00:37:34,731
- a celebrity Italian chef in Korea.
- He's bragging about him now.

851
00:37:34,731 --> 00:37:36,132
He's bragging now.

852
00:37:36,132 --> 00:37:38,835
[So proud]
He's really showing off now.

853
00:37:38,835 --> 00:37:40,003
[Where?]

854
00:37:40,003 --> 00:37:42,171
[Who?]

855
00:37:43,306 --> 00:37:47,243
[Sam Kim's story spreads like wildfire]

856
00:37:47,243 --> 00:37:49,345
It turns out...

857
00:37:49,345 --> 00:37:53,416
he was one of Korea's top Italian chefs.

858
00:37:53,416 --> 00:37:55,819
The man who was prepping our tortelli!

859
00:37:55,819 --> 00:38:00,156
That's only half of what happened.
Can you believe it?

860
00:38:00,156 --> 00:38:06,159
[Thanks to the proud owner, everyone knows]

861
00:38:06,159 --> 00:38:11,893
I bet that owner will tell
this story for at least a year.

862
00:38:11,893 --> 00:38:14,460
A year? I'd say ten.

863
00:38:14,460 --> 00:38:18,174
[Giancarlo's ten-year bragging story]
For ten years, he'll tell everyone he meets.

864
00:38:18,174 --> 00:38:20,242
[We had a celebrity chef in our kitchen!]

865
00:38:20,944 --> 00:38:24,426
I'm still looking for Bimby.

866
00:38:24,426 --> 00:38:28,518
That expensive machine?

867
00:38:28,518 --> 00:38:30,519
The one you said you'd buy your mom?

868
00:38:31,321 --> 00:38:35,059
[Oops...]

869
00:38:35,059 --> 00:38:38,026
"It's Bimby for my mom."

870
00:38:38,026 --> 00:38:39,893
[Oh, my!]

871
00:38:39,893 --> 00:38:44,366
What a sweet son.

872
00:38:46,626 --> 00:38:48,359
You have social media, right?

873
00:38:48,359 --> 00:38:50,540
Yes.

874
00:38:50,540 --> 00:38:52,293
Of course he does.

875
00:38:52,293 --> 00:38:54,577
- Sahm Kim!
- This is going to surprise them.

876
00:38:54,577 --> 00:38:56,479
Chef Sam Kim.

877
00:38:57,126 --> 00:39:01,083
[The farmer who claimed he had no Instagram]

878
00:39:01,751 --> 00:39:04,353
[315,000 followers]
315,000!

879
00:39:05,188 --> 00:39:07,157
[He was this famous?]
315,000!

880
00:39:07,157 --> 00:39:08,558
[All she can do is smile]

881
00:39:08,558 --> 00:39:10,960
[The real Hee Tae keeps surprising them]

882
00:39:10,960 --> 00:39:12,829
Sam Kim.

883
00:39:12,829 --> 00:39:14,531
Imagine telling Sorem about this.

884
00:39:14,531 --> 00:39:16,900
- Oh, Sorem.
- I wonder how Sorem will react.

885
00:39:16,900 --> 00:39:19,068
Sorem's the only one who doesn't know.

886
00:39:19,068 --> 00:39:20,092
[Sorem has no clue]

887
00:39:20,092 --> 00:39:21,905
Sorem will probably go...

888
00:39:21,905 --> 00:39:24,174
Sorem will probably go...

889
00:39:24,174 --> 00:39:26,242
"Oh, really?"

890
00:39:30,092 --> 00:39:32,126
- "Oh, really?"
- Oh, man.

891
00:39:32,126 --> 00:39:33,385
These people...

892
00:39:33,385 --> 00:39:35,193
How did they get this funny on the last day?

893
00:39:35,193 --> 00:39:38,293
- They saved it all for the end.
- Were they actually this funny all along?

894
00:39:38,293 --> 00:39:39,660
The finale's the funniest episode.

895
00:39:39,660 --> 00:39:41,457
The finale's the funniest.

896
00:39:41,457 --> 00:39:42,827
[Secretly funny introverts?]

897
00:39:42,827 --> 00:39:45,359
We're on vacation in February,
so we'll close for three weeks.

898
00:39:45,359 --> 00:39:49,860
I'll go to Korea for a week.

899
00:39:49,860 --> 00:39:51,367
Come to Korea.

900
00:39:51,367 --> 00:39:52,869
- Come visit.
- Yes, come visit.

901
00:39:52,869 --> 00:39:55,159
- Let's do a survival show.
- Why a survival show?

902
00:39:55,159 --> 00:39:57,259
- Let's face off.
- A survival show?

903
00:39:57,259 --> 00:39:58,326
Sounds good.

904
00:39:58,326 --> 00:40:02,177
[A Korea trip is suddenly in the works]

905
00:40:02,177 --> 00:40:03,112
[Then...]

906
00:40:03,112 --> 00:40:05,348
Club?

907
00:40:05,348 --> 00:40:08,425
[A shocking staff dinner, part two?]
A club in Korea?

908
00:40:08,425 --> 00:40:11,086
- You've never been either.
- No.

909
00:40:12,422 --> 00:40:15,491
[Looking forward to meeting again in Korea]

910
00:40:15,491 --> 00:40:16,593
[Sam Kim runs dinner service in Parma]

911
00:40:16,593 --> 00:40:19,128
He's back to work.

912
00:40:19,128 --> 00:40:21,731
[Sam Kim mode activated]

913
00:40:21,731 --> 00:40:25,426
[Finally showing them what he can do]
- Oh, man. - Of course.

914
00:40:25,426 --> 00:40:27,337
[Ooh...]

915
00:40:27,337 --> 00:40:30,573
[Now his skills make sense]

916
00:40:30,573 --> 00:40:31,908
Now they can relax.

917
00:40:31,908 --> 00:40:33,776
They'd just assume he'll do well.

918
00:40:33,776 --> 00:40:36,050
[Completely relaxed]

919
00:40:36,050 --> 00:40:37,146
Yes, Chef.

920
00:40:37,146 --> 00:40:38,893
Yes, Chef.

921
00:40:38,893 --> 00:40:40,860
Now they're calling you Chef?

922
00:40:40,860 --> 00:40:42,059
Chef.

923
00:40:42,059 --> 00:40:44,593
Now they're calling him Chef.

924
00:40:44,593 --> 00:40:45,755
Chef Sam.

925
00:40:45,755 --> 00:40:47,489
Chef Sam.

926
00:40:48,359 --> 00:40:49,525
Yes, Chef.

927
00:40:49,525 --> 00:40:52,893
[We have Chef Sam Kim in our kitchen]

928
00:40:52,893 --> 00:40:54,326
- That's hilarious.
- I'll do it, Chef.

929
00:40:54,326 --> 00:40:55,593
They're so much fun.

930
00:40:55,593 --> 00:40:57,100
- They really are.
- I love this.

931
00:40:57,100 --> 00:41:00,970
[As dinner service stays lighthearted]

932
00:41:02,326 --> 00:41:03,393
Who are you?

933
00:41:03,393 --> 00:41:05,092
[Late to the news, Sorem arrives]

934
00:41:05,092 --> 00:41:07,379
He's here!

935
00:41:07,379 --> 00:41:08,693
[So good to see him]
Sorem's here!

936
00:41:08,693 --> 00:41:10,512
Now...

937
00:41:11,126 --> 00:41:13,444
Who are you?

938
00:41:13,444 --> 00:41:14,484
I'm Hee Tae.

939
00:41:14,484 --> 00:41:15,927
- Hee Tae?
- Hee Tae.

940
00:41:15,927 --> 00:41:17,420
- But?
- Yes.

941
00:41:17,420 --> 00:41:20,256
What do you do?

942
00:41:20,256 --> 00:41:22,593
I'm a chef.

943
00:41:22,593 --> 00:41:25,426
I knew it.

944
00:41:25,426 --> 00:41:28,030
You're a good actor, too.

945
00:41:29,827 --> 00:41:34,303
[Sorem learns Sam Kim's identity]

946
00:41:34,959 --> 00:41:38,074
[Stares...]

947
00:41:38,074 --> 00:41:41,910
I was so happy to be here.

948
00:41:43,259 --> 00:41:44,660
[Nods]

949
00:41:44,660 --> 00:41:46,155
Yes.

950
00:41:47,116 --> 00:41:49,460
Liar?

951
00:41:49,460 --> 00:41:51,987
I'll miss you.

952
00:41:52,956 --> 00:41:55,090
I'll miss you.

953
00:41:58,893 --> 00:42:00,897
I really don't know...

954
00:42:00,897 --> 00:42:02,326
I don't know where the time went.

955
00:42:02,326 --> 00:42:04,233
After the first day, I thought,

956
00:42:04,233 --> 00:42:05,326
"What am I going to do?"

957
00:42:05,326 --> 00:42:07,804
Now that it's over, I feel sad to leave.

958
00:42:07,804 --> 00:42:11,574
[A bittersweet final day]

959
00:42:11,574 --> 00:42:12,575
Hee Tae.

960
00:42:12,575 --> 00:42:14,959
[The champagne wouldn't pop]

961
00:42:14,959 --> 00:42:16,159
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

962
00:42:16,159 --> 00:42:18,715
I've gotten really attached to them.

963
00:42:18,715 --> 00:42:20,927
[Toasting with his Parma family]

964
00:42:20,927 --> 00:42:24,320
That's why I really want
to invite them to Korea.

965
00:42:24,320 --> 00:42:27,636
Then I just want us all to have fun.

966
00:42:31,928 --> 00:42:34,430
[Sunny in Chengdu, not Jung Ji Sun]
[The unstoppable Jung Sunny]

967
00:42:34,430 --> 00:42:36,893
On the long-awaited final day...

968
00:42:36,893 --> 00:42:39,635
only half a day remains.

969
00:42:40,837 --> 00:42:44,140
[Sunny's XO garlic dish]
- That looks good. - That looks good.

970
00:42:44,140 --> 00:42:46,075
[Chengdu heat meets XO umami, but...]
This is a dish they'd love.

971
00:42:46,075 --> 00:42:47,377
Oh, this one...

972
00:42:47,377 --> 00:42:49,178
- It's sweet.
- Sweet?

973
00:42:49,178 --> 00:42:50,526
Is it sweet?

974
00:42:50,526 --> 00:42:52,515
[Sunny's XO garlic dish fails the mission]
I thought this one was a sure thing.

975
00:42:52,515 --> 00:42:53,583
That's too bad.

976
00:42:53,583 --> 00:42:57,119
[Will she give up now?]

977
00:42:58,221 --> 00:43:00,556
[Sunny roams the kitchen]

978
00:43:00,556 --> 00:43:01,593
Master Tang.

979
00:43:01,593 --> 00:43:06,462
Could I go buy some ingredients and cook here?

980
00:43:06,462 --> 00:43:10,933
[She retries the final mission]

981
00:43:10,933 --> 00:43:14,103
[Sunny's final mission isn't over yet]
That's impressive.

982
00:43:15,526 --> 00:43:17,426
[Every second counts after the retry]
What should I get?

983
00:43:17,426 --> 00:43:19,108
[Sigh]

984
00:43:19,927 --> 00:43:22,979
[Impressive]
She never stops working.

985
00:43:22,979 --> 00:43:25,914
Come to think of it, I haven't seen taro here.

986
00:43:26,849 --> 00:43:27,617
Taro?

987
00:43:27,617 --> 00:43:28,959
- Taro is...
- You're right.

988
00:43:28,959 --> 00:43:31,054
Taro's so good.

989
00:43:31,929 --> 00:43:34,927
[Taro found]

990
00:43:34,927 --> 00:43:36,225
Two, please.

991
00:43:36,225 --> 00:43:38,760
[Two large taros purchased]

992
00:43:38,760 --> 00:43:41,026
Are these yellow chives?

993
00:43:41,026 --> 00:43:43,232
- Are these yellow chives?
- Oh, yellow chives.

994
00:43:43,232 --> 00:43:44,333
That's interesting.

995
00:43:44,333 --> 00:43:46,405
These are seasonal too.

996
00:43:46,405 --> 00:43:49,238
[One bunch of yellow chives]
- These are so good stir-fried. - Interesting.

997
00:43:49,238 --> 00:43:52,277
- Why is that mushroom so big?
- King oyster mushroom.

998
00:43:52,277 --> 00:43:54,158
[Tomatoes]

999
00:43:54,158 --> 00:43:56,646
Half a portion, please.

1000
00:43:56,646 --> 00:43:57,580
Cut it into strips.

1001
00:43:57,580 --> 00:43:58,971
Meat?

1002
00:44:00,116 --> 00:44:01,784
[Shredded pork purchased]

1003
00:44:01,784 --> 00:44:03,719
Yes, thank you.

1004
00:44:03,719 --> 00:44:06,722
[She returns with her hands full]
Why does she have so many ingredients?

1005
00:44:07,560 --> 00:44:08,791
I'm looking forward to this.

1006
00:44:08,791 --> 00:44:11,160
[Empty kitchen during break, 4:00 PM]

1007
00:44:12,261 --> 00:44:14,931
[But Sunny can't rest]
That's some serious passion.

1008
00:44:14,931 --> 00:44:18,992
[Only by working this hard]
Ji Sun's way of doing things is incredible too.

1009
00:44:18,992 --> 00:44:21,437
No one can stop Jung Ji Sun now.

1010
00:44:21,437 --> 00:44:23,539
[Can she add a dish in half a day]

1011
00:44:25,808 --> 00:44:29,178
How do yellow chives taste different
from Korean chives?

1012
00:44:29,178 --> 00:44:30,513
They're more flavorful.

1013
00:44:30,513 --> 00:44:33,149
- Compared to Korean chives, the flavor...
- And they're much more tender.

1014
00:44:33,149 --> 00:44:34,739
More tender.

1015
00:44:35,418 --> 00:44:36,619
[King oyster mushrooms]

1016
00:44:36,619 --> 00:44:39,355
[Shiitake mushrooms]

1017
00:44:39,355 --> 00:44:41,860
[Green chilies] [Tomatoes]

1018
00:44:41,860 --> 00:44:43,292
Taro looks unusual.

1019
00:44:43,292 --> 00:44:46,796
Taro is really hard.

1020
00:44:46,796 --> 00:44:48,998
[Shredded pork]

1021
00:44:48,998 --> 00:44:50,526
[Oyster sauce] [Chicken stock] [Starch]

1022
00:44:50,526 --> 00:44:52,860
- Seasoning.
- Marinade.

1023
00:44:52,860 --> 00:44:56,221
[Once the shredded pork is mixed in]

1024
00:44:56,221 --> 00:44:58,601
[All the ingredients are ready]
What is she making?

1025
00:44:59,560 --> 00:45:02,178
[Cutting Board No. 2 spots Sunny]
The staff there...

1026
00:45:02,178 --> 00:45:04,927
[What is Sunny making this time?]
must think she's incredible too.

1027
00:45:04,927 --> 00:45:07,993
[A different approach this time]

1028
00:45:08,860 --> 00:45:12,121
[She asked him for advice]
What flavors does everyone like?

1029
00:45:12,121 --> 00:45:14,159
[The senior's hint: home-style...]
Home-style.

1030
00:45:14,159 --> 00:45:15,958
[With doubanjiang]
- Home-style. - Doubanjiang.

1031
00:45:15,958 --> 00:45:16,860
Doubanjiang.

1032
00:45:16,860 --> 00:45:20,396
[A stir-fry]
- And stir-fry. - Stir-fry.

1033
00:45:20,396 --> 00:45:22,131
[Looks around]

1034
00:45:22,131 --> 00:45:23,332
What is she looking for?

1035
00:45:23,332 --> 00:45:26,668
[What does she keep looking for?]

1036
00:45:27,827 --> 00:45:29,205
- What are you looking for?
- Huangdoujiang.

1037
00:45:29,205 --> 00:45:30,339
Huangdoujiang!

1038
00:45:30,339 --> 00:45:32,474
- Huangdoujiang?
- Yes.

1039
00:45:33,526 --> 00:45:37,246
[Huangdoujiang: fermented soybean paste]
It's like Korean doenjang, only saltier.

1040
00:45:37,246 --> 00:45:39,581
It has more umami.

1041
00:45:40,550 --> 00:45:43,418
- Is this it?
- Yes!

1042
00:45:44,987 --> 00:45:46,689
[First, she checks the aroma]

1043
00:45:46,689 --> 00:45:48,891
This is really strong.

1044
00:45:48,891 --> 00:45:51,928
[Ready. Time to heat the wok]

1045
00:45:51,928 --> 00:45:52,995
What is she making?

1046
00:45:52,995 --> 00:45:54,830
[King oyster mushrooms]

1047
00:45:54,830 --> 00:45:55,998
King oyster mushrooms.

1048
00:45:55,998 --> 00:45:57,166
I fried them.

1049
00:45:57,166 --> 00:46:01,526
- You fried them?
- To give them a meatier texture.

1050
00:46:01,526 --> 00:46:03,072
That's interesting.

1051
00:46:03,072 --> 00:46:04,159
[Numbing Sichuan peppercorns]

1052
00:46:04,159 --> 00:46:06,408
[Spicy dried chilies]
Making it spicy.

1053
00:46:07,946 --> 00:46:09,178
[Shredded green chilies go in]
Green chilies.

1054
00:46:09,178 --> 00:46:10,913
Chilies.

1055
00:46:12,267 --> 00:46:14,383
[Seasoned with rich huangdoujiang]

1056
00:46:14,383 --> 00:46:15,827
I mixed the saltiness

1057
00:46:15,827 --> 00:46:17,687
[Spicy doubanjiang]
with a little heat.

1058
00:46:17,687 --> 00:46:20,389
That looks good.

1059
00:46:20,389 --> 00:46:23,592
[She uses the senior's seasoning tip]

1060
00:46:25,526 --> 00:46:26,532
Stir-fry.

1061
00:46:26,532 --> 00:46:29,498
[Rapid wok tosses add smoky flavor]

1062
00:46:30,693 --> 00:46:32,235
What's she making this time?

1063
00:46:32,235 --> 00:46:34,203
[Kim Pung wants to know too]

1064
00:46:34,203 --> 00:46:37,959
[Time to taste]

1065
00:46:37,959 --> 00:46:39,909
[After tasting it, she walks away]

1066
00:46:39,909 --> 00:46:41,811
Where's she going? Why?
Is there something over there?

1067
00:46:41,811 --> 00:46:43,793
Do you need something?

1068
00:46:43,793 --> 00:46:45,393
Do you need something?

1069
00:46:45,393 --> 00:46:47,683
A small plate.

1070
00:46:49,485 --> 00:46:51,593
[First, she gets a small plate]
A plate.

1071
00:46:51,593 --> 00:46:53,326
Okay.

1072
00:46:53,326 --> 00:46:55,992
I wanted to make a single serving.

1073
00:46:55,992 --> 00:46:57,193
Oh, one serving.

1074
00:46:57,193 --> 00:46:58,259
Good thinking.

1075
00:46:58,259 --> 00:47:00,162
You don't need to make a lot.

1076
00:47:00,162 --> 00:47:02,098
Who told you to make that much? No one did.

1077
00:47:02,098 --> 00:47:03,359
It was for the staff meal!

1078
00:47:03,359 --> 00:47:05,901
You decided that yourself
and did it on your own.

1079
00:47:05,901 --> 00:47:08,544
No, they kept telling me to make more,
so that's why I made so much.

1080
00:47:08,544 --> 00:47:10,126
- Oh, did they?
- When I'm cooking alone...

1081
00:47:10,126 --> 00:47:12,959
How many dishes
are you making in those tiny portions?

1082
00:47:12,959 --> 00:47:16,511
I don't know.
I just wanted to try small portions.

1083
00:47:17,680 --> 00:47:23,680
[A new spicy home-style stir-fry]

1084
00:47:24,860 --> 00:47:28,057
[Determined]

1085
00:47:28,057 --> 00:47:29,226
[King Oyster Mushroom and Chili Stir-fry]

1086
00:47:29,226 --> 00:47:31,760
- This one looks good too.
- It looks good.

1087
00:47:33,863 --> 00:47:37,760
[She grabs the wok again?]

1088
00:47:37,760 --> 00:47:40,836
[Another dish?]

1089
00:47:40,836 --> 00:47:42,126
[Another new dish!]

1090
00:47:42,126 --> 00:47:45,686
She's making several dishes at once.

1091
00:47:45,686 --> 00:47:47,476
[A classic Sunny move]
Not a big batch of one dish.

1092
00:47:47,476 --> 00:47:50,479
[Less food, endless dishes?]
She's making several small ones.

1093
00:47:50,479 --> 00:47:54,516
[No telling how badly she wants this]

1094
00:47:55,393 --> 00:47:57,593
[She slowly cooks pork in oil]
It's called "hua," cooking it in oil.

1095
00:47:57,593 --> 00:47:58,454
- "Hua?"
- Yes.

1096
00:47:58,454 --> 00:48:02,591
It's a method of cooking it slowly
over low heat.

1097
00:48:03,526 --> 00:48:07,596
[The cooked pork rests for now]

1098
00:48:08,726 --> 00:48:10,032
Vegetables.

1099
00:48:10,032 --> 00:48:12,771
[Frying shredded taro in oil]

1100
00:48:12,771 --> 00:48:14,837
- That looks so good.
- Taro's really good fried.

1101
00:48:14,837 --> 00:48:18,026
[Sunny guarantees the fried taro]

1102
00:48:18,026 --> 00:48:23,211
[She sets aside the crispy taro]

1103
00:48:24,013 --> 00:48:25,827
[The pork goes back into the wok!]

1104
00:48:25,827 --> 00:48:28,226
Oh, that looks good.

1105
00:48:28,226 --> 00:48:29,352
She combines it with the pork?

1106
00:48:29,352 --> 00:48:32,788
[Then she adds the fried taro and stir-fries]

1107
00:48:33,726 --> 00:48:35,159
Oh, that looks good.

1108
00:48:35,159 --> 00:48:37,359
- That looks so good...
- Oh, that looks really good.

1109
00:48:38,461 --> 00:48:41,396
[Sunny's Fried Taro Stir-fry]
That looks good.

1110
00:48:44,400 --> 00:48:45,968
[It's ready!]

1111
00:48:45,968 --> 00:48:47,126
Try it.

1112
00:48:47,126 --> 00:48:48,838
Tasting time.

1113
00:48:48,838 --> 00:48:51,626
[Two spicy home-style stir-fries]
[King Oyster Mushroom and Chili Stir-fry]

1114
00:48:51,626 --> 00:48:54,402
[Fried Taro Stir-fry]
- They all look good. - Right.

1115
00:48:55,044 --> 00:48:58,948
[Will the two dishes win over Chengdu?]

1116
00:48:58,948 --> 00:49:02,684
[First, the Fried Taro Stir-fry]

1117
00:49:04,560 --> 00:49:06,354
I'll try one.

1118
00:49:08,324 --> 00:49:10,726
It's got to taste good.

1119
00:49:10,726 --> 00:49:12,761
[Nervous]

1120
00:49:13,896 --> 00:49:15,526
What is this? Stir-fried shredded potato?

1121
00:49:15,526 --> 00:49:18,401
- Shredded potato?
- No. It's taro.

1122
00:49:18,401 --> 00:49:20,569
- Taro?
- Yes.

1123
00:49:21,904 --> 00:49:23,860
It sticks to my teeth.

1124
00:49:23,860 --> 00:49:25,040
It sticks to his teeth?

1125
00:49:25,040 --> 00:49:28,110
[Hahaha]
Is it unfamiliar?

1126
00:49:28,110 --> 00:49:29,978
Oh, my.

1127
00:49:31,560 --> 00:49:34,159
[The fried taro texture seems unfamiliar]
I've never seen taro prepared like that either.

1128
00:49:34,159 --> 00:49:35,885
I've never tried it.

1129
00:49:35,885 --> 00:49:36,952
The second one.

1130
00:49:36,952 --> 00:49:40,322
[Next, the King Oyster Mushroom
and Chili Stir-fry]

1131
00:49:40,322 --> 00:49:42,258
This one's a little spicier.

1132
00:49:42,258 --> 00:49:43,660
[How is the spicy mushroom stir-fry?]

1133
00:49:43,660 --> 00:49:46,461
Did you stir-fry enoki mushrooms,
bell peppers, and shredded pork?

1134
00:49:46,461 --> 00:49:48,563
Something like that.

1135
00:49:50,793 --> 00:49:52,426
[I've got a feeling about this one]
This one...

1136
00:49:52,426 --> 00:49:53,669
- It's spicy.
- How is it?

1137
00:49:53,669 --> 00:49:56,404
[Doubanjiang meets huangdoujiang]

1138
00:49:57,226 --> 00:49:59,178
It's good.

1139
00:49:59,178 --> 00:50:00,259
He definitely likes spicy food.

1140
00:50:00,259 --> 00:50:02,978
[The mushroom stir-fry is a hit]
They really do like spicy food.

1141
00:50:02,978 --> 00:50:08,150
Our usual dishes also have
bell peppers and shredded pork.

1142
00:50:08,150 --> 00:50:10,553
[Similar to Chengdu's familiar Qingjiao Rousi]
This is based on Qingjiao Rousi,

1143
00:50:10,553 --> 00:50:12,655
- made like pepper japchae in Korea.
- Pepper japchae.

1144
00:50:12,655 --> 00:50:15,560
[The praise boosts her confidence]

1145
00:50:15,560 --> 00:50:16,592
Master.

1146
00:50:16,592 --> 00:50:17,693
[She immediately invites another taster]
Master.

1147
00:50:17,693 --> 00:50:19,395
Please try it.

1148
00:50:19,395 --> 00:50:21,159
Please try it.

1149
00:50:21,159 --> 00:50:23,199
- You want me to try it?
- She's excited.

1150
00:50:23,199 --> 00:50:24,436
I wonder what he'll say.

1151
00:50:24,436 --> 00:50:27,102
[Stove No. 3 joins the tasting]

1152
00:50:27,102 --> 00:50:28,393
[He picks the King Oyster Mushroom
and Chili Stir-fry]

1153
00:50:28,393 --> 00:50:31,806
Master Stove No. 3.

1154
00:50:33,809 --> 00:50:37,279
[Anticipation]

1155
00:50:40,560 --> 00:50:42,660
- Is it salty?
- It's good.

1156
00:50:42,660 --> 00:50:43,886
It's good.

1157
00:50:43,886 --> 00:50:44,992
[One good word, then he's gone]

1158
00:50:44,992 --> 00:50:46,541
He's so cool.

1159
00:50:47,560 --> 00:50:49,660
That little bit of approval isn't enough.

1160
00:50:49,660 --> 00:50:51,727
[Nods]
She's not satisfied.

1161
00:50:51,727 --> 00:50:53,128
[Let's see...]

1162
00:50:53,128 --> 00:50:55,564
Who's next?

1163
00:50:55,564 --> 00:50:59,835
[She invites a whole group of seniors]
I made a few dishes. Please try them.

1164
00:50:59,835 --> 00:51:03,359
[They head over for a group tasting]

1165
00:51:03,359 --> 00:51:05,641
This is fun.

1166
00:51:05,641 --> 00:51:07,259
- Is this it?
- Yes.

1167
00:51:07,259 --> 00:51:09,110
[Anticipation]
The Cutting Board Chief.

1168
00:51:10,045 --> 00:51:14,249
[He tries the King Oyster Mushroom
and Chili Stir-fry]

1169
00:51:15,284 --> 00:51:19,468
[Will the familiar flavor win him over?]
Let's see what he thinks.

1170
00:51:20,092 --> 00:51:22,757
[Nervous]

1171
00:51:27,460 --> 00:51:29,565
It's a little bland.

1172
00:51:29,565 --> 00:51:31,426
It's a little bland.

1173
00:51:31,426 --> 00:51:33,126
- He says it's bland.
- They really eat spicy food.

1174
00:51:33,126 --> 00:51:35,193
- It's bland?
- Exactly.

1175
00:51:35,193 --> 00:51:37,827
It has to be spicy and salty.

1176
00:51:37,827 --> 00:51:39,842
[Even this is bland?]

1177
00:51:39,842 --> 00:51:42,460
[That can't be...]

1178
00:51:42,460 --> 00:51:44,460
I think it's fine.

1179
00:51:44,460 --> 00:51:47,293
You have to eat it with the mushrooms.
There's no way it's bland.

1180
00:51:47,293 --> 00:51:52,658
[Unlike the chief, No. 2 loves it]

1181
00:51:52,658 --> 00:51:56,126
So people are divided on this one.

1182
00:51:56,126 --> 00:51:57,460
[It's hard to please Chengdu diners...]

1183
00:51:57,460 --> 00:51:59,227
This isn't easy.

1184
00:52:00,496 --> 00:52:02,797
Time for roll call.

1185
00:52:03,666 --> 00:52:05,034
[The tasting pauses after mixed reviews]

1186
00:52:05,034 --> 00:52:08,003
[It wouldn't feel right without roll call]

1187
00:52:08,804 --> 00:52:11,426
[Sunny's final roll call at Grandma's]
It's Sunny's final roll call.

1188
00:52:11,426 --> 00:52:13,126
Everyone, attention.

1189
00:52:13,126 --> 00:52:15,277
- Hello.
- Hello.

1190
00:52:15,277 --> 00:52:16,912
- Hello.
- Hello.

1191
00:52:16,912 --> 00:52:18,480
[Everyone focuses on the roll call]

1192
00:52:18,480 --> 00:52:22,318
[But Sunny can only think about...]

1193
00:52:22,318 --> 00:52:23,485
[Her new dish]

1194
00:52:23,485 --> 00:52:26,042
She's only thinking about her new dish.

1195
00:52:26,042 --> 00:52:27,672
You can tell she has a lot on her mind.

1196
00:52:27,672 --> 00:52:29,586
[Still no clear choice for the menu]

1197
00:52:30,259 --> 00:52:34,763
[Sunny ends roll call deep in thought]

1198
00:52:34,763 --> 00:52:37,059
How can she get a dish on the menu now?

1199
00:52:37,059 --> 00:52:38,867
- They're probably busy now.
- Exactly.

1200
00:52:38,867 --> 00:52:43,026
[Dinner prep, 4:35 PM]

1201
00:52:43,026 --> 00:52:45,240
[The senior spots Sunny's new dishes]
There's our senior in glasses.

1202
00:52:46,075 --> 00:52:49,578
- Try some.
- Sure, I'll try it.

1203
00:52:49,578 --> 00:52:53,348
[Hope he'll like it]
She wants everyone to give it a taste.

1204
00:52:54,183 --> 00:52:57,927
[First, the Fried Taro Stir-fry]

1205
00:52:57,927 --> 00:53:00,322
[How does it taste?]
There's fried taro stir-fry too.

1206
00:53:00,322 --> 00:53:01,590
Is this stir-fried shredded potato?

1207
00:53:01,590 --> 00:53:03,325
No, it's taro.

1208
00:53:03,325 --> 00:53:05,260
- What?
- Taro.

1209
00:53:05,260 --> 00:53:06,762
- Shredded taro?
- Yes.

1210
00:53:06,762 --> 00:53:09,731
[Even the senior finds taro unfamiliar]
Looks like he isn't familiar with taro.

1211
00:53:11,166 --> 00:53:13,501
King Oyster Mushroom and Chili Stir-fry.

1212
00:53:16,939 --> 00:53:20,309
[Will it get a positive reaction?]

1213
00:53:20,309 --> 00:53:24,380
[He takes another bite]

1214
00:53:24,380 --> 00:53:25,614
It's good.

1215
00:53:25,614 --> 00:53:27,950
[King Oyster Mushroom and Chili Stir-fry]
This one is good.

1216
00:53:27,950 --> 00:53:30,085
- You like that one?
- Yes.

1217
00:53:31,506 --> 00:53:32,788
Everyone says that one's good.

1218
00:53:32,788 --> 00:53:34,323
[The familiar spicy flavor works]

1219
00:53:35,057 --> 00:53:38,894
[He heads elsewhere after tasting her dish]

1220
00:53:38,894 --> 00:53:40,293
What?

1221
00:53:40,293 --> 00:53:41,296
What's going on?

1222
00:53:41,296 --> 00:53:43,632
[Taking Sunny's dish somewhere?]

1223
00:53:43,632 --> 00:53:45,701
Who to?

1224
00:53:45,701 --> 00:53:47,436
This one's good.

1225
00:53:47,436 --> 00:53:48,604
This one's good.

1226
00:53:48,604 --> 00:53:51,073
He's telling them it's good...

1227
00:53:51,073 --> 00:53:52,226
Not the Taro Stir-fry.

1228
00:53:52,226 --> 00:53:54,726
King Oyster Mushroom
and Chili Stir-fry is good.

1229
00:53:54,726 --> 00:53:56,145
"This one didn't work, but this one did."

1230
00:53:56,145 --> 00:53:57,479
[Showing off Sunny's dish to everyone]

1231
00:53:57,479 --> 00:53:59,485
[Sneaks over]

1232
00:53:59,485 --> 00:54:00,816
She's following the senior again.

1233
00:54:00,816 --> 00:54:02,460
[Sunny follows him]

1234
00:54:02,460 --> 00:54:04,319
Has the boss tried it?

1235
00:54:04,319 --> 00:54:08,026
[Boss Nam shows interest too]

1236
00:54:08,026 --> 00:54:11,326
- The boss has to approve it first.
- Right.

1237
00:54:11,927 --> 00:54:15,563
[Curious about Sunny's food]

1238
00:54:17,032 --> 00:54:20,268
[Boss Nam tastes it too]
He took the chopsticks.

1239
00:54:21,460 --> 00:54:22,827
Come on, try it!

1240
00:54:22,827 --> 00:54:26,059
He's acting like it's his own dish.

1241
00:54:26,059 --> 00:54:27,493
- That's my senior.
- Look at that face.

1242
00:54:27,493 --> 00:54:29,878
[Thank you, Guo Li Hong]
That's my senior.

1243
00:54:29,878 --> 00:54:33,148
[The fate of the King Oyster Mushroom
and Chili Stir-fry?]

1244
00:54:34,183 --> 00:54:35,451
Put it in the lunchboxes.

1245
00:54:35,451 --> 00:54:36,485
Put it in the lunchboxes.

1246
00:54:36,485 --> 00:54:38,787
I agree.

1247
00:54:40,092 --> 00:54:41,190
They're packing it to go?

1248
00:54:41,190 --> 00:54:44,760
Hold on. It looks like she pulled it off.

1249
00:54:44,760 --> 00:54:47,259
It's really good. It's delicious.

1250
00:54:47,259 --> 00:54:49,760
- It's stir-fried well. It suits our taste.
- Did she add meat?

1251
00:54:49,760 --> 00:54:51,800
[It's delicious!]
It's a vegetable dish, but...

1252
00:54:51,800 --> 00:54:56,126
Adding something spicy definitely
seems to suit their taste better.

1253
00:54:56,126 --> 00:54:57,673
Then this counts as a success, right?

1254
00:54:57,673 --> 00:55:00,560
- It's a success.
- Did she pull it off?

1255
00:55:00,560 --> 00:55:02,845
[Served as a side for delivery orders]
Lunchboxes have several side dishes anyway...

1256
00:55:02,845 --> 00:55:04,279
Like today's side dish.

1257
00:55:04,279 --> 00:55:06,248
This is basically...

1258
00:55:06,248 --> 00:55:08,450
I think that was basically a pass.

1259
00:55:08,450 --> 00:55:10,152
That's a 99% pass.

1260
00:55:10,152 --> 00:55:11,620
I didn't take it that way.

1261
00:55:11,620 --> 00:55:13,722
[That's too ambiguous]

1262
00:55:13,722 --> 00:55:15,224
As expected.

1263
00:55:15,224 --> 00:55:17,025
[That's our girl]
That's our chef.

1264
00:55:17,025 --> 00:55:20,326
[Still, a clear green light for the dish]

1265
00:55:20,326 --> 00:55:22,965
I think I put a lot of thought
into how to cook it.

1266
00:55:22,965 --> 00:55:24,626
It was a sauce they had here.

1267
00:55:24,626 --> 00:55:28,270
It smelled a little funky,
and it was really strong.

1268
00:55:28,270 --> 00:55:29,493
It made me wonder...

1269
00:55:29,493 --> 00:55:32,059
[She tried the local paste despite doubts]
"Is this going to work?"

1270
00:55:32,059 --> 00:55:34,109
That was the kind of sauce it was.

1271
00:55:34,109 --> 00:55:36,711
This is really strong.

1272
00:55:37,579 --> 00:55:41,293
[And spicy doubanjiang]

1273
00:55:41,293 --> 00:55:43,051
I used the sauces they had here.

1274
00:55:43,051 --> 00:55:44,953
Even if they were unfamiliar to me,

1275
00:55:44,953 --> 00:55:50,592
I realized I hadn't really understood
the local palate.

1276
00:55:50,592 --> 00:55:52,959
I finally got a feel for it today.

1277
00:55:52,959 --> 00:55:56,565
My goal is to get my dish
on this restaurant's menu.

1278
00:55:56,565 --> 00:55:58,600
So I'm going to give it a try.

1279
00:55:58,600 --> 00:56:00,702
I think it could definitely work.

1280
00:56:00,702 --> 00:56:02,471
- Looks like she might pull it off.
- She really might.

1281
00:56:02,471 --> 00:56:04,760
[Watch out, menu. Sunny's coming!]

1282
00:56:04,760 --> 00:56:06,574
[Current time: 5:00 PM]
5:00 PM.

1283
00:56:07,412 --> 00:56:09,159
[Everyone is getting ready for guests]

1284
00:56:09,159 --> 00:56:12,014
They're getting ready for guests now, right?
Everyone's busy.

1285
00:56:12,014 --> 00:56:13,693
[Sunny wanders instead of taking her station]

1286
00:56:13,693 --> 00:56:16,084
[Why?]

1287
00:56:16,084 --> 00:56:17,119
[Glances over]

1288
00:56:17,119 --> 00:56:18,720
Where's she going again?

1289
00:56:18,720 --> 00:56:20,722
[The prep station's slammed]

1290
00:56:21,992 --> 00:56:23,158
Sunny is...

1291
00:56:23,158 --> 00:56:26,060
[Sunny is heading toward...]

1292
00:56:27,863 --> 00:56:29,193
[Where the staff is gathered?]

1293
00:56:29,193 --> 00:56:30,726
The staff are gathered there.

1294
00:56:30,726 --> 00:56:32,500
What are they doing?

1295
00:56:33,159 --> 00:56:38,373
Which drink shop do you all like?

1296
00:56:38,373 --> 00:56:39,726
[Drinks?]
Or tea?

1297
00:56:39,726 --> 00:56:41,293
- Delivery?
- Coffee?

1298
00:56:41,293 --> 00:56:42,293
Why do you ask?

1299
00:56:42,293 --> 00:56:47,049
It's my last day, so I want to buy you coffee.

1300
00:56:47,049 --> 00:56:48,359
[That's Sunny] [That's our girl]

1301
00:56:48,359 --> 00:56:49,924
Oh, of course.

1302
00:56:49,924 --> 00:56:51,393
You don't need to do that.

1303
00:56:51,393 --> 00:56:54,590
- You don't need to do that.
- I'd feel bad if I didn't.

1304
00:56:54,590 --> 00:56:57,392
It's okay. We're all coworkers.

1305
00:56:57,392 --> 00:57:01,384
Even if you work here for one day,
we're still coworkers.

1306
00:57:02,359 --> 00:57:04,426
- That's admirable.
- The wisdom here...

1307
00:57:04,426 --> 00:57:05,526
It just keeps coming.

1308
00:57:05,526 --> 00:57:07,069
[Even one day makes you one of us]
This is like a Chinese movie.

1309
00:57:07,069 --> 00:57:08,760
[Getting swept up in the romance]
Chinese people are so romantic.

1310
00:57:08,760 --> 00:57:11,768
- Chinese people definitely have that.
- Right?

1311
00:57:12,507 --> 00:57:14,667
What drinks do you like? Tell me.

1312
00:57:14,667 --> 00:57:17,346
[The youngest gets excited]
- What do you like? - Drinks?

1313
00:57:17,346 --> 00:57:19,248
Why are you ordering so many?

1314
00:57:19,248 --> 00:57:24,019
I know. It's on me.

1315
00:57:24,019 --> 00:57:25,560
Are you getting them delivered?

1316
00:57:25,560 --> 00:57:28,726
[Guo Li Hong beams]

1317
00:57:28,726 --> 00:57:32,027
[Guo Li Hong and the youngest are thrilled]

1318
00:57:32,027 --> 00:57:33,460
- Don't order 30% sugar.
- Bubble tea?

1319
00:57:33,460 --> 00:57:35,693
It should be 30% sugar.
How could you drink it any sweeter?

1320
00:57:35,693 --> 00:57:37,626
It'll make your diabetes worse.

1321
00:57:37,626 --> 00:57:41,102
He's in his early twenties.
Why is he talking about diabetes?

1322
00:57:41,904 --> 00:57:43,338
[Grandma comes out too]

1323
00:57:43,338 --> 00:57:45,173
Grandma too.

1324
00:57:46,259 --> 00:57:48,277
Let me see.

1325
00:57:48,277 --> 00:57:50,126
[She's adorable]

1326
00:57:50,126 --> 00:57:53,315
[Everyone gathers to place their orders]

1327
00:57:53,315 --> 00:57:54,950
How about pickup?

1328
00:57:54,950 --> 00:57:57,393
- Ordering delivery runs over 500 yuan.
- That's okay.

1329
00:57:57,393 --> 00:57:58,726
- Delivery?
- Yeah.

1330
00:57:58,726 --> 00:58:00,022
[43 drinks for the entire staff]

1331
00:58:00,022 --> 00:58:02,824
- 43 drinks!
- 43 drinks.

1332
00:58:02,824 --> 00:58:05,894
- There are a lot of people.
- Her entire appearance fee...

1333
00:58:05,894 --> 00:58:07,696
On her ingredients...

1334
00:58:07,696 --> 00:58:10,259
[Spent on meals, ingredients, and gifts]
and now she's buying everyone drinks.

1335
00:58:10,259 --> 00:58:13,226
[Sunny cooks big and spends big]
She really goes big.

1336
00:58:13,226 --> 00:58:14,503
[Final dinner service, 6:00 PM]
This is the final service, right?

1337
00:58:14,503 --> 00:58:16,904
It's really ending.

1338
00:58:18,109 --> 00:58:20,943
[Guests may get Sunny's new dish]
Hold on. Will they really serve her new dish?

1339
00:58:20,943 --> 00:58:22,878
If it gets served, she succeeds.

1340
00:58:22,878 --> 00:58:24,546
- Right?
- Then it's definitely a success.

1341
00:58:24,546 --> 00:58:26,481
If it gets served here, she succeeds.

1342
00:58:26,481 --> 00:58:28,316
[Will she get her dish on the menu?]

1343
00:58:28,984 --> 00:58:30,519
[First, she handles the incoming orders]

1344
00:58:30,519 --> 00:58:33,055
At this point...

1345
00:58:33,055 --> 00:58:35,490
She's handling everything by herself.

1346
00:58:35,490 --> 00:58:39,927
[Everyone is fully focused on cooking]

1347
00:58:42,097 --> 00:58:48,570
[The busy kitchen is filled with heat]

1348
00:58:48,570 --> 00:58:49,771
[Sunny's gift arrives right on time]

1349
00:58:49,771 --> 00:58:50,959
It's here.

1350
00:58:50,959 --> 00:58:53,275
43 drinks.

1351
00:58:53,275 --> 00:58:55,243
Can the two of us carry all this?

1352
00:58:55,243 --> 00:58:57,127
Yes. Let's go.

1353
00:58:59,514 --> 00:59:01,893
This is really heavy.

1354
00:59:01,893 --> 00:59:04,653
She really goes big.

1355
00:59:04,653 --> 00:59:06,355
Sunny bought them.

1356
00:59:06,355 --> 00:59:08,090
It cost over 500 yuan.

1357
00:59:08,090 --> 00:59:09,591
That's a lot...

1358
00:59:09,591 --> 00:59:14,696
Sunny bought over 500 yuan worth
of drinks for all of you.

1359
00:59:14,696 --> 00:59:17,833
[Ooh]

1360
00:59:17,833 --> 00:59:20,026
[The owner tells the kitchen about the gift]

1361
00:59:20,026 --> 00:59:22,170
She really goes big.

1362
00:59:23,208 --> 00:59:24,873
They're here.

1363
00:59:24,873 --> 00:59:26,308
[Startled]
The tea delivery's here.

1364
00:59:26,308 --> 00:59:28,910
- The tea's here?
- Yes.

1365
00:59:28,910 --> 00:59:33,126
[Hurries to hand them out chilled]

1366
00:59:33,126 --> 00:59:36,159
[Proud]
She's really good at things like this.

1367
00:59:36,159 --> 00:59:37,819
She is.

1368
00:59:37,819 --> 00:59:40,293
That's why she tops the buzz rankings.

1369
00:59:40,293 --> 00:59:42,958
[Awkward]

1370
00:59:42,958 --> 00:59:46,660
Would you like a drink, Grandma?

1371
00:59:46,660 --> 00:59:48,763
Thank you.

1372
00:59:51,366 --> 00:59:55,404
[Sunny even puts in the straw herself]

1373
00:59:55,404 --> 00:59:58,293
- That's something our Ji Sun does well.
- She's very warm-hearted.

1374
00:59:58,293 --> 00:59:59,307
Thank you.

1375
00:59:59,307 --> 01:00:00,992
[Even the grill veteran says "thank you"]

1376
01:00:00,992 --> 01:00:03,177
That's what makes it so touching.

1377
01:00:04,793 --> 01:00:07,585
Xiexie-seumnida.

1378
01:00:07,585 --> 01:00:09,616
"Xiexie-seumnida."

1379
01:00:10,226 --> 01:00:11,553
That's touching.

1380
01:00:11,553 --> 01:00:15,239
I sometimes do that at my restaurant.

1381
01:00:15,239 --> 01:00:18,769
When the kitchen gets too hot and tough,
a glass of soda...

1382
01:00:18,769 --> 01:00:21,109
It's not a big deal, really.

1383
01:00:23,119 --> 01:00:26,239
Thank you for taking care of the staff.

1384
01:00:26,239 --> 01:00:28,449
- Thank you so much.
- I'm more grateful for everyone's help.

1385
01:00:28,449 --> 01:00:30,839
[She wanted to show her gratitude]
When it's at its hottest...

1386
01:00:30,839 --> 01:00:32,659
They're so thankful for this.

1387
01:00:33,619 --> 01:00:36,419
[The bustling hall]

1388
01:00:36,419 --> 01:00:38,129
[starts to quiet down as time passes]

1389
01:00:38,129 --> 01:00:40,159
[Is service almost over?]
Is it almost over?

1390
01:00:40,159 --> 01:00:43,059
[Day 5, closing soon]
Wait, emergency.

1391
01:00:43,059 --> 01:00:45,559
[Final mission ending soon]
Is it coming in now? The new menu?

1392
01:00:45,559 --> 01:00:47,349
Let's go, let's go.

1393
01:00:47,349 --> 01:00:48,819
[Sunny is on the move?]

1394
01:00:48,819 --> 01:00:52,088
- I have to try the menu now.
- You have to do it now, now's the time.

1395
01:00:52,839 --> 01:00:56,259
[She's been waiting for this moment]

1396
01:00:57,059 --> 01:00:58,979
Are you doing the one from earlier? Or...

1397
01:00:58,979 --> 01:01:00,579
- Something new.
- Something new?

1398
01:01:00,579 --> 01:01:01,839
- Yes.
- Wow.

1399
01:01:01,839 --> 01:01:03,173
Again?

1400
01:01:03,173 --> 01:01:04,879
- This is the fourth dish today.
- I'm going to try...

1401
01:01:04,879 --> 01:01:06,159
Until it works.

1402
01:01:06,159 --> 01:01:07,749
- It's the fourth dish.
- Something new again?

1403
01:01:07,749 --> 01:01:11,219
Oh... you're making another menu?

1404
01:01:11,219 --> 01:01:13,399
I have a feeling this won't be the last.

1405
01:01:13,399 --> 01:01:15,459
- That's what I'm thinking.
- No, it's because of the mission.

1406
01:01:15,459 --> 01:01:17,509
Are you going to be in Season 2 as well?

1407
01:01:17,509 --> 01:01:19,679
[In Chengdu forever... until it works...]
"If it doesn't work, I'll be in Season 2."

1408
01:01:19,679 --> 01:01:22,499
- Because of the mission...
- "I'll keep making staff meals until it works."

1409
01:01:22,499 --> 01:01:25,089
[Season 2 from the very start]
- "I'll start with the staff meal." - "I'll do it."

1410
01:01:25,089 --> 01:01:27,409
- "You're hungry, right?"
- Aw man...

1411
01:01:27,409 --> 01:01:30,245
I don't think this will be the last one.

1412
01:01:31,619 --> 01:01:34,416
[What's Sunny's new menu for the final goal?]
I wonder.

1413
01:01:36,529 --> 01:01:38,979
[Gearing up with determination]
Oh... as expected.

1414
01:01:38,979 --> 01:01:40,079
She looks determined.

1415
01:01:40,079 --> 01:01:42,159
[Into the heated wok,]

1416
01:01:42,159 --> 01:01:44,853
[the oil is swirled]

1417
01:01:45,668 --> 01:01:46,898
Garlic.

1418
01:01:46,898 --> 01:01:48,862
[Infusing oil with minced garlic and ginger]

1419
01:01:49,519 --> 01:01:51,969
[The next ingredient?]

1420
01:01:51,969 --> 01:01:55,109
[Tossing in meat marinated in special sauce]
Meat.

1421
01:01:57,479 --> 01:02:00,039
[Skillful]
- She's really skillful now. - I know.

1422
01:02:00,039 --> 01:02:01,249
[Yellow chives]
Chives?

1423
01:02:01,249 --> 01:02:03,158
Yellow chives.

1424
01:02:03,859 --> 01:02:06,599
[Adding ingredients without hesitation]

1425
01:02:06,599 --> 01:02:11,119
[Sunny's confidence]

1426
01:02:11,119 --> 01:02:13,599
I need the chilies behind you.

1427
01:02:13,599 --> 01:02:15,239
Are you making it spicy?

1428
01:02:15,239 --> 01:02:19,969
- Yes. Let's add a lot of doubanjiang.
- I keep thinking about that feedback.

1429
01:02:19,969 --> 01:02:21,439
[Bam!]
Yes, add plenty of it.

1430
01:02:21,439 --> 01:02:23,279
[Huangdoujiang returns]
I'll add huangdoujiang and other ingredients.

1431
01:02:23,279 --> 01:02:24,919
- Huangdoujiang.
- I'm stir-frying it again.

1432
01:02:24,919 --> 01:02:26,369
- It looks delicious.
- It'll have a different flavor.

1433
01:02:26,369 --> 01:02:27,799
[Doubanjiang and huangdoujiang]
That's it.

1434
01:02:27,799 --> 01:02:32,559
[Trying a new dish with the rich sauce
that had a good rating earlier]

1435
01:02:34,239 --> 01:02:37,249
[Using the popular seasoning
with ingredients familiar to Chengdu locals]

1436
01:02:37,939 --> 01:02:39,799
[Welcoming]
It's Yellow Chives with Shredded Pork.

1437
01:02:39,799 --> 01:02:41,989
Yellow Chives with Shredded Pork.

1438
01:02:42,929 --> 01:02:48,337
[Bringing out the spice
with passionate wok-work]

1439
01:02:49,719 --> 01:02:51,439
[Yum]
It looks delicious.

1440
01:02:51,439 --> 01:02:53,169
[Carefully tasting it]

1441
01:02:53,169 --> 01:02:54,979
Let's see.

1442
01:02:54,979 --> 01:02:56,789
[Something's missing...]

1443
01:02:56,789 --> 01:02:58,265
- What is it?
- Why?

1444
01:02:58,265 --> 01:02:59,799
- This is chili oil, right?
- Chili oil.

1445
01:02:59,799 --> 01:03:00,833
Yes, it's chili oil.

1446
01:03:00,833 --> 01:03:02,149
- Finally!
- Yes!

1447
01:03:02,149 --> 01:03:03,969
- It was chili oil.
- You have to use chili oil.

1448
01:03:03,969 --> 01:03:05,799
- It's chili oil.
- That's right.

1449
01:03:05,799 --> 01:03:07,919
- Can't miss out on chili oil.
- Chili oil is the key.

1450
01:03:07,919 --> 01:03:08,999
Finally.

1451
01:03:08,999 --> 01:03:10,419
That's a relief.

1452
01:03:10,419 --> 01:03:12,659
[Relieved]
I feel better now.

1453
01:03:12,659 --> 01:03:14,359
[Drawn by the spicy aroma]
This is it. This is it.

1454
01:03:14,359 --> 01:03:15,909
This will definitely work.

1455
01:03:15,909 --> 01:03:19,429
[People flocking around Sunny]

1456
01:03:19,429 --> 01:03:20,879
- This can't fail.
- Exactly.

1457
01:03:20,879 --> 01:03:23,719
She even added chili oil.

1458
01:03:23,719 --> 01:03:25,539
[Intrigued]

1459
01:03:25,539 --> 01:03:28,839
[Focus]
Everyone's gathered around now.

1460
01:03:28,839 --> 01:03:31,999
[Sunny's spicy new dish is finished in no time]

1461
01:03:31,999 --> 01:03:33,699
- I'm 100% sure they'll like it.
- This one...

1462
01:03:33,699 --> 01:03:35,399
- 100%.
- Look at the color.

1463
01:03:35,399 --> 01:03:37,349
[Yellow Chives with Shredded Pork]
- She added chili oil. - It's reddish now.

1464
01:03:37,349 --> 01:03:39,679
- This is it, this is it.
- This will work.

1465
01:03:39,679 --> 01:03:40,879
It's reddish now.

1466
01:03:40,879 --> 01:03:43,409
- I was waiting for this color.
- This is the one.

1467
01:03:43,409 --> 01:03:44,919
[Crowding around]
Here it comes.

1468
01:03:44,919 --> 01:03:46,209
This is a success.

1469
01:03:46,209 --> 01:03:47,969
[Gulp]
Everyone likes it.

1470
01:03:47,969 --> 01:03:49,109
Everyone's salivating.

1471
01:03:49,109 --> 01:03:50,499
Right, right.

1472
01:03:50,499 --> 01:03:52,319
And she already gave them drinks.

1473
01:03:52,319 --> 01:03:53,969
Oh, that's right.

1474
01:03:53,969 --> 01:03:56,046
[Good thing she gave out drinks]
They already had the drinks.

1475
01:03:56,046 --> 01:03:57,429
Right.

1476
01:03:57,429 --> 01:04:00,253
- Everyone's in a good mood now.
- They're in a great mood.

1477
01:04:00,253 --> 01:04:02,239
For sure.

1478
01:04:02,239 --> 01:04:05,029
[People gather, drawn by the smell]

1479
01:04:05,029 --> 01:04:08,879
[A good feeling about this]

1480
01:04:08,879 --> 01:04:12,069
[I want to eat it now]

1481
01:04:12,739 --> 01:04:15,429
[Sunny turns back to the stove]

1482
01:04:15,429 --> 01:04:17,679
[She's grabbing the wok again?]

1483
01:04:17,679 --> 01:04:19,159
All of a sudden?

1484
01:04:19,159 --> 01:04:20,885
[Knowing Sunny well]
- Is there another dish? - Yes.

1485
01:04:20,885 --> 01:04:25,089
- Another one? Hold on. The fifth menu item.
- Again? Why is she grabbing the wok?

1486
01:04:25,089 --> 01:04:26,659
- Oh, really?
- Super ambitious.

1487
01:04:26,659 --> 01:04:27,879
- The fifth menu item.
- No way.

1488
01:04:27,879 --> 01:04:29,619
See? I told you that wasn't the last one.

1489
01:04:29,619 --> 01:04:30,719
[Impressive]
Hold on.

1490
01:04:30,719 --> 01:04:31,919
It's like that show.

1491
01:04:31,919 --> 01:04:34,439
Master of Living. "It's not over yet."

1492
01:04:35,319 --> 01:04:38,039
[Master of Chinese Cuisine]
- "There's more." - "It's not over yet."

1493
01:04:38,039 --> 01:04:40,639
Don't think about whether it'll work.

1494
01:04:40,639 --> 01:04:42,368
I just do as much as I can!

1495
01:04:42,368 --> 01:04:44,334
That's my mindset right now.

1496
01:04:44,334 --> 01:04:45,371
I knew it.

1497
01:04:45,371 --> 01:04:47,799
[Evaluations aside]

1498
01:04:47,799 --> 01:04:51,889
[Starting the fifth dish with conviction]

1499
01:04:51,889 --> 01:04:54,130
[Tomato]
Tomatoes.

1500
01:04:54,949 --> 01:04:55,959
Oh? This is it.

1501
01:04:55,959 --> 01:04:57,059
Yes, chili oil sauce.

1502
01:04:57,059 --> 01:04:58,100
Chili oil sauce, this is it!

1503
01:04:58,100 --> 01:05:01,989
- Yes, yes! This is it!
- This is what I'm talking about.

1504
