A new menu in just one day.

1741
01:14:56,899 --> 01:14:59,459
Though, I can't handle the cooking station.

1742
01:14:59,459 --> 01:15:02,209
[The prep station is his limit]
I'm strictly prep station material.

1743
01:15:02,209 --> 01:15:04,629
King oyster mushrooms, shiitake mushrooms...

1744
01:15:05,839 --> 01:15:10,759
[The mushroom dish hits the spot
for Xu Jian Kai]

1745
01:15:10,759 --> 01:15:14,259
[While positive reviews are pouring in...]

1746
01:15:14,259 --> 01:15:15,639
Now, this table here...

1747
01:15:15,639 --> 01:15:17,859
- These people are the important ones.
- This is the crucial part.

1748
01:15:18,549 --> 01:15:20,129
What dish is this? Is it mushrooms?

1749
01:15:20,129 --> 01:15:22,049
Shiitake mushrooms!

1750
01:15:22,049 --> 01:15:25,174
[The owner tastes the mushroom dish]

1751
01:15:26,471 --> 01:15:27,649
This mushroom dish is good. It's to my taste.

1752
01:15:27,649 --> 01:15:29,972
She says it's to her taste.

1753
01:15:30,689 --> 01:15:31,879
This is good, right?

1754
01:15:31,879 --> 01:15:34,149
Oh. "It's delicious."

1755
01:15:34,149 --> 01:15:35,559
[The mushroom dish is praised by leadership]
"It's delicious."

1756
01:15:35,559 --> 01:15:38,529
- This looks really delicious.
- Yeah, it does.

1757
01:15:39,646 --> 01:15:42,365
[What about this?]

1758
01:15:42,365 --> 01:15:44,209
Yellow chive and pork.

1759
01:15:44,209 --> 01:15:46,309
The seasoning on this one is a bit lacking...

1760
01:15:46,309 --> 01:15:49,079
- Okay, okay. That's fine.
- The seasoning is a bit off on this.

1761
01:15:49,079 --> 01:15:50,832
[Nods]
Right?

1762
01:15:51,969 --> 01:15:53,619
It'd be better with some pickled peppers...

1763
01:15:53,619 --> 01:15:56,309
- Pickled peppers...
- She should've added more peppers.

1764
01:15:56,309 --> 01:16:05,599
[It must pass the leadership to be on the menu]

1765
01:16:06,519 --> 01:16:08,279
- Have you eaten?
- Yes, I have.

1766
01:16:08,279 --> 01:16:10,891
[Time to face it head-on!]
- Have you eaten, Sunny? - I don't eat.

1767
01:16:11,989 --> 01:16:15,189
[Sunny comes out to hear the feedback]

1768
01:16:15,189 --> 01:16:17,639
Did you enjoy the food?

1769
01:16:17,639 --> 01:16:19,089
It was good!

1770
01:16:19,089 --> 01:16:22,049
The Stir-fried Mushrooms with Chili
and Soy Sauce were good.

1771
01:16:22,049 --> 01:16:23,889
That stir-fried mushroom dish was good.

1772
01:16:23,889 --> 01:16:25,719
That stir-fried king oyster mushroom.

1773
01:16:25,719 --> 01:16:27,799
- Let's put it on the menu!
- Everyone's reacting well to this one.

1774
01:16:27,799 --> 01:16:29,749
- Yeah, yeah.
- We can put this on the menu.

1775
01:16:29,749 --> 01:16:30,989
Right.

1776
01:16:30,989 --> 01:16:33,200
That stir-fried king oyster mushroom.

1777
01:16:33,200 --> 01:16:35,376
[Confirming the positive reaction]

1778
01:16:36,474 --> 01:16:41,084
[Sunny prepares to ask the big question]

1779
01:16:42,039 --> 01:16:44,079
Let me ask you one thing!

1780
01:16:47,468 --> 01:16:50,359
Is there anything we can sell to customers?

1781
01:16:50,359 --> 01:16:53,703
[Out of the three dishes]
Is there anything we can sell to customers?

1782
01:16:53,703 --> 01:16:56,339
Which of these can we sell to customers?

1783
01:16:56,339 --> 01:16:58,378
I'm curious.

1784
01:17:00,719 --> 01:17:02,309
I think the Yellow Chive and Pork is okay.

1785
01:17:02,309 --> 01:17:03,989
- Me too.
- Oh, the Yellow Chive and Pork.

1786
01:17:03,989 --> 01:17:06,839
Those two liked it.

1787
01:17:06,839 --> 01:17:11,009
[Granny and Boss Nam remain silent...]

1788
01:17:11,009 --> 01:17:14,759
What Sunny cooked today...

1789
01:17:14,759 --> 01:17:18,229
wasn't authentic Sichuan cuisine.

1790
01:17:18,229 --> 01:17:22,749
Sichuan cuisine is actually...
a very demanding and complex cuisine.

1791
01:17:22,749 --> 01:17:24,359
Sunny...

1792
01:17:24,359 --> 01:17:28,949
doesn't have a deep understanding
of Sichuan cuisine yet.

1793
01:17:28,949 --> 01:17:33,519
If it's not authentic Sichuan,

1794
01:17:33,519 --> 01:17:38,394
it doesn't meet the local standards.

1795
01:17:38,394 --> 01:17:41,089
I agree.

1796
01:17:41,089 --> 01:17:44,229
[The consensus: it's not authentic Sichuan]
That it's not authentic Sichuan cuisine...

1797
01:17:44,229 --> 01:17:46,179
[Sunny in Chengdu]

1798
01:17:46,179 --> 01:17:47,679
[Final mission failed]

1799
01:17:47,679 --> 01:17:49,429
Oh, she failed.

1800
01:17:49,429 --> 01:17:51,009
Gosh! It's a failure.

1801
01:17:51,009 --> 01:17:52,179
[Head drops]

1802
01:17:52,179 --> 01:17:54,069
- Oh, no...
- This is an emergency.

1803
01:17:54,069 --> 01:17:55,779
[Solemn...]
Oh, wait a minute.

1804
01:17:55,779 --> 01:17:57,559
No, wait a second.

1805
01:17:57,559 --> 01:17:59,459
Wait, what happens to the show then?

1806
01:17:59,459 --> 01:18:01,482
Oh, wait a minute.

1807
01:18:02,769 --> 01:18:04,039
[Sunny's unbelievable mission failure]
No way...

1808
01:18:04,039 --> 01:18:05,399
The process is what matters.

1809
01:18:05,399 --> 01:18:08,439
Wait, is this a real failure?
Did she really fail everything?

1810
01:18:08,439 --> 01:18:10,375
- This is crazy.
- Oh, guys.

1811
01:18:10,375 --> 01:18:12,609
[She made six dishes today alone...]

1812
01:18:12,609 --> 01:18:14,305
[Eyes wide]
Do you know how much money we spent?

1813
01:18:14,305 --> 01:18:17,498
[Even the introvert can't stay silent]
She just went there and spent money.

1814
01:18:17,498 --> 01:18:19,409
This is really a failure...

1815
01:18:19,409 --> 01:18:21,779
[She accepts it] [Final mission failed]
Failure.

1816
01:18:21,779 --> 01:18:23,159
Honestly...

1817
01:18:23,159 --> 01:18:25,969
- I thought she'd make it.
- To be honest, I thought she'd make it.

1818
01:18:25,969 --> 01:18:28,099
[Now, he's their only hope]
- She failed? - This...

1819
01:18:28,099 --> 01:18:30,479
- Hold on...
- Sichuan cuisine is tough.

1820
01:18:30,479 --> 01:18:32,439
[I should've made more dishes]

1821
01:18:32,439 --> 01:18:35,159
Sichuan cuisine values three things:
color, aroma, and taste.

1822
01:18:35,159 --> 01:18:38,035
Color, aroma, and taste.

1823
01:18:38,839 --> 01:18:42,062
I understand. I'll keep studying.

1824
01:18:43,223 --> 01:18:44,823
[Grandma holds her wrist one last time]

1825
01:18:44,823 --> 01:18:46,919
[Rubbing]

1826
01:18:46,919 --> 01:18:49,649
She's touching it
because it's a boxer's wrist, isn't she?

1827
01:18:50,839 --> 01:18:52,727
Look at Sunny's hands.

1828
01:18:52,727 --> 01:18:53,863
Look at her hands.

1829
01:18:53,863 --> 01:18:57,009
Look at her hands. She's a boxer for sure.

1830
01:18:57,009 --> 01:19:00,229
My hands are big. Very big.

1831
01:19:01,169 --> 01:19:03,559
[A boxer's hands are different]
A boxer.

1832
01:19:03,559 --> 01:19:05,319
She says it right away.

1833
01:19:05,319 --> 01:19:08,119
How old were you when you started boxing?

1834
01:19:08,709 --> 01:19:11,239
At what age?

1835
01:19:11,239 --> 01:19:13,779
I think I was about 19.

1836
01:19:13,779 --> 01:19:17,178
[Still zero suspicion about Sunny's identity]

1837
01:19:18,869 --> 01:19:22,899
[It's time to reveal her identity...]
You have to reveal your identity now.

1838
01:19:22,899 --> 01:19:24,789
[Sunny's identity reveal is imminent]
Oh, right. The identity.

1839
01:19:24,789 --> 01:19:26,639
- Right.
- She has to reveal who she is.

1840
01:19:26,639 --> 01:19:28,279
- I didn't know how to do it.
- Her identity...

1841
01:19:28,279 --> 01:19:29,999
- How should she reveal it now?
- She has to do it.

1842
01:19:29,999 --> 01:19:32,819
[How will Sunny reveal her identity?]
This is hard.

1843
01:19:32,819 --> 01:19:34,279
Was it hard for you to cook?

1844
01:19:34,279 --> 01:19:35,879
The wok was a bit heavy.

1845
01:19:35,879 --> 01:19:37,219
It was really heavy.

1846
01:19:37,219 --> 01:19:40,519
You had a great rhythm with the wok.

1847
01:19:40,519 --> 01:19:42,289
You're really good at using it.

1848
01:19:42,289 --> 01:19:44,370
Oh, really?

1849
01:19:46,309 --> 01:19:50,239
[She's receiving compliments, but...]

1850
01:19:50,239 --> 01:19:53,199
[Sunny's smile is forced]

1851
01:19:53,199 --> 01:19:56,309
[Her lips are dry]

1852
01:19:56,309 --> 01:20:02,039
[The staff gathers around Sunny]

1853
01:20:03,189 --> 01:20:06,049
[Restless]

1854
01:20:07,379 --> 01:20:08,519
[Sunny approaches Xu Jian Kai]

1855
01:20:08,519 --> 01:20:10,559
You know...

1856
01:20:10,559 --> 01:20:13,159
- TikTok, TikTok.
- TikTok?

1857
01:20:13,159 --> 01:20:16,549
[Using MZ Kai's SNS to reveal her identity]

1858
01:20:16,549 --> 01:20:18,119
No one...

1859
01:20:18,119 --> 01:20:20,259
- Since they don't use SNS at all.
- In China,

1860
01:20:20,259 --> 01:20:21,619
they use different social media.

1861
01:20:21,619 --> 01:20:24,369
Here, they only use TikTok.

1862
01:20:24,369 --> 01:20:26,639
- They use TikTok.
- Yes, only that.

1863
01:20:26,639 --> 01:20:29,310
[Revealing her identity with MZ Kai's help!]
Xu Jian Kai, until the very end...

1864
01:20:29,310 --> 01:20:33,009
- Played a big role.
- He helped because he's young.

1865
01:20:33,009 --> 01:20:34,849
[But what are they looking for?]

1866
01:20:34,849 --> 01:20:35,959
That's right.

1867
01:20:35,959 --> 01:20:38,079
My name...

1868
01:20:38,079 --> 01:20:39,889
Jung Ji Sun.

1869
01:20:39,889 --> 01:20:42,199
[Her name?]
Jung Ji Sun.

1870
01:20:42,199 --> 01:20:45,969
[Searching for "Jung Ji Sun" on social media]

1871
01:20:45,969 --> 01:20:47,719
When you search for Jung Ji Sun...

1872
01:20:47,719 --> 01:20:51,109
- She's there.
- Sunny's there!

1873
01:20:51,109 --> 01:20:53,249
Her name...

1874
01:20:53,249 --> 01:20:54,819
[She's on there?]

1875
01:20:54,819 --> 01:20:56,979
You can search for Jung Ji Sun.

1876
01:20:56,979 --> 01:20:58,759
Jung Ji Sun.

1877
01:20:58,759 --> 01:21:00,419
You can search for Jung Ji Sun.

1878
01:21:00,419 --> 01:21:01,679
Everyone is starting to...

1879
01:21:01,679 --> 01:21:04,100
[Why is Sunny on there?]
They're starting to get surprised now.

1880
01:21:04,100 --> 01:21:06,499
Sunny is on TikTok?

1881
01:21:06,499 --> 01:21:08,499
This person is Sunny?

1882
01:21:08,499 --> 01:21:09,969
Yes, this is Sunny.

1883
01:21:09,969 --> 01:21:13,079
[While they're looking at Sunny
on social media]

1884
01:21:13,079 --> 01:21:14,679
Look at that.

1885
01:21:14,679 --> 01:21:16,689
- Look at that.
- Look at what?

1886
01:21:16,689 --> 01:21:18,399
- Look over there?
- Why? Where?

1887
01:21:18,399 --> 01:21:20,116
- Where?
- Is there something?

1888
01:21:20,116 --> 01:21:22,319
What are they looking at all of a sudden?

1889
01:21:22,319 --> 01:21:25,749
[What are they supposed to look at?]

1890
01:21:26,719 --> 01:21:29,109
[Everyone focuses on the big screen]

1891
01:21:29,109 --> 01:21:31,279
[The "Sunny" you all know]
Actually, I...

1892
01:21:31,279 --> 01:21:32,879
[A video revealing Sunny's identity]
Through a video...

1893
01:21:32,879 --> 01:21:34,879
Like that.

1894
01:21:35,589 --> 01:21:41,089
[Korea's top Chinese cuisine chef, Jung Ji Sun]
[Footage provided by Netflix]

1895
01:21:43,473 --> 01:21:45,839
[Blink, blink]
He's blinking his eyes right now.

1896
01:21:45,839 --> 01:21:47,349
Who... Who is that?

1897
01:21:47,349 --> 01:21:48,789
Who is that?

1898
01:21:48,789 --> 01:21:50,019
[Why is Sunny on TV?]
They don't recognize her.

1899
01:21:50,019 --> 01:21:52,209
Who is that?

1900
01:21:52,209 --> 01:21:53,919
[Huh? What is this?]
None of them know.

1901
01:21:53,919 --> 01:21:55,647
Look at Xu Jian Kai's expression.

1902
01:21:55,647 --> 01:21:56,659
Look at his face.

1903
01:21:56,659 --> 01:21:58,549
Jung Ji Sun...

1904
01:21:58,549 --> 01:22:00,609
[Jung Ji Sun... is Sunny?]

1905
01:22:00,633 --> 01:22:03,762
[Undercover revealed]

1906
01:22:06,738 --> 01:22:07,811
[Chop, chop]

1907
01:22:07,811 --> 01:22:10,292
Wow, she's amazing...

1908
01:22:10,292 --> 01:22:11,978
[Wok skills?]

1909
01:22:11,978 --> 01:22:14,122
[She's always been good!]
Basically,

1910
01:22:14,122 --> 01:22:17,002
[Jung Ji Sun, Queen of Chinese Cuisine]
Chinese cuisine...

1911
01:22:17,002 --> 01:22:20,152
[And another person who is most surprised]

1912
01:22:20,152 --> 01:22:21,942
Our Senior Chef with glasses!

1913
01:22:21,942 --> 01:22:23,562
Senior Chef with glasses.

1914
01:22:23,562 --> 01:22:26,402
[The Senior Chef with glasses keeps searching]
Look at him now.

1915
01:22:26,402 --> 01:22:27,802
I was so surprised to find out

1916
01:22:27,802 --> 01:22:32,372
that she's actually a top-tier chef.

1917
01:22:32,372 --> 01:22:35,108
Sunny was a hidden master,
and I was just a novice.

1918
01:22:37,142 --> 01:22:41,402
Actually, I graduated from

1919
01:22:41,402 --> 01:22:44,692
the culinary department in Yangzhou.

1920
01:22:44,692 --> 01:22:46,612
[I see]
I graduated from Yangzhou University.

1921
01:22:46,612 --> 01:22:48,842
I run two Chinese restaurants in Korea.

1922
01:22:48,842 --> 01:22:50,322
They're Chinese restaurants.

1923
01:22:50,322 --> 01:22:53,112
My specialty is dim sum.

1924
01:22:53,112 --> 01:22:56,402
[Korea's Dim Sum Queen]
My specialty is dim sum.

1925
01:22:56,402 --> 01:22:58,742
No wonder her knife work was so fast.

1926
01:23:00,902 --> 01:23:03,012
Xu Jian Kai.

1927
01:23:03,012 --> 01:23:06,182
[Still in shock]

1928
01:23:07,092 --> 01:23:09,572
Sunny's wok skills were amazing. Truly!

1929
01:23:09,572 --> 01:23:12,312
She was better than our chefs.

1930
01:23:12,312 --> 01:23:14,520
No wonder she learned everything so fast.

1931
01:23:14,520 --> 01:23:16,792
"No wonder. I knew something was up."

1932
01:23:16,792 --> 01:23:18,372
I kind of felt it.

1933
01:23:18,372 --> 01:23:19,562
[Xu Jian Kai]

1934
01:23:19,562 --> 01:23:23,322
She was a beginner, but better than others!

1935
01:23:23,322 --> 01:23:25,382
She only learned for a few days,

1936
01:23:25,382 --> 01:23:27,302
but she was already so good.

1937
01:23:27,302 --> 01:23:29,112
[There was a reason]

1938
01:23:29,112 --> 01:23:32,501
But the grandmother still thinks I'm a boxer.

1939
01:23:32,501 --> 01:23:35,892
[Sunny? Boxer and Chef!]
- Even now? - Even now.

1940
01:23:35,892 --> 01:23:37,332
She's just that pure.

1941
01:23:37,332 --> 01:23:38,852
- Yeah.
- Exactly.

1942
01:23:38,852 --> 01:23:41,592
[No suspicion even after the reveal]
- No one suspects a thing. - No suspicion.

1943
01:23:41,592 --> 01:23:43,892
I only found out today
that Sunny is a boss too.

1944
01:23:43,892 --> 01:23:47,562
So Sunny is a boss as well.

1945
01:23:47,562 --> 01:23:50,602
I hope we can meet often in the future

1946
01:23:50,602 --> 01:23:53,032
and talk more.

1947
01:23:53,032 --> 01:23:54,632
Sunny.

1948
01:23:54,632 --> 01:23:56,362
Sunny, you are a wonderful person.

1949
01:23:56,362 --> 01:23:58,444
Oh, that's so cool.

1950
01:23:58,444 --> 01:23:59,972
When are you coming back to Chengdu?

1951
01:23:59,972 --> 01:24:02,662
I think I'll be back this year.

1952
01:24:02,662 --> 01:24:04,602
- This year?
- Yes, this year.

1953
01:24:04,602 --> 01:24:06,122
Will you come to see us then?

1954
01:24:06,122 --> 01:24:07,892
- Of course!
- "Of course."

1955
01:24:07,892 --> 01:24:10,842
[Greeting the young Prep Station Senior]
- "Of course." - "Of course."

1956
01:24:10,842 --> 01:24:13,082
I've run this place for over 20 years,

1957
01:24:13,082 --> 01:24:14,772
but I had no idea about Sunny's identity.

1958
01:24:14,772 --> 01:24:17,702
I'll make dim sum for you next time.

1959
01:24:17,702 --> 01:24:20,746
Great. You're always welcome.

1960
01:24:20,746 --> 01:24:24,472
Grandma, you're amazing. You're the best.

1961
01:24:24,472 --> 01:24:27,062
I think that for this show,

1962
01:24:27,062 --> 01:24:30,522
regardless of success or failure...

1963
01:24:30,522 --> 01:24:34,102
I'm grateful that I could just hold the wok
and cook like that.

1964
01:24:34,102 --> 01:24:36,562
[Satisfied!]
I'm satisfied with these five days.

1965
01:24:36,562 --> 01:24:40,532
I'm grateful that I was able
to hold the wok in such a short time.

1966
01:24:40,532 --> 01:24:43,012
[Even for Jung Ji Sun, the Dim Sum Queen]
I learned so much.

1967
01:24:43,012 --> 01:24:44,152
These five days...

1968
01:24:44,152 --> 01:24:46,042
I can only think about how short they were.

1969
01:24:46,042 --> 01:24:47,462
- To be honest.
- We learned a lot too.

1970
01:24:47,462 --> 01:24:49,002
Exactly.

1971
01:24:49,002 --> 01:24:53,119
[Jung Ji Sun's "Undercover Chef" ends]

1972
01:24:53,119 --> 01:24:54,532
Now,

1973
01:24:54,532 --> 01:24:57,512
the actual last hope of "Undercover Chef..."

1974
01:24:57,512 --> 01:24:59,302
[Ahem, ahem]
He's become our last hope.

1975
01:24:59,302 --> 01:25:02,003
Everyone, just trust me.

1976
01:25:02,003 --> 01:25:04,360
Our Napoli Matfia!

1977
01:25:04,360 --> 01:25:06,322
- Let's go, let's go!
- Chef Kwon Sung Jun...

1978
01:25:06,322 --> 01:25:07,812
In Naples...

1979
01:25:07,812 --> 01:25:11,163
will he really be able to leave his name?

1980
01:25:11,163 --> 01:25:13,942
[Day 5, Naples, Italy. Sam Kwon, not Kwon Sung Jun]
- I'm excited. - I'm really excited.

1981
01:25:13,942 --> 01:25:16,867
[Identity in danger?]
- What? - What?

1982
01:25:16,867 --> 01:25:20,232
[Before the last lunch service...]

1983
01:25:20,232 --> 01:25:21,828
[In the middle of chatting]

1984
01:25:21,828 --> 01:25:22,908
Yes, yes.

1985
01:25:22,908 --> 01:25:24,228
Kwon, what's your real Korean name?

1986
01:25:24,228 --> 01:25:25,868
Pardon?

1987
01:25:25,868 --> 01:25:27,808
Wait a minute.

1988
01:25:27,808 --> 01:25:29,168
- What's going on?
- All of a sudden?

1989
01:25:29,168 --> 01:25:30,828
What's with the sudden question?

1990
01:25:30,828 --> 01:25:32,578
Hold on. If he gets caught now,

1991
01:25:32,578 --> 01:25:33,988
the final mission won't even matter.

1992
01:25:33,988 --> 01:25:35,728
It'll just be over.

1993
01:25:35,728 --> 01:25:37,838
Emergency! Emergency!

1994
01:25:37,838 --> 01:25:39,458
[Haha]

1995
01:25:39,458 --> 01:25:41,148
Oh, man. What do we do?

1996
01:25:41,148 --> 01:25:42,588
[Getting caught on the 5th day?]

1997
01:25:42,588 --> 01:25:46,208
Actually, he prepared the most
meticulously out of the three.

1998
01:25:46,208 --> 01:25:48,208
[Emergency 5 hours before undercover ends]
The one...

1999
01:25:48,208 --> 01:25:51,458
who prepared most meticulously
is about to get caught.

2000
01:25:51,458 --> 01:25:55,168
[Adjusts his bandana due to the crisis...]
We'll see tonight.

2001
01:25:55,168 --> 01:25:56,228
Emergency.

2002
01:25:56,228 --> 01:25:58,918
[Do something, Sung Jun!]
- Emergency. - No.

2003
01:25:58,918 --> 01:26:00,068
Should we take a photo?

2004
01:26:00,068 --> 01:26:01,988
- A sudden change of topic.
- Sure, let's take one!

2005
01:26:01,988 --> 01:26:04,498
- Let's take a photo.
- Let's take a photo.

2006
01:26:04,498 --> 01:26:07,648
- Okay.
- That was close.

2007
01:26:09,378 --> 01:26:10,928
[Rustle, rustle]

2008
01:26:10,928 --> 01:26:13,118
- What now?
- What is it?

2009
01:26:13,118 --> 01:26:15,348
[What's going on now?]

2010
01:26:15,348 --> 01:26:16,988
- What is it?
- Huh?

2011
01:26:16,988 --> 01:26:18,258
- What's going on?
- What is it?

2012
01:26:18,258 --> 01:26:20,125
- What are you looking for?
- What...

2013
01:26:20,911 --> 01:26:23,078
- Oh, Senior Chef Pa.
- Why?

2014
01:26:23,078 --> 01:26:25,742
[Senior Chef Pa brings something
from the locker room]

2015
01:26:26,588 --> 01:26:30,288
[Kwon whistles as he heads to the back kitchen]

2016
01:26:30,288 --> 01:26:32,398
[The two run into each other]

2017
01:26:32,398 --> 01:26:35,548
Kwon! Come here for a second.

2018
01:26:35,548 --> 01:26:37,088
[What's going on all of a sudden?]
Why?

2019
01:26:37,088 --> 01:26:39,148
Why is he calling you?

2020
01:26:40,958 --> 01:26:42,638
Take off your bandana!

2021
01:26:42,638 --> 01:26:44,448
- Take off your bandana!
- Oh!

2022
01:26:44,448 --> 01:26:45,938
[Finally!]

2023
01:26:45,938 --> 01:26:47,468
Oh, really?

2024
01:26:47,468 --> 01:26:49,868
[The long-awaited moment?]

2025
01:26:49,868 --> 01:26:53,438
- You'll wear this to work from now on.
- Really?

2026
01:26:53,438 --> 01:26:55,438
Kwon, you've finally been promoted!

2027
01:26:55,438 --> 01:26:56,958
He's been recognized.

2028
01:26:56,958 --> 01:26:58,948
[The glorious chef's hat ceremony]
So this is the promotion.

2029
01:26:58,948 --> 01:27:00,908
He's a full-time employee now.

2030
01:27:00,908 --> 01:27:03,248
[The past days flash by like a panorama...]
From an intern...

2031
01:27:03,248 --> 01:27:07,678
While cooking, the heat...

2032
01:27:08,318 --> 01:27:10,788
[Finally taking off the tight bandana]

2033
01:27:10,788 --> 01:27:14,078
[Upgrading to a chef's hat]
Does it fit?

2034
01:27:14,078 --> 01:27:15,378
[Failed to upgrade to a chef's hat?]
[Crumple, crumple]

2035
01:27:15,378 --> 01:27:17,199
My head is a bit big...

2036
01:27:18,588 --> 01:27:21,468
[Me?]
Wait a second. Isn't that Xu Jian Kai?

2037
01:27:21,468 --> 01:27:23,468
[I'm Kwon Jian Kai]
- It's Xu Jian Kai. - Oh, you're right.

2038
01:27:23,468 --> 01:27:25,568
He looks like Xu Jian Kai now.

2039
01:27:25,568 --> 01:27:27,108
You say your head is big?

2040
01:27:27,108 --> 01:27:29,458
[Embarrassed]
- I'll make it larger. - Yes, yes.

2041
01:27:29,458 --> 01:27:32,768
[Wait a second]

2042
01:27:32,768 --> 01:27:34,388
[Extraordinary measures for Grande-sized Kwon]

2043
01:27:34,388 --> 01:27:36,978
- Because his head is big...
- My head is big.

2044
01:27:36,978 --> 01:27:39,838
[Are those scissors?]
- Use scissors? - With scissors...

2045
01:27:40,478 --> 01:27:42,978
[Instant chef's hat alteration]

2046
01:27:42,978 --> 01:27:44,688
- Is it ready?
- Let's see.

2047
01:27:44,688 --> 01:27:46,478
[Heart pounding]

2048
01:27:46,478 --> 01:27:48,148
Ah, one, two!

2049
01:27:48,148 --> 01:27:50,498
[The hat ceremony resumes]
One, two!

2050
01:27:50,498 --> 01:27:51,858
Perfect, perfect.

2051
01:27:51,858 --> 01:27:54,108
- It's finally on.
- Great!

2052
01:27:54,108 --> 01:27:56,078
There, it's perfect!

2053
01:27:56,078 --> 01:27:57,908
- Very good.
- Now that you're wearing this...

2054
01:27:57,908 --> 01:28:00,658
- You really look like one of them.
- Right.

2055
01:28:01,508 --> 01:28:05,491
- It means you're an official member of our restaurant.
- Official.

2056
01:28:05,491 --> 01:28:06,528
A full-time employee.

2057
01:28:06,528 --> 01:28:11,268
It means you've officially
become a member of our restaurant.

2058
01:28:11,268 --> 01:28:13,988
You've only been here a few days,
but you've adapted well.

2059
01:28:13,988 --> 01:28:18,237
And you have a good relationship with us.

2060
01:28:18,237 --> 01:28:19,348
That's our Senior Chef Pa.

2061
01:28:19,348 --> 01:28:21,998
- That's so heartwarming.
- It really is.

2062
01:28:21,998 --> 01:28:24,448
I think I'll cry when it's time to leave.

2063
01:28:24,448 --> 01:28:27,858
- It's perfect!
- It looks great on you.

2064
01:28:27,858 --> 01:28:29,988
- You're so handsome!
- Really?

2065
01:28:29,988 --> 01:28:33,808
- I know.
- He says he knows.

2066
01:28:33,808 --> 01:28:35,888
- What did Kwon say?
- He said he knows.

2067
01:28:35,888 --> 01:28:37,508
"You're so handsome." And he said, "I know."

2068
01:28:37,508 --> 01:28:38,948
Naples style!

2069
01:28:38,948 --> 01:28:40,988
[Shameless]
He likes it, so he's smiling.

2070
01:28:40,988 --> 01:28:42,368
[You're the best!]

2071
01:28:42,368 --> 01:28:43,518
Yes, I know.

2072
01:28:43,518 --> 01:28:45,138
"Yes, I know."

2073
01:28:45,138 --> 01:28:47,408
He says he knows.

2074
01:28:47,408 --> 01:28:50,498
[The last lunch service begins]
[1:00 PM]

2075
01:28:50,498 --> 01:28:52,418
[The empty dining area...]

2076
01:28:52,418 --> 01:28:53,568
[is soon packed with customers]

2077
01:28:53,568 --> 01:28:56,188
- It's so busy even on the last day.
- You're right.

2078
01:28:56,188 --> 01:28:57,358
Emergency.

2079
01:28:57,358 --> 01:29:00,048
[The kitchen gets busy]
Emergency.

2080
01:29:00,996 --> 01:29:04,048
[But Sam Kwon
still has his final mission left...]

2081
01:29:04,048 --> 01:29:06,828
By the way, how is he going
to do the final mission?

2082
01:29:06,828 --> 01:29:09,758
- This is bad.
- He must be so nervous.

2083
01:29:09,758 --> 01:29:11,728
[Anxious...]

2084
01:29:11,728 --> 01:29:13,308
[And just like that, the last lunch service...]

2085
01:29:13,308 --> 01:29:14,638
Wait a minute.

2086
01:29:14,638 --> 01:29:18,448
- There's no time.
- This is no time to be laughing.

2087
01:29:19,598 --> 01:29:23,148
[Lunch service is already coming to an end]

2088
01:29:23,148 --> 01:29:24,798
[Without even having time
to think about the final mission]

2089
01:29:24,798 --> 01:29:26,608
- There's almost no time to rest.
- You're right.

2090
01:29:26,608 --> 01:29:29,868
[Lunch service is over in a heartbeat]
Another half-day has passed.

2091
01:29:29,868 --> 01:29:32,308
Goodbye!

2092
01:29:32,308 --> 01:29:34,478
[Current time: 6:00 PM]
It's 6:00 PM.

2093
01:29:34,478 --> 01:29:35,858
They finished really late.

2094
01:29:35,858 --> 01:29:37,328
Lunch service was long.

2095
01:29:37,328 --> 01:29:39,568
Lunch service was really long.

2096
01:29:42,548 --> 01:29:43,758
[Only the menu is on his mind...]
Right now, Kwon Sung Jun is...

2097
01:29:43,758 --> 01:29:45,618
- He must be so stressed.
- It's an emergency.

2098
01:29:45,618 --> 01:29:47,148
- It's a real emergency.
- It really is.

2099
01:29:47,148 --> 01:29:49,548
A major emergency.

2100
01:29:49,548 --> 01:29:52,708
What time should we have dinner?

2101
01:29:52,708 --> 01:29:54,978
Around 7:00?

2102
01:29:54,978 --> 01:29:57,668
[Since it's 6:00 now...]

2103
01:29:57,668 --> 01:29:58,798
No, there's no time...

2104
01:29:58,798 --> 01:30:00,848
[Jumping up]
Yes, there's surprisingly little time.

2105
01:30:00,848 --> 01:30:03,588
I'll be done at 6:00 PM.
I have to get ready for business again.

2106
01:30:03,588 --> 01:30:07,223
[To get ready for business?]
You need to get ready. What do you do now?

2107
01:30:07,908 --> 01:30:10,120
[But...]
- Hold on. - What?

2108
01:30:10,788 --> 01:30:13,408
- Where did he go?
- Where did he go?

2109
01:30:14,498 --> 01:30:16,188
- Why?
- Why?

2110
01:30:16,188 --> 01:30:17,918
[Wandering alone in the front yard]

2111
01:30:17,918 --> 01:30:20,238
Why?

2112
01:30:20,238 --> 01:30:22,689
[All of a sudden?]
Why? What are you going to do up there?

2113
01:30:22,689 --> 01:30:24,559
What's up there?

2114
01:30:26,027 --> 01:30:28,768
[Quietly enters the kitchen on the 2nd floor]

2115
01:30:28,768 --> 01:30:31,538
[Suddenly opens the fridge]

2116
01:30:31,538 --> 01:30:33,268
What is it?

2117
01:30:33,268 --> 01:30:34,658
[He's pulling something out]

2118
01:30:34,658 --> 01:30:36,258
- He did something.
- What is it?

2119
01:30:36,258 --> 01:30:37,788
- What did you do?
- I prepared something!

2120
01:30:37,788 --> 01:30:40,078
Wait, it looks like a liquid.

2121
01:30:40,078 --> 01:30:42,558
[Observing carefully...]
What could it be?

2122
01:30:42,558 --> 01:30:44,128
[Sigh]

2123
01:30:44,128 --> 01:30:47,468
The most important thing
is that it's the last day,

2124
01:30:47,468 --> 01:30:50,308
but I'm already busy with work,
and they're making me do all this.

2125
01:30:50,308 --> 01:30:51,668
But still...

2126
01:30:51,668 --> 01:30:54,208
[His true feelings on the last day]
That's true...

2127
01:30:54,208 --> 01:30:56,208
- He has so many complaints.
- Seriously.

2128
01:30:56,208 --> 01:30:57,488
Look at my face right now.

2129
01:30:57,488 --> 01:30:58,848
Full of dissatisfaction!

2130
01:30:58,848 --> 01:31:00,848
- You're like a pufferfish full of venom.
- So venomous!

2131
01:31:00,848 --> 01:31:02,828
He really looks like a venomous pufferfish.

2132
01:31:02,828 --> 01:31:04,188
I'm so busy with work,

2133
01:31:04,188 --> 01:31:06,768
and they're making me do all this. But still,

2134
01:31:06,768 --> 01:31:09,328
[Final mission]
since there was a mission for this show,

2135
01:31:09,328 --> 01:31:13,148
I put in some effort to accomplish it.

2136
01:31:13,148 --> 01:31:16,964
[Final Mission Strategy]
[Through the staff meal]

2137
01:31:16,964 --> 01:31:20,277
[Planning to be evaluated for the new menu]
Oh, really?

2138
01:31:21,108 --> 01:31:24,596
[What menu will Kwon present?]
What menu will he make?

2139
01:31:24,596 --> 01:31:28,244
The secret ingredient is...

2140
01:31:28,244 --> 01:31:29,348
[Clams]

2141
01:31:29,348 --> 01:31:31,508
- Manila clams!
- Manila clams.

2142
01:31:31,508 --> 01:31:33,348
[Why choose clams for the final mission?]
Vongole.

2143
01:31:33,348 --> 01:31:34,772
At the very beginning,

2144
01:31:34,772 --> 01:31:37,796
they asked me what food I like.

2145
01:31:37,796 --> 01:31:42,018
[Day 3, Lunch]
Kwon! What kind of food do you like to cook?

2146
01:31:42,018 --> 01:31:45,396
Vongole pasta.

2147
01:31:45,396 --> 01:31:47,188
- Vongole pasta?
- Yes.

2148
01:31:47,188 --> 01:31:49,556
- Oil-based or tomato-based?
- Oil-based!

2149
01:31:49,556 --> 01:31:50,964
- Oil-based?
- Yes.

2150
01:31:50,964 --> 01:31:53,708
[Satisfied with the answer]
- That's classic Naples cuisine! - Yes.

2151
01:31:53,708 --> 01:31:56,324
- So it's typical Naples cuisine.
- Vongole is Naples cuisine.

2152
01:31:56,324 --> 01:31:58,768
Since this is a Trattoria,

2153
01:31:58,768 --> 01:32:01,037
I decided to cook local food.

2154
01:32:01,037 --> 01:32:01,796
The tone and manner.

2155
01:32:01,796 --> 01:32:05,092
And I noticed there was no vongole
or seafood pasta on the menu.

2156
01:32:05,092 --> 01:32:09,248
There's baccalà, but I wouldn't call it
a typical seafood pasta.

2157
01:32:09,248 --> 01:32:11,092
[Pork fat pasta]
Is there no oil-based pasta here?

2158
01:32:11,092 --> 01:32:13,012
[Potato pasta]
- No. - Wait, no vongole pasta at all?

2159
01:32:13,012 --> 01:32:14,884
[Genovese beef and onion pasta]
No vongole.

2160
01:32:14,884 --> 01:32:17,908
[Amidst meat and vegetable-based pastas]
- It's an inland area. - That's true.

2161
01:32:17,908 --> 01:32:21,428
So I thought it'd be good
to try a dish using clams.

2162
01:32:21,428 --> 01:32:23,508
[Max confidence]
I made it because I'm confident in it.

2163
01:32:23,508 --> 01:32:26,436
[Kwon chooses an authentic Naples pasta]
- A direct approach. - Indeed.

2164
01:32:26,436 --> 01:32:29,156
[Near the end of lunch today]

2165
01:32:29,156 --> 01:32:30,500
[Thinking]

2166
01:32:30,500 --> 01:32:32,436
So, what are we having for dinner?

2167
01:32:32,436 --> 01:32:35,380
Did you have any ideas?

2168
01:32:35,380 --> 01:32:37,913
["Something else..." Is this an opportunity?]
Something else?

2169
01:32:37,913 --> 01:32:39,492
I had to seize the opportunity.

2170
01:32:39,492 --> 01:32:42,244
[Pondering...]

2171
01:32:42,244 --> 01:32:45,476
In that case, could I try making vongole pasta?

2172
01:32:45,476 --> 01:32:47,556
Making his move immediately.

2173
01:32:47,556 --> 01:32:50,116
[Will it work?]
I'm going for it!

2174
01:32:50,116 --> 01:32:52,148
[Senior Pa agrees]
Okay!

2175
01:32:52,148 --> 01:32:54,116
I think oil-based is tastier!

2176
01:32:54,116 --> 01:32:56,158
[Laura also agrees without hesitation]
Oil-based is tastier.

2177
01:32:56,158 --> 01:32:58,852
Here's how we do it sometimes!

2178
01:32:58,852 --> 01:33:01,812
It's oil-based, but we add cherry tomatoes!

2179
01:33:01,812 --> 01:33:04,100
[Kwon's final mission is set!]
Oil-based with cherry tomatoes!

2180
01:33:04,100 --> 01:33:08,244
They're giving hints away.

2181
01:33:08,244 --> 01:33:11,988
[He checked in between business hours]

2182
01:33:11,988 --> 01:33:15,188
[Kwon checked the clams being purged]
They've been purged.

2183
01:33:15,188 --> 01:33:17,604
[Starting to cook]
[Rinsing the purged clams]

2184
01:33:17,604 --> 01:33:18,660
[Scrubbing]
But there's no time.

2185
01:33:18,660 --> 01:33:21,204
- To purge them properly...
- Right.

2186
01:33:21,204 --> 01:33:22,964
[Since it's an important mission]

2187
01:33:22,964 --> 01:33:25,316
[It'd be a disaster if there's sand!]

2188
01:33:25,316 --> 01:33:26,468
[Clatter]

2189
01:33:26,468 --> 01:33:29,188
[Means "Damn it"]
Mannaggia...

2190
01:33:30,388 --> 01:33:31,661
[Is he nervous?]

2191
01:33:31,661 --> 01:33:34,580
At that time,
I was in a rush because I had no time.

2192
01:33:34,580 --> 01:33:36,612
I used to say I could do it
with my eyes closed.

2193
01:33:36,612 --> 01:33:38,948
But if I make a mistake, it's over.

2194
01:33:38,948 --> 01:33:40,740
[Nervously checking each one carefully]
Clams are...

2195
01:33:40,740 --> 01:33:43,220
- They're not easy.
- True.

2196
01:33:43,220 --> 01:33:46,018
- If there's one grain of sand in it...
- Exactly.

2197
01:33:46,018 --> 01:33:47,044
Really.

2198
01:33:47,044 --> 01:33:49,908
[After washing them so thoroughly]
- It's just over. - It's over.

2199
01:33:49,908 --> 01:33:52,628
[A bowl of clams]

2200
01:33:52,628 --> 01:33:55,892
[Vongole pasta begins]
So you're making authentic vongole now?

2201
01:33:55,892 --> 01:33:58,788
[Plenty of olive oil and garlic in a pot]
It's authentic vongole.

2202
01:34:00,608 --> 01:34:03,508
[When the garlic starts to sizzle]
- You put garlic in with the skin? - Yes.

2203
01:34:03,508 --> 01:34:05,089
You'll crush it slightly.

2204
01:34:06,020 --> 01:34:09,188
[The clams go in]

2205
01:34:09,188 --> 01:34:13,444
[The clams he's been cleaning
and rinsing all day...]

2206
01:34:13,444 --> 01:34:15,844
[Scraping every last one in]

2207
01:34:15,844 --> 01:34:18,100
Wow, that's a lot.

2208
01:34:19,028 --> 01:34:20,918
[Sniff]

2209
01:34:21,988 --> 01:34:23,636
[Pouring in white wine
to remove the fishy smell]

2210
01:34:23,636 --> 01:34:25,194
White wine.

2211
01:34:26,500 --> 01:34:28,052
[Covering it with foil as a lid]

2212
01:34:28,052 --> 01:34:30,628
Are you covering it to trap the heat?

2213
01:34:30,628 --> 01:34:32,936
[Boiling until the clams open]
Since there's no lid.

2214
01:34:35,268 --> 01:34:39,700
[Taking out a pan to sauté the pasta]

2215
01:34:39,700 --> 01:34:41,044
[He disappears somewhere...]

2216
01:34:41,044 --> 01:34:43,364
Why? Is there a problem?

2217
01:34:43,364 --> 01:34:44,920
[A moment later]
Why?

2218
01:34:46,148 --> 01:34:47,454
[He appears wearing the chef's hat
he'd forgotten]

2219
01:34:47,454 --> 01:34:49,540
- He changed his hat.
- Wow.

2220
01:34:49,540 --> 01:34:51,428
[Looking dignified, he praises himself]
It looks dignified.

2221
01:34:52,036 --> 01:34:54,740
[Opening the clam pot with dignity]

2222
01:34:54,740 --> 01:34:57,748
- The clams are cooked well.
- Are they cooked well?

2223
01:34:57,748 --> 01:35:01,088
[Mixing so they cook evenly]

2224
01:35:01,088 --> 01:35:04,308
[While the clam broth
becomes rich and flavorful]

2225
01:35:04,308 --> 01:35:07,268
[Another item appears]
What's that?

2226
01:35:07,268 --> 01:35:09,684
[Peperoncino oil]

2227
01:35:09,684 --> 01:35:10,980
Peperoncino oil.

2228
01:35:10,980 --> 01:35:15,012
[Pouring it straight into the pasta pan]

2229
01:35:15,012 --> 01:35:17,524
- Do they like spicy food here?
- No.

2230
01:35:17,524 --> 01:35:19,860
[Warning: It's quite spicy]
Hold on.

2231
01:35:19,860 --> 01:35:22,148
[He has a plan]

2232
01:35:22,148 --> 01:35:24,068
[The dish Sam Kwon made
for the staff meal on Day 3]

2233
01:35:24,068 --> 01:35:26,068
Thank you for the food, Kwon.

2234
01:35:26,068 --> 01:35:30,308
[Soy Sauce & Spicy Seasoned Chicken]
Thank you for what you've made.

2235
01:35:30,308 --> 01:35:33,172
[Especially...]

2236
01:35:33,172 --> 01:35:35,524
The spicy sauce is delicious!

2237
01:35:35,524 --> 01:35:38,468
You're right, it's good.

2238
01:35:38,468 --> 01:35:39,988
[He was even praised
for the "perfect level of spiciness"]

2239
01:35:39,988 --> 01:35:41,428
[He has a plan]
The perfect spiciness.

2240
01:35:41,428 --> 01:35:43,012
That's important.

2241
01:35:43,012 --> 01:35:47,435
[Trying that "perfect spiciness" again!]
They'll probably like this level.

2242
01:35:50,128 --> 01:35:51,684
[But...]

2243
01:35:51,684 --> 01:35:54,964
[He adds quite a lot]

2244
01:35:54,964 --> 01:35:56,836
Huh?

2245
01:35:56,836 --> 01:35:59,700
Wait, this is basically Sichuan cuisine.

2246
01:36:00,372 --> 01:36:03,524
[Is this a spicy food challenge?]
He's making Sichuan food here.

2247
01:36:05,508 --> 01:36:06,852
[Sensing something...
Laura heads to the kitchen]

2248
01:36:06,852 --> 01:36:08,268
What? Seriously?

2249
01:36:08,268 --> 01:36:09,380
Is that spicy?

2250
01:36:09,380 --> 01:36:11,668
[Kwon?]

2251
01:36:12,644 --> 01:36:15,572
[First...]
I added some peperoncino oil.

2252
01:36:17,220 --> 01:36:20,516
[That looks like it'll be very spicy...]

2253
01:36:20,516 --> 01:36:22,532
[I knew it!]

2254
01:36:22,532 --> 01:36:23,828
Is this regular oil?

2255
01:36:23,828 --> 01:36:25,051
- Olive oil.
- Regular oil.

2256
01:36:25,051 --> 01:36:29,668
[To control the heat,
he adds regular olive oil]

2257
01:36:29,668 --> 01:36:31,364
To make it as mild as possible.

2258
01:36:31,364 --> 01:36:33,140
To enhance the umami flavor,

2259
01:36:33,140 --> 01:36:34,932
[Watching closely]
I mixed them together.

2260
01:36:34,932 --> 01:36:38,428
Did you film five days' worth
of interviews at once?

2261
01:36:38,428 --> 01:36:40,644
- No... I don't think so.
- How can he be so consistent?

2262
01:36:40,644 --> 01:36:42,628
[Every day is exactly the same.]
It's probably just the same.

2263
01:36:42,628 --> 01:36:44,340
A consistent man.

2264
01:36:44,340 --> 01:36:45,924
Exactly the same.

2265
01:36:45,924 --> 01:36:47,572
To make it as mild as possible,

2266
01:36:47,572 --> 01:36:50,372
I mixed them together to enhance the umami.

2267
01:36:50,372 --> 01:36:52,878
[It's confusing!]
He's exceptionally consistent.

2268
01:36:52,878 --> 01:36:57,124
[While Kwon's carefully blended oil
is infused with garlic aroma]

2269
01:36:57,124 --> 01:37:01,140
[Clams open up, releasing milky broth]

2270
01:37:01,140 --> 01:37:05,652
[Checking if they're cooked
under the owner's watchful eye]

2271
01:37:07,908 --> 01:37:11,252
[Tilting head...]
Are they all cooked?

2272
01:37:11,252 --> 01:37:13,860
- I think I taste... some sand.
- Sand?

2273
01:37:13,860 --> 01:37:16,180
- Wait a minute.
- You washed them thoroughly, right?

2274
01:37:16,180 --> 01:37:17,588
Purging them...

2275
01:37:17,588 --> 01:37:19,652
[He washed them one by one...]
- It usually takes... - Right.

2276
01:37:19,652 --> 01:37:21,204
- It takes a long time.
- Did you do it for a day?

2277
01:37:21,204 --> 01:37:22,612
It hasn't been a full day.

2278
01:37:22,612 --> 01:37:24,768
[Purged for about half a day]
I couldn't do it for a full day.

2279
01:37:24,768 --> 01:37:27,644
[The smell is okay]
[Let me try one more...]

2280
01:37:29,284 --> 01:37:33,332
[Laura also carefully tastes it]

2281
01:37:33,332 --> 01:37:36,080
[There's sand in it]
Yes, yes.

2282
01:37:36,080 --> 01:37:38,249
[The owner eventually spits out the clam]
What are we going to do about this?

2283
01:37:38,249 --> 01:37:41,012
Purging is the most important part.

2284
01:37:41,012 --> 01:37:43,844
You have to get all the sand
out from inside the shell.

2285
01:37:43,844 --> 01:37:45,508
Even if they look fine on the outside,

2286
01:37:45,508 --> 01:37:47,476
if you catch one that still has sand...

2287
01:37:47,476 --> 01:37:49,476
- It'll be gritty in the mouth.
- Exactly.

2288
01:37:49,476 --> 01:37:51,972
- You can't tell by looking.
- A risky menu.

2289
01:37:51,972 --> 01:37:53,444
Risky.

2290
01:37:53,444 --> 01:37:56,788
He really chose a very risky dish.

2291
01:37:56,788 --> 01:37:59,540
That's right. I'm a man who enjoys risk.

2292
01:37:59,540 --> 01:38:01,236
You enjoy risk?

2293
01:38:01,236 --> 01:38:03,892
[Overpowering the risk with confidence]

2294
01:38:03,892 --> 01:38:06,988
- I like that he's consistent.
- It'll be delicious.

2295
01:38:07,988 --> 01:38:10,900
[Meanwhile, Kwon gets serious
over the clam issue...]

2296
01:38:10,900 --> 01:38:12,372
[The aroma and taste
indicate they're fresh, but]

2297
01:38:12,372 --> 01:38:14,937
Oh, what should you do?

2298
01:38:14,937 --> 01:38:20,004
[Still gritty even after tasting again]
They weren't purged well enough.

2299
01:38:20,004 --> 01:38:21,380
[Sigh]

2300
01:38:21,380 --> 01:38:23,878
I wasn't quite happy
with the condition of the clams...

2301
01:38:23,878 --> 01:38:25,156
This is a bit of a problem.

2302
01:38:25,156 --> 01:38:27,732
- This is bad.
- I should've bought it yesterday.

2303
01:38:27,732 --> 01:38:30,587
[What he picks up is...]

2304
01:38:31,428 --> 01:38:32,980
[A strainer?]

2305
01:38:32,980 --> 01:38:35,124
A strainer?

2306
01:38:35,124 --> 01:38:37,332
[Planning to strain the clam stock]

2307
01:38:37,332 --> 01:38:39,380
He's going to use the stock like that?

2308
01:38:39,380 --> 01:38:41,844
[Pot full of clams and stock]
You have to strain the broth well.

2309
01:38:41,844 --> 01:38:43,828
[Risky...]
Oh, the sand might...

2310
01:38:43,828 --> 01:38:46,500
- It might get in.
- Right.

2311
01:38:46,500 --> 01:38:48,305
[Pouring]

2312
01:38:49,252 --> 01:38:51,460
It feels like I'm the one cooking.

2313
01:38:51,460 --> 01:38:54,292
[He's in such a hurry...]

2314
01:38:55,188 --> 01:38:59,252
[Covering it with a stainless bowl]

2315
01:39:00,532 --> 01:39:01,668
[Pouring it out steadily again]

2316
01:39:01,668 --> 01:39:02,788
Anyway, I was in such a rush.

2317
01:39:02,788 --> 01:39:03,876
- Right, right.
- There's no time.

2318
01:39:03,876 --> 01:39:05,988
- We're out of time.
- It's 7:00.

2319
01:39:05,988 --> 01:39:08,870
- It has to be done within 30 minutes.
- You're right.

2320
01:39:14,228 --> 01:39:15,396
- It's an emergency.
- What?

2321
01:39:15,396 --> 01:39:16,564
Emergency, emergency!

2322
01:39:16,564 --> 01:39:18,436
- Did you throw them all in the trash?
- Yes.

2323
01:39:18,436 --> 01:39:20,607
- Really?
- Why?

2324
01:39:20,607 --> 01:39:22,924
In Italy, you should never throw food away.

2325
01:39:22,924 --> 01:39:24,308
But the thing is...

2326
01:39:24,308 --> 01:39:25,700
I had no choice. I didn't have time...

2327
01:39:25,700 --> 01:39:27,124
I'd have to shuck them all.

2328
01:39:27,124 --> 01:39:29,204
I'd have to shuck and then wash them.

2329
01:39:29,204 --> 01:39:31,588
[Less than 25 minutes until dinner]
So you only used the stock due to time?

2330
01:39:31,588 --> 01:39:34,478
[The kitchen staff waiting for dinner]
Everyone was waiting for it.

2331
01:39:34,478 --> 01:39:36,404
[Sam's decision]
Okay.

2332
01:39:36,404 --> 01:39:38,612
I'll only use the clam stock.

2333
01:39:38,612 --> 01:39:40,340
Okay!

2334
01:39:40,340 --> 01:39:41,698
Like a seafood stock.

2335
01:39:41,698 --> 01:39:45,012
But where did the clams go?

2336
01:39:45,012 --> 01:39:47,204
- Oh, no.
- I'll use the stock instead of the clams!

2337
01:39:47,204 --> 01:39:49,492
[Asking again]
- Then the clams? - Where are they?

2338
01:39:49,492 --> 01:39:50,756
- Where are the clams?
- Emergency, emergency!

2339
01:39:50,756 --> 01:39:51,892
I threw them away earlier.

2340
01:39:51,892 --> 01:39:53,716
- You threw them away? Why?
- Yes, yes.

2341
01:39:53,716 --> 01:39:56,137
Because there's...

2342
01:39:56,137 --> 01:39:57,588
- Because of the sand?
- Yes...

2343
01:39:57,588 --> 01:39:59,999
[Oh, dear...]
Ah, but why?

2344
01:39:59,999 --> 01:40:01,976
I wanted to do a good job.

2345
01:40:01,976 --> 01:40:03,908
Then what will you do without clams?

2346
01:40:03,908 --> 01:40:05,604
There won't be any clams,

2347
01:40:05,604 --> 01:40:08,516
[Clam stock]
but all the flavor will be in here.

2348
01:40:08,516 --> 01:40:10,388
But you still need something to chew on.

2349
01:40:10,388 --> 01:40:13,204
It'd be weird if you just ate the noodles.

2350
01:40:13,204 --> 01:40:15,668
[The pasta needs to be flavored
with just the clam broth...]

2351
01:40:15,668 --> 01:40:18,420
[Where did Sam go now?]

2352
01:40:18,420 --> 01:40:20,132
[Clatter, bang]
- What? - What's going on?

2353
01:40:20,132 --> 01:40:21,844
[Rattle]
- What's going on? It's chaos. - Huh?

2354
01:40:21,844 --> 01:40:24,324
[What on earth happened?]
- What? - It's a mess in here.

2355
01:40:24,324 --> 01:40:26,468
Did a rat get in here or something?

2356
01:40:26,468 --> 01:40:29,138
[Sam the mouse visits
the back kitchen again...]

2357
01:40:30,012 --> 01:40:31,344
Let's see.

2358
01:40:31,344 --> 01:40:33,780
[What he brought back with him]

2359
01:40:33,780 --> 01:40:36,177
[Breadcrumbs]

2360
01:40:36,177 --> 01:40:37,188
Breadcrumbs.

2361
01:40:37,188 --> 01:40:39,732
[Since the clams are gone]
There was nothing to give it a highlight.

2362
01:40:39,732 --> 01:40:44,158
[Clams and texture are missing]
That's a good choice to add some texture.

2363
01:40:44,158 --> 01:40:47,236
[Decides to add breadcrumbs for texture]
I'm using breadcrumbs instead.

2364
01:40:47,797 --> 01:40:50,528
[Breadcrumb topping]
It's a Southern Italian style.

2365
01:40:50,528 --> 01:40:52,372
You'll toast the breadcrumbs.

2366
01:40:52,372 --> 01:40:55,508
[Oh...]
It gives it a bit of texture.

2367
01:40:57,012 --> 01:40:58,500
[Until they turn golden brown]

2368
01:40:58,500 --> 01:41:01,428
[After toasting them thoroughly]

2369
01:41:01,428 --> 01:41:02,548
[Finally, the pasta goes in]

2370
01:41:02,548 --> 01:41:04,388
[One bag]
He must be feeling rushed.

2371
01:41:04,388 --> 01:41:06,048
[Two bags]

2372
01:41:06,048 --> 01:41:07,700
[Three bags, boiling 1.5kg in total]
That's a lot of pasta.

2373
01:41:07,700 --> 01:41:09,572
All of that.

2374
01:41:09,572 --> 01:41:12,308
[While the pasta noodles cook]

2375
01:41:12,308 --> 01:41:14,004
[Trying to clear his head...]

2376
01:41:14,004 --> 01:41:15,931
I think Chef Kwon is quite flustered.

2377
01:41:15,931 --> 01:41:17,308
- Exactly.
- Right now,

2378
01:41:17,308 --> 01:41:19,412
- He looks the most flustered so far.
- I was the most flustered in five days.

2379
01:41:19,412 --> 01:41:22,068
He looks the most flustered
he's been in five days.

2380
01:41:22,068 --> 01:41:23,844
[A rough road to the final mission]
I'm out of time.

2381
01:41:23,844 --> 01:41:26,708
- And out of ingredients.
- Exactly.

2382
01:41:26,708 --> 01:41:27,972
[Preparing the base to toss the pasta]

2383
01:41:27,972 --> 01:41:31,654
[Removing the garlic and chili peppers]

2384
01:41:32,548 --> 01:41:35,620
[Next is the clam broth]

2385
01:41:35,620 --> 01:41:39,648
[Adding clam broth to the garlic oil]

2386
01:41:39,648 --> 01:41:42,868
[Clam broth, peperoncino, and garlic]

2387
01:41:42,868 --> 01:41:45,796
[An umami-packed vongole pasta base]

2388
01:41:45,796 --> 01:41:49,332
I like cherry tomatoes in an oil base.

2389
01:41:49,332 --> 01:41:50,564
Oh, he added tomatoes.

2390
01:41:50,564 --> 01:41:51,684
Good job, good job.

2391
01:41:51,684 --> 01:41:54,068
- I didn't have many ingredients.
- There really aren't many.

2392
01:41:54,068 --> 01:41:56,260
There wasn't even any parsley.

2393
01:41:56,260 --> 01:42:00,228
[Adding the pasta noodles]

2394
01:42:01,060 --> 01:42:02,948
[Starting the mantecare from the left pan]
But you know,

2395
01:42:02,948 --> 01:42:05,492
Long pasta is the hardest for large groups.

2396
01:42:05,492 --> 01:42:07,412
That's so true.

2397
01:42:08,340 --> 01:42:11,748
[Starting the mantecare]

2398
01:42:11,748 --> 01:42:12,958
[Ctrl+C]

2399
01:42:12,958 --> 01:42:15,764
[Ctrl+V]

2400
01:42:17,940 --> 01:42:19,332
[Clam stock and pasta water]

2401
01:42:19,332 --> 01:42:21,284
[Vongole station set up]

2402
01:42:21,284 --> 01:42:23,316
[Poking it with a shallow spatula]
[Careful...]

2403
01:42:23,316 --> 01:42:26,212
[The owner assists today]
[Ladle ready]

2404
01:42:27,364 --> 01:42:30,724
[Refilling clam stock with the ladle
Laura gave him]

2405
01:42:30,724 --> 01:42:32,356
Actually, all the flavor of the clams
is in that stock.

2406
01:42:32,356 --> 01:42:34,223
That's true.

2407
01:42:38,500 --> 01:42:42,004
Oil-based pasta like vongole needs
a lot of starch

2408
01:42:42,004 --> 01:42:43,428
to have a rich texture.

2409
01:42:43,428 --> 01:42:46,548
It makes it coat the mouth better.

2410
01:42:47,684 --> 01:42:49,568
Now I'll emulsify it.

2411
01:42:49,568 --> 01:42:52,308
I'll extract as much starch as possible.

2412
01:42:52,308 --> 01:42:54,897
[That's right]

2413
01:42:56,468 --> 01:42:57,588
[Slurp]

2414
01:42:57,588 --> 01:43:00,996
[Tasting as he goes]
It's going to be delicious.

2415
01:43:00,996 --> 01:43:02,548
A look of intense focus.

2416
01:43:02,548 --> 01:43:04,676
[Adding pasta water this time]

2417
01:43:04,676 --> 01:43:07,156
- The clam flavor is too strong...
- Yes, exactly.

2418
01:43:07,156 --> 01:43:09,076
[Impressive...]
So he made a very rich clam stock

2419
01:43:09,076 --> 01:43:11,198
- and is mixing it with pasta water?
- Right, right.

2420
01:43:11,198 --> 01:43:14,516
[As the clam flavor and Sam's skill blend]
Keep tasting it.

2421
01:43:16,452 --> 01:43:19,780
[Curious Senior An appears]

2422
01:43:19,780 --> 01:43:21,700
[Grin]

2423
01:43:23,780 --> 01:43:26,078
- How's it going, Sam?
- Well, it's going well.

2424
01:43:26,078 --> 01:43:27,188
It's going well so far.

2425
01:43:27,188 --> 01:43:29,688
So far?

2426
01:43:29,688 --> 01:43:31,185
What's on the menu for tonight?

2427
01:43:31,185 --> 01:43:32,884
It's vongole pasta.

2428
01:43:32,884 --> 01:43:34,862
But it's one without clams.

2429
01:43:35,748 --> 01:43:37,028
Without clams?

2430
01:43:37,028 --> 01:43:38,820
A pasta where the clams are missing.

2431
01:43:38,820 --> 01:43:41,796
We call this kind of pasta
"runaway clam pasta."

2432
01:43:41,796 --> 01:43:43,988
[Runaway: fujute]
"Runaway?"

2433
01:43:43,988 --> 01:43:45,844
Oh, really?

2434
01:43:45,844 --> 01:43:48,292
It smells like clams...

2435
01:43:48,292 --> 01:43:50,244
- but there aren't any clams in it!
- Yes, exactly.

2436
01:43:50,244 --> 01:43:53,284
[Vongole pasta without vongole!]
It's a real dish.

2437
01:43:53,284 --> 01:43:54,932
This is how it's made.

2438
01:43:54,932 --> 01:43:56,564
They take stones from the sea...

2439
01:43:56,564 --> 01:43:58,996
and there's a pasta flavored with those stones.

2440
01:43:58,996 --> 01:44:01,524
Since the stones are infused with sea flavor,

2441
01:44:01,524 --> 01:44:02,724
they boil the stones together.

2442
01:44:02,724 --> 01:44:04,692
That's how they get the flavor.

2443
01:44:04,692 --> 01:44:06,436
[Spaghetti alle vongole fujute: Traditional Naples
dish that is sea-flavored pasta without clams]

2444
01:44:06,436 --> 01:44:08,324
That poor...

2445
01:44:08,324 --> 01:44:09,748
- Since it has that history...
- Right.

2446
01:44:09,748 --> 01:44:12,468
Historically, they had no choice.

2447
01:44:13,348 --> 01:44:15,588
[Losing the clams by accident,
Sam's pasta ends up being authentic]

2448
01:44:15,588 --> 01:44:16,644
Oh, really?

2449
01:44:16,644 --> 01:44:19,476
Naples is full of surprises.

2450
01:44:19,476 --> 01:44:22,228
[After many twists and turns,
it's finally coming together]

2451
01:44:22,228 --> 01:44:24,260
Can I try some?

2452
01:44:24,260 --> 01:44:28,084
[How will vongole pasta taste without clams?]
This is the moment of truth.

2453
01:44:28,084 --> 01:44:30,900
- How is it?
- I think he'll like it.

2454
01:44:30,900 --> 01:44:32,164
You added something spicy again?

2455
01:44:32,164 --> 01:44:34,644
[Busted...]
[Sorry, Senior An]

2456
01:44:34,644 --> 01:44:36,564
Antonio really can't handle spicy food.

2457
01:44:36,564 --> 01:44:37,828
Senior An is a bit...

2458
01:44:37,828 --> 01:44:39,572
- He can't eat spicy food.
- Oh, he can't eat it.

2459
01:44:39,572 --> 01:44:41,188
It's not that spicy...

2460
01:44:41,188 --> 01:44:42,452
I only added peperoncino oil.

2461
01:44:42,452 --> 01:44:43,748
"Only?"

2462
01:44:43,748 --> 01:44:45,988
What else is there to add?

2463
01:44:45,988 --> 01:44:47,620
- The peperoncino must have been spicy.
- That's right.

2464
01:44:47,620 --> 01:44:49,156
The oil was spicier than I thought.

2465
01:44:49,156 --> 01:44:50,948
I didn't realize it, but it was quite spicy.

2466
01:44:50,948 --> 01:44:53,524
Do you want to plate it and I'll finish?
You decide.

2467
01:44:53,524 --> 01:44:54,685
Senior An, you plate it.

2468
01:44:54,685 --> 01:44:55,620
I'll do this.

2469
01:44:55,620 --> 01:44:57,700
Should we also serve this?

2470
01:44:57,700 --> 01:44:59,300
And Laura, you do the lemon.

2471
01:44:59,300 --> 01:45:01,716
[Following Sam's division of labor]
A little lemon zest here.

2472
01:45:01,716 --> 01:45:04,188
[Senior An plates the pasta]
The finishing touch.

2473
01:45:04,188 --> 01:45:05,998
[Sam adds breadcrumbs]

2474
01:45:05,998 --> 01:45:08,638
[Lastly, Laura grates the lemon]

2475
01:45:08,638 --> 01:45:10,916
[Finally complete]

2476
01:45:10,916 --> 01:45:12,588
[Sam's final mission: Lemon Vongole Pasta]

2477
01:45:12,588 --> 01:45:14,244
Oh, it's beautiful.

2478
01:45:14,244 --> 01:45:15,540
Using breadcrumbs like that...

2479
01:45:15,540 --> 01:45:17,833
The breadcrumbs add a nice touch.

2480
01:45:18,793 --> 01:45:20,336
It looks delicious.

2481
01:45:20,336 --> 01:45:23,228
[How will Sam's lemon vongole pasta
be received?]

2482
01:45:23,228 --> 01:45:26,644
- It actually feels more like authentic Naples.
- Exactly.

2483
01:45:26,644 --> 01:45:27,796
[Clams X, Breadcrumbs O]
There are no clams.

2484
01:45:27,796 --> 01:45:29,076
- I used breadcrumbs.
- It looks intentional.

2485
01:45:29,076 --> 01:45:31,263
- A more classic version was created.
- So, you see...

2486
01:45:31,263 --> 01:45:33,748
You shouldn't say it was intentional.

2487
01:45:33,748 --> 01:45:35,044
[All eyes on him]
Now...

2488
01:45:35,044 --> 01:45:36,948
- Intentional...
- Right, that...

2489
01:45:36,948 --> 01:45:39,460
It wasn't intentional.

2490
01:45:39,460 --> 01:45:40,548
- That...
- But...

2491
01:45:40,548 --> 01:45:43,140
Because good ideas
sometimes come from failures.

2492
01:45:43,140 --> 01:45:44,420
Oh, this...

2493
01:45:44,420 --> 01:45:47,708
[Will it be accepted for its authenticity?]
Wait, is he actually going to pull this off?

2494
01:45:47,708 --> 01:45:50,516
[Sam's vongole pasta is served to the table]

2495
01:45:50,516 --> 01:45:51,764
Oh, wow.

2496
01:45:51,764 --> 01:45:53,652
[The owners enter with high expectations]

2497
01:45:53,652 --> 01:45:56,980
It smells wonderful.

2498
01:45:56,980 --> 01:45:58,420
Shall we go?

2499
01:45:58,420 --> 01:46:00,388
I'm so curious to see their reaction.

2500
01:46:00,388 --> 01:46:02,788
Kwon!

2501
01:46:02,788 --> 01:46:05,060
Thank you.

2502
01:46:05,060 --> 01:46:07,228
Hey, Kwon!

2503
01:46:07,228 --> 01:46:10,468
Can you explain the dish to us?

2504
01:46:10,468 --> 01:46:12,811
[Hehe]
[Full of mischief]

2505
01:46:12,811 --> 01:46:14,308
It's a vongole pasta.

2506
01:46:14,308 --> 01:46:16,238
The clams ran away.

2507
01:46:16,238 --> 01:46:18,468
They ran away!

2508
01:46:18,468 --> 01:46:20,388
[They ran away]
Fujute.

2509
01:46:20,388 --> 01:46:24,148
[Server]
Francesco also prepared a very nice wine!

2510
01:46:24,148 --> 01:46:25,604
A glass of sparkling wine, too.

2511
01:46:25,604 --> 01:46:27,588
- It goes well with it.
- Since it's my last day.

2512
01:46:27,588 --> 01:46:28,724
Since it's your last day.

2513
01:46:28,724 --> 01:46:30,788
To Kwon!

2514
01:46:30,788 --> 01:46:31,972
[A virtual toast]

2515
01:46:31,972 --> 01:46:33,108
Cheers!

2516
01:46:33,108 --> 01:46:34,404
No.

2517
01:46:34,404 --> 01:46:35,744
Why?

2518
01:46:35,744 --> 01:46:37,194
- Cheers!
- No.

2519
01:46:37,194 --> 01:46:38,778
[Did I do something wrong?]
Why?

2520
01:46:38,778 --> 01:46:43,338
No, I want to give you a round of applause.
You've done so well!

2521
01:46:43,338 --> 01:46:46,442
[Bravo, Kwon]
Thank you.

2522
01:46:46,442 --> 01:46:48,826
[A surprise round of applause]
You did a great job.

2523
01:46:48,826 --> 01:46:51,466
[Touched]
I did well, but...

2524
01:46:51,466 --> 01:46:53,706
[Shy]
Thank you.

2525
01:46:54,612 --> 01:46:57,112
[Cute]

2526
01:46:57,112 --> 01:46:59,306
[Finally, time for the tasting]
Oh, I'm so curious.

2527
01:46:59,306 --> 01:47:00,874
Oh, please.

2528
01:47:00,874 --> 01:47:05,738
[To be added to the menu,
it must taste good first!]

2529
01:47:05,738 --> 01:47:07,434
- Please.
- Everyone, don't be so nervous.

2530
01:47:07,434 --> 01:47:08,746
[Restless]

2531
01:47:08,746 --> 01:47:10,938
Just relax and watch.

2532
01:47:10,938 --> 01:47:13,002
It'll be delicious, though.

2533
01:47:13,002 --> 01:47:14,922
[Eyes wide open]

2534
01:47:14,922 --> 01:47:17,578
[Hmm...]

2535
01:47:18,298 --> 01:47:20,506
[How will Kwon's lemon vongole pasta taste?]

2536
01:47:20,506 --> 01:47:22,425
Let's see.

2537
01:47:22,425 --> 01:47:24,600
I was a bit nervous about the vongole pasta.

2538
01:47:24,600 --> 01:47:25,706
For the first time.

2539
01:47:25,706 --> 01:47:27,578
Because I wasn't quite satisfied with it.

2540
01:47:27,578 --> 01:47:29,898
Personally...

2541
01:47:29,898 --> 01:47:31,482
[Sniffing the aroma out of worry]

2542
01:47:31,482 --> 01:47:33,066
What if they all say it's delicious?

2543
01:47:33,066 --> 01:47:35,242
- Exactly.
- Let's see.

2544
01:47:37,738 --> 01:47:42,698
[Owner Giacomo takes a big bite]

2545
01:47:43,738 --> 01:47:45,306
Wait, this is delicious!

2546
01:47:45,306 --> 01:47:46,506
He said it's great. It's great.

2547
01:47:46,506 --> 01:47:48,362
He says it's delicious.

2548
01:47:48,362 --> 01:47:51,050
- It's good.
- It's good.

2549
01:47:51,050 --> 01:47:53,172
Doesn't everyone like it?

2550
01:47:53,978 --> 01:47:57,498
[I wonder how the others will like it...]

2551
01:47:57,498 --> 01:48:00,058
[Guido, the top gourmet, also tastes it carefully]
Guido is scary.

2552
01:48:00,058 --> 01:48:02,257
He's very strict.

2553
01:48:03,501 --> 01:48:04,666
Whoa.

2554
01:48:04,666 --> 01:48:06,234
[Kwon is startled]

2555
01:48:06,234 --> 01:48:08,212
- It's delicious.
- He shouted.

2556
01:48:09,097 --> 01:48:10,154
Whoa!

2557
01:48:10,154 --> 01:48:12,810
I can taste the clams.

2558
01:48:12,810 --> 01:48:16,482
- You should.
- Because he used clams.

2559
01:48:16,482 --> 01:48:20,490
[Only their flavor behind...]
Do you know how many clams went in here?

2560
01:48:20,490 --> 01:48:23,306
You can really taste them
even without the meat.

2561
01:48:23,306 --> 01:48:25,786
Even though it's made this way, it's great.

2562
01:48:25,786 --> 01:48:27,930
[It's a compliment]
Good job.

2563
01:48:28,831 --> 01:48:31,633
Even though there were no clams in the dish,

2564
01:48:31,633 --> 01:48:36,982
Kwon's improvisation was impressive.

2565
01:48:36,982 --> 01:48:38,714
Especially the breadcrumbs.

2566
01:48:38,714 --> 01:48:42,458
They gave it a nice, crispy texture.

2567
01:48:42,458 --> 01:48:45,765
And the lemon zest added a nice freshness.

2568
01:48:45,765 --> 01:48:47,386
- It was delicious.
- It was delicious.

2569
01:48:47,386 --> 01:48:49,386
[Unanimous praise]

2570
01:48:49,386 --> 01:48:50,890
It's really delicious.

2571
01:48:50,890 --> 01:48:53,146
[Hmph]
He did put some spicy stuff in it, though!

2572
01:48:53,146 --> 01:48:56,282
- Senior An is not a fan of the spice.
- For someone who doesn't like spice...

2573
01:48:56,282 --> 01:48:57,706
It was a bit too spicy.

2574
01:48:57,706 --> 01:48:59,450
It's spicy.

2575
01:48:59,450 --> 01:49:01,258
It is spicier than I expected.

2576
01:49:01,258 --> 01:49:04,922
[Victims of the spice appearing everywhere]
It was a little spicy.

2577
01:49:04,922 --> 01:49:07,754
[Tense again]
- Was it a bit spicy? - It was spicy.

2578
01:49:08,746 --> 01:49:11,210
I think we could tone down the spice a bit.

2579
01:49:11,210 --> 01:49:13,610
Because of the lemon.

2580
01:49:13,610 --> 01:49:14,794
Right.

2581
01:49:14,794 --> 01:49:17,546
Lemon actually enhances the spiciness.

2582
01:49:17,546 --> 01:49:18,762
The heat, right?

2583
01:49:18,762 --> 01:49:22,170
When you add acidity,
it's stimulus on top of stimulus.

2584
01:49:22,170 --> 01:49:24,298
It makes you feel the heat even more.

2585
01:49:24,298 --> 01:49:29,552
And the spice can throw off the flavor balance.

2586
01:49:29,552 --> 01:49:31,220
I hadn't used that one before.

2587
01:49:31,220 --> 01:49:33,322
[Was the peperoncino oil too much?]

2588
01:49:33,322 --> 01:49:37,082
But the way the pasta was cooked was perfect!

2589
01:49:37,082 --> 01:49:41,850
Aside from the spiciness, this dish
is a 110, not just a 100.

2590
01:49:41,850 --> 01:49:43,626
110 points, except for the spice.

2591
01:49:43,626 --> 01:49:46,342
[Clap]
- What a compliment. - It's really good.

2592
01:49:46,342 --> 01:49:47,770
[Confidence restored]

2593
01:49:47,770 --> 01:49:49,418
I think so too.

2594
01:49:49,418 --> 01:49:51,098
[Clean plate]

2595
01:49:51,098 --> 01:49:52,722
Oh, wow.

2596
01:49:52,722 --> 01:49:55,098
[At this rate, the new menu might be possible]

2597
01:49:55,098 --> 01:49:56,452
Good job!

2598
01:49:56,452 --> 01:49:59,142
[Despite the ups and downs,
the meal ends with a compliment]

2599
01:49:59,142 --> 01:50:02,426
[Easy]
Bravo!

2600
01:50:02,426 --> 01:50:04,234
[Now for Sam's final mission...]
Okay.

2601
01:50:04,234 --> 01:50:05,578
I wonder.

2602
01:50:05,578 --> 01:50:08,586
[Only the request to list the new menu remains]
I wonder if he'll be able to ask.

2603
01:50:09,592 --> 01:50:13,258
[While everyone is laughing and chatting]

2604
01:50:13,258 --> 01:50:14,932
[Alone and serious...]

2605
01:50:14,932 --> 01:50:17,412
I know that feeling.

2606
01:50:17,412 --> 01:50:21,412
[Sam's "what should I do" look]

2607
01:50:21,412 --> 01:50:23,546
[But he can't put it off any longer]

2608
01:50:23,546 --> 01:50:26,010
If it's possible...

2609
01:50:26,010 --> 01:50:28,522
Later, after this program airs...

2610
01:50:28,522 --> 01:50:31,222
Wait, I didn't hear you. Everyone, quiet!

2611
01:50:32,234 --> 01:50:34,562
[Shush...]
- Why make everyone focus? - Sudden focus.

2612
01:50:34,562 --> 01:50:35,834
- Why make everyone focus?
- Why?

2613
01:50:35,834 --> 01:50:37,994
[Shh! Focus on Sam!]
This is too much pressure.

2614
01:50:37,994 --> 01:50:40,234
Why make it so everyone can hear?
I was going to tell you privately.

2615
01:50:40,234 --> 01:50:44,162
[What is he going to say?]
Everyone's listening now.

2616
01:50:44,162 --> 01:50:45,386
[Listening intently]

2617
01:50:45,386 --> 01:50:48,922
[After it airs...]
- Look at their faces. - He must be so nervous.

2618
01:50:48,922 --> 01:50:50,394
If possible,

2619
01:50:50,394 --> 01:50:53,546
on the menu, could you list it?

2620
01:50:53,546 --> 01:50:55,555
My menu.

2621
01:50:55,555 --> 01:50:57,223
- So bold.
- He's confident.

2622
01:50:57,223 --> 01:51:00,426
- Isn't that an order?
- Hold on.

2623
01:51:00,426 --> 01:51:01,658
Hold on.

2624
01:51:01,658 --> 01:51:02,735
[Unbelievable]
Hold on.

2625
01:51:02,735 --> 01:51:03,928
- This is...
- Hold on, so...

2626
01:51:03,928 --> 01:51:05,770
- No, no.
- The translation...

2627
01:51:05,770 --> 01:51:07,930
- Was the translation too literal?
- No, it's not that.

2628
01:51:07,930 --> 01:51:10,148
- I'm sure he meant it more politely.
- No.

2629
01:51:10,148 --> 01:51:11,821
That's exactly what I intended.

2630
01:51:11,821 --> 01:51:13,274
That's exactly what I meant.

2631
01:51:13,274 --> 01:51:14,970
You have to just go for it.

2632
01:51:14,970 --> 01:51:18,218
Introverts like us would've fainted by now.

2633
01:51:18,218 --> 01:51:20,762
Fainted?

2634
01:51:20,762 --> 01:51:22,290
If possible,

2635
01:51:22,290 --> 01:51:25,818
could you add it to the menu?

2636
01:51:25,818 --> 01:51:27,363
My dish, that is.

2637
01:51:28,538 --> 01:51:31,210
[Kwon's pasta]

2638
01:51:31,210 --> 01:51:33,722
[Onto the menu?]
Let's be bold, everyone.

2639
01:51:33,722 --> 01:51:37,274
Ah, Kwon's dish?

2640
01:51:37,274 --> 01:51:38,554
Since Korean guests might come in?

2641
01:51:38,554 --> 01:51:40,106
Okay! Great idea!

2642
01:51:40,106 --> 01:51:41,762
Huh?

2643
01:51:41,762 --> 01:51:44,426
[Really?]
- It's vongole pasta. - Yes.

2644
01:51:44,426 --> 01:51:46,482
Just tone down the spice a bit!

2645
01:51:46,482 --> 01:51:49,562
[Fair enough]
Exactly.

2646
01:51:49,562 --> 01:51:51,194
[You know, right?]

2647
01:51:51,194 --> 01:51:52,243
[I know]

2648
01:51:52,243 --> 01:51:53,370
- What, why like this?
- What?

2649
01:51:53,370 --> 01:51:55,306
[What's with this suddenly natural success vibe?]
What's with this vibe?

2650
01:51:55,306 --> 01:51:57,732
- This isn't what I meant, though.
- Totally.

2651
01:51:57,732 --> 01:52:00,090
- We've got to be bold, everyone.
- Wow, impressive.

2652
01:52:00,090 --> 01:52:01,754
- What is this?
- I'm just going for it.

2653
01:52:01,754 --> 01:52:04,394
[Did it actually work?]
- Really? - You actually put it in?

2654
01:52:04,394 --> 01:52:06,552
- Seriously?
- Wow, this is just too much.

2655
01:52:06,552 --> 01:52:09,322
[Feeling triumphant]
I'd call that a success, right?

2656
01:52:09,322 --> 01:52:11,738
My dish is definitely getting on the menu.

2657
01:52:11,738 --> 01:52:13,546
I gave them the idea, after all,

2658
01:52:13,546 --> 01:52:15,968
based on the vongole pasta I made,

2659
01:52:15,968 --> 01:52:17,658
with a bit of their own spin added!

2660
01:52:17,658 --> 01:52:20,538
Maybe it'll make it onto the menu!

2661
01:52:20,538 --> 01:52:23,476
It'd be fun if it went up
as "Sam's Spaghetti" or something.

2662
01:52:23,476 --> 01:52:25,645
Something like "Sam's Spaghetti."

2663
01:52:25,645 --> 01:52:27,002
Hang on.

2664
01:52:27,002 --> 01:52:28,330
[Haha!]

2665
01:52:28,330 --> 01:52:31,306
[As Kwon savors his final mission success?]

2666
01:52:31,306 --> 01:52:35,818
[Kwon's sudden proposal leaves Boss Laura torn]

2667
01:52:35,818 --> 01:52:38,831
I think Kwon did well.

2668
01:52:38,831 --> 01:52:40,848
He handled it calmly.

2669
01:52:42,026 --> 01:52:45,738
After boiling the clams and tasting them,

2670
01:52:45,738 --> 01:52:47,530
throwing it out was the right call.

2671
01:52:47,530 --> 01:52:49,002
Either way,

2672
01:52:49,002 --> 01:52:52,202
- he improvised well, that's the point.
- If he'd used it as is, the dish could've been ruined.

2673
01:52:52,202 --> 01:52:54,842
Even though it wasn't a dish he was used to,

2674
01:52:54,842 --> 01:52:59,258
the execution was perfect.

2675
01:52:59,258 --> 01:53:01,194
[So what happens to Kwon's plan
to launch his vongole pasta?]

2676
01:53:01,194 --> 01:53:04,570
Okay, this really is the final mission.

2677
01:53:05,754 --> 01:53:07,178
It's a no.

2678
01:53:07,178 --> 01:53:09,162
"No."

2679
01:53:09,162 --> 01:53:10,538
[Firm]

2680
01:53:10,538 --> 01:53:12,202
Miss.

2681
01:53:12,890 --> 01:53:14,506
What, just like that?

2682
01:53:14,506 --> 01:53:15,674
[Fail!]
What?

2683
01:53:15,674 --> 01:53:18,810
[If it's gonna end like this, why act so cocky?]
Seriously, acting like such hot stuff...

2684
01:53:18,810 --> 01:53:20,666
[Betrayed]
I mean, I actually, I really thought

2685
01:53:20,666 --> 01:53:23,402
- it was going to work.
- I figured it'd obviously work too.

2686
01:53:23,402 --> 01:53:25,812
[No way]
I thought it'd work, I really did.

2687
01:53:25,812 --> 01:53:27,386
Failing with confidence,

2688
01:53:27,386 --> 01:53:29,306
even I wouldn't put it out.

2689
01:53:29,306 --> 01:53:32,570
- Exactly.
- What do you mean?

2690
01:53:32,570 --> 01:53:34,282
No!

2691
01:53:34,282 --> 01:53:35,418
[That's a tough one...]

2692
01:53:35,418 --> 01:53:37,002
But there's a reason.

2693
01:53:37,002 --> 01:53:39,258
There's a reason.

2694
01:53:39,258 --> 01:53:43,018
It's not that his dish didn't taste good

2695
01:53:43,018 --> 01:53:46,274
it's that the dish just
doesn't show who we are.

2696
01:53:46,274 --> 01:53:48,058
- Right.
- That's really important.

2697
01:53:48,058 --> 01:53:49,242
- Exactly.
- You need to have that.

2698
01:53:49,242 --> 01:53:50,890
- The recipe matters.
- Tone and manner.

2699
01:53:50,890 --> 01:53:52,890
It's a dish with none of our identity in it.

2700
01:53:52,890 --> 01:53:55,802
If I'd made it, I would've done it differently.

2701
01:53:55,802 --> 01:53:58,362
- Just clams alone.
- Right.

2702
01:53:58,362 --> 01:54:00,250
Or just vegetables alone.

2703
01:54:00,250 --> 01:54:02,202
The lemon scent was nice, I think.

2704
01:54:02,202 --> 01:54:04,730
Yeah, the lemon scent was good.

2705
01:54:04,730 --> 01:54:07,226
I liked that idea,

2706
01:54:07,226 --> 01:54:10,554
so I'll definitely use it next time.

2707
01:54:10,554 --> 01:54:11,946
But

2708
01:54:11,946 --> 01:54:13,530
we won't be putting Kwon's pasta on the menu.

2709
01:54:13,530 --> 01:54:16,506
[Even Kwon agrees]
Not in that state, no.

2710
01:54:17,258 --> 01:54:19,114
I'm not even mad.

2711
01:54:19,114 --> 01:54:22,538
[Napoli Kwon, final mission: failed.
Reason: lack of Napoli spirit]

2712
01:54:22,538 --> 01:54:24,266
In bright red letters, no less.

2713
01:54:24,266 --> 01:54:26,807
Reason: lack of Napoli spirit.

2714
01:54:26,807 --> 01:54:29,002
I was lacking.

2715
01:54:29,002 --> 01:54:30,970
Good thing we all three failed.

2716
01:54:30,970 --> 01:54:33,034
But...

2717
01:54:33,034 --> 01:54:34,186
[All failed]

2718
01:54:34,186 --> 01:54:36,074
Oh, thank goodness.

2719
01:54:36,074 --> 01:54:39,114
- I thought I was the only one who failed.
- Seriously.

2720
01:54:39,114 --> 01:54:42,042
He showed his off at the end,
so I thought he'd succeeded.

2721
01:54:42,042 --> 01:54:43,754
Wow, seriously.

2722
01:54:43,754 --> 01:54:46,426
There's a bit of satisfaction in it, too.

2723
01:54:46,426 --> 01:54:49,130
Catharsis, right there.

2724
01:54:49,130 --> 01:54:51,242
Catharsis from my own failure.

2725
01:54:51,242 --> 01:54:52,986
Laughing at him, this is fun.

2726
01:54:54,335 --> 01:54:58,099
[So what's left now is...]

2727
01:54:58,730 --> 01:55:00,466
Time to reveal his identity.

2728
01:55:00,466 --> 01:55:02,378
Right, this is really the last one now.

2729
01:55:02,378 --> 01:55:04,490
Get ready to be surprised.

2730
01:55:05,402 --> 01:55:07,930
The most important thing
is that it's the last day,

2731
01:55:07,930 --> 01:55:10,346
but it's also the day
I have to reveal who I am.

2732
01:55:10,346 --> 01:55:12,026
I've been watching for that moment

2733
01:55:12,026 --> 01:55:14,938
[Glancing]
this whole time.

2734
01:55:14,938 --> 01:55:15,974
[Nervous]

2735
01:55:15,974 --> 01:55:19,178
Okay, is he going to bring it up now?

2736
01:55:19,178 --> 01:55:20,849
Now is the time.

2737
01:55:21,658 --> 01:55:23,498
Sam, it's now.

2738
01:55:23,498 --> 01:55:26,442
[Hmm...]

2739
01:55:26,442 --> 01:55:27,658
[Paolo notices Kwon acting like that]

2740
01:55:27,658 --> 01:55:30,217
As expected, Paolo's so perceptive.

2741
01:55:31,466 --> 01:55:33,682
Wait, seems like Kwon
has something he wants to say.

2742
01:55:33,682 --> 01:55:34,842
I knew it.

2743
01:55:34,842 --> 01:55:37,672
[What does he want to say?]
So perceptive.

2744
01:55:37,672 --> 01:55:39,866
Cut, cut!

2745
01:55:39,866 --> 01:55:43,466
[Um, well...]
Cut, cut!

2746
01:55:43,466 --> 01:55:46,519
My name isn't Sam Kwon.

2747
01:55:46,519 --> 01:55:48,554
It's not Sam Kwon.

2748
01:55:48,554 --> 01:55:51,498
Oh, like this.

2749
01:55:52,226 --> 01:55:55,242
[He's not Sam Kwon?]

2750
01:55:55,242 --> 01:55:57,138
Then...

2751
01:55:58,122 --> 01:55:59,898
[Then what's your real name?]
Okay, so what is it?

2752
01:55:59,898 --> 01:56:02,291
[Puzzled]
Your name is...

2753
01:56:04,202 --> 01:56:07,658
- All right! Let's look me up on Instagram.
- Okay, like this.

2754
01:56:07,658 --> 01:56:10,953
- MZ-style! The Gen Z way.
- Just who are you?

2755
01:56:10,953 --> 01:56:12,554
So, my name is...

2756
01:56:12,554 --> 01:56:14,346
So, my name is...

2757
01:56:14,346 --> 01:56:16,874
[Curious]

2758
01:56:16,874 --> 01:56:19,338
"Napoli Matfia?"

2759
01:56:19,338 --> 01:56:21,179
"Matfia."

2760
01:56:21,179 --> 01:56:23,002
"Napoli... Mah-tfia."

2761
01:56:23,002 --> 01:56:26,262
[They start looking through Kwon's Instagram]
"Mat" means "taste" in Korean.

2762
01:56:26,262 --> 01:56:27,642
[Napoli Matfia, 496K followers]
It's a lot.

2763
01:56:27,642 --> 01:56:30,970
[Owner Chef]
- You're already a chef? - Yeah.

2764
01:56:30,970 --> 01:56:32,138
[Ohh]

2765
01:56:32,138 --> 01:56:34,162
[Kwon... you were a chef?]
Senior Pa.

2766
01:56:34,162 --> 01:56:38,722
I already run a restaurant in Seoul.

2767
01:56:38,722 --> 01:56:40,548
[Whoa]

2768
01:56:42,458 --> 01:56:45,354
And I worked here in Naples too.

2769
01:56:45,354 --> 01:56:48,106
With Nino Di Costanzo, six or seven years ago.

2770
01:56:48,106 --> 01:56:50,932
Ah, so that's it.

2771
01:56:50,932 --> 01:56:54,932
[See episode 4]
So that's what he meant back then!

2772
01:56:54,932 --> 01:56:58,554
What kind of restaurant is it?

2773
01:56:58,554 --> 01:57:02,472
It's an Italian fine dining restaurant.

2774
01:57:02,472 --> 01:57:05,834
- Is it Kwon's own restaurant?
- Yes.

2775
01:57:05,834 --> 01:57:08,250
Then he's an owner chef!

2776
01:57:08,250 --> 01:57:09,752
An owner chef.

2777
01:57:09,752 --> 01:57:11,622
[Oh...]
Wait, right now Antonio...

2778
01:57:11,622 --> 01:57:13,610
- Antonio's face looks pretty rough.
- He's a little shocked right now.

2779
01:57:13,610 --> 01:57:17,306
[Antonio can't look away from
Kwon's Instagram...]

2780
01:57:17,306 --> 01:57:20,394
[Meanwhile]

2781
01:57:21,272 --> 01:57:26,122
[Paolo scrutinizes Kwon's Instagram]
There are a lot of famous people on my page.

2782
01:57:26,122 --> 01:57:28,154
[3-star Michelin]
He's even following Fabrizio Mellino.

2783
01:57:28,154 --> 01:57:30,810
The best chef in Naples, Fabrizio Mellino.

2784
01:57:30,810 --> 01:57:33,242
There are soccer players in there too.

2785
01:57:33,242 --> 01:57:35,258
[Global soccer star]
- Beckham. - Beckham's there too.

2786
01:57:35,258 --> 01:57:37,066
[Italian legendary goalkeeper, Buffon?]
Buffon.

2787
01:57:37,066 --> 01:57:39,202
[Nesta, Buffon, Marchisio: Italian soccer legends]
Bragging about soccer players.

2788
01:57:39,202 --> 01:57:41,002
[Cannavaro, Pirlo, Bonucci, Del Piero]
- Buffon. - Along with Buffon.

2789
01:57:41,002 --> 01:57:44,186
Cannavaro is from Naples.

2790
01:57:44,186 --> 01:57:46,774
[Tennis emperor Roger Federer]
Federer.

2791
01:57:46,774 --> 01:57:48,186
[Nino Di Costanzo, Pierre Gagnaire, Gordon Ramsay]

2792
01:57:48,186 --> 01:57:49,594
- Hanging out with celebs.
- Gordon Ramsay.

2793
01:57:49,594 --> 01:57:52,312
[Famous Michelin chefs]
Pierre Gagnaire.

2794
01:57:54,042 --> 01:57:56,826
[Kwon's got insane clout]

2795
01:57:56,826 --> 01:58:00,650
[At the time of filming]
Followed by 492,000 people.

2796
01:58:00,650 --> 01:58:03,962
- So he's a famous chef in Korea.
- Right.

2797
01:58:03,962 --> 01:58:05,066
That's exactly me.

2798
01:58:05,066 --> 01:58:08,874
[That's exactly me]
Yes, yes.

2799
01:58:08,874 --> 01:58:12,422
I should get back to the kitchen now.

2800
01:58:12,422 --> 01:58:16,287
[Antonio makes his escape]
Antonio's making a run for it.

2801
01:58:16,287 --> 01:58:18,154
No, no, Kwon, stay seated.

2802
01:58:18,154 --> 01:58:20,282
Stay seated.

2803
01:58:20,282 --> 01:58:21,690
Just kidding, get up.

2804
01:58:21,690 --> 01:58:24,714
Now how are they all
even supposed to treat him?

2805
01:58:25,914 --> 01:58:29,850
[After the meal, staff gather in the kitchen]
Let's work, now.

2806
01:58:29,850 --> 01:58:31,018
There's something over there?

2807
01:58:31,018 --> 01:58:33,738
It's not over yet.

2808
01:58:33,738 --> 01:58:36,426
[A mysterious video begins to play]
Who's that?

2809
01:58:36,426 --> 01:58:38,234
So they're showing it with that.

2810
01:58:38,234 --> 01:58:40,058
There's something.

2811
01:58:41,732 --> 01:58:42,682
Who's that?

2812
01:58:42,682 --> 01:58:44,986
That's me.

2813
01:58:44,986 --> 01:58:47,930
It's a Korean show I was on.

2814
01:58:47,930 --> 01:58:50,879
[His true identity, revealed on TV]

2815
01:58:50,879 --> 01:58:53,198
I won this one, everyone.

2816
01:58:53,198 --> 01:58:55,130
[Winner who beat 100 chefs:
Culinary Class Wars]

2817
01:58:55,130 --> 01:58:56,666
[Whoaaa]

2818
01:58:56,666 --> 01:58:58,058
You won a survival show.

2819
01:58:58,058 --> 01:59:00,442
- Beating 100 people!
- That's really me right there.

2820
01:59:00,442 --> 01:59:02,778
That's really me right there.

2821
01:59:02,778 --> 01:59:04,982
[Well done!]

2822
01:59:04,982 --> 01:59:07,755
[Ugh, embarrassing]
It was so embarrassing, though.

2823
01:59:07,755 --> 01:59:09,098
What is it?

2824
01:59:09,098 --> 01:59:11,127
It's a show.

2825
01:59:12,217 --> 01:59:14,298
[End of video]
Aw, it ended? Right at the important part.

2826
01:59:14,298 --> 01:59:16,490
- Replay, replay.
- Again, again!

2827
01:59:16,490 --> 01:59:18,378
Play it again!

2828
01:59:18,378 --> 01:59:20,612
- I wasn't here for it!
- One more time!

2829
01:59:20,612 --> 01:59:22,346
One more time! One more time!

2830
01:59:22,346 --> 01:59:24,794
"One more time."

2831
01:59:24,794 --> 01:59:27,210
[Video replay]
Okay, I replayed it.

2832
01:59:27,210 --> 01:59:30,074
- So the truth is...
- Look at Kwon Sung Jun's face.

2833
01:59:30,074 --> 01:59:31,322
So embarrassing.

2834
01:59:31,322 --> 01:59:34,762
"Culinary Class Wars" winner?

2835
01:59:34,762 --> 01:59:37,482
On Netflix? That's amazing.

2836
01:59:37,482 --> 01:59:39,946
[Amid the cheerful mood,
Antonio just can't bring himself to smile...]

2837
01:59:39,946 --> 01:59:41,194
- Antonio...
- He isn't laughing.

2838
01:59:41,194 --> 01:59:44,010
I wonder how he's feeling right now.

2839
01:59:44,010 --> 01:59:45,994
That's our goalkeeper right there.

2840
01:59:45,994 --> 01:59:48,102
That's the legendary keeper Cannavaro.

2841
01:59:48,102 --> 01:59:49,706
[Chef Kwon, who once cooked for Italian soccer legends]
They're legends.

2842
01:59:49,706 --> 01:59:53,482
[Buffon, Nesta, Marchisio]
And all those soccer players came to eat there too.

2843
01:59:53,482 --> 01:59:55,898
For Italian soccer legends

2844
01:59:55,898 --> 01:59:58,322
[Mumbling...]
the chef who cooked for them.

2845
01:59:59,882 --> 02:00:02,186
[Oh... uh...]
[Gulp]

2846
02:00:02,186 --> 02:00:04,445
Kwohn Soon Joon.

2847
02:00:05,274 --> 02:00:09,418
[He's way more impressive than I thought?]

2848
02:00:10,314 --> 02:00:13,274
You really fooled us, you really did.

2849
02:00:13,274 --> 02:00:15,122
I kind of expected it, but...

2850
02:00:15,122 --> 02:00:17,082
Because

2851
02:00:17,082 --> 02:00:22,692
coming from Korea
for just a short training stint,

2852
02:00:22,692 --> 02:00:28,186
- being this good right away isn't easy.
- Right, it's strange.

2853
02:00:28,186 --> 02:00:34,458
I had a hunch,
but actually finding out who he was

2854
02:00:34,458 --> 02:00:36,490
- made me go...
- "Wow."

2855
02:00:36,490 --> 02:00:38,182
"Wow."

2856
02:00:38,182 --> 02:00:41,322
If I'd known he was a chef,

2857
02:00:41,322 --> 02:00:45,162
I would've been more nervous and pressured.

2858
02:00:45,162 --> 02:00:47,178
It's better that I found out unexpectedly.

2859
02:00:47,178 --> 02:00:50,522
- It was unexpected.
- It's better that I found out unexpectedly.

2860
02:00:50,522 --> 02:00:52,554
But even if he's a top chef, nothing changes.

2861
02:00:52,554 --> 02:00:54,642
[Antonio's cocky mode: ON]
- Of course. - Just as expected.

2862
02:00:54,642 --> 02:00:56,362
- This is what you'd call cocky.
- Neapolitans

2863
02:00:56,362 --> 02:00:57,866
- have an ego.
- This is what a Neapolitan is like.

2864
02:00:57,866 --> 02:00:59,226
[He's a top chef, so what?]
"So what?"

2865
02:00:59,226 --> 02:01:00,794
- "So what?"
- "What are you gonna do about it?"

2866
02:01:00,794 --> 02:01:04,810
[Top chef or not, a junior's still a junior]
We noticed that he was a good cook.

2867
02:01:04,810 --> 02:01:08,522
- All right, let's get back to it.
- Let's go.

2868
02:01:08,522 --> 02:01:11,112
[Off to the last service!]
Last service, come on.

2869
02:01:11,112 --> 02:01:13,882
Let's do this.

2870
02:01:13,882 --> 02:01:15,194
[7:50 PM]

2871
02:01:15,194 --> 02:01:18,058
[The final service prep begins]

2872
02:01:18,058 --> 02:01:20,090
Okay, let's wipe down the counter.

2873
02:01:20,090 --> 02:01:22,346
[Scrub, scrub]
Now, how will Antonio treat him?

2874
02:01:22,346 --> 02:01:25,082
[Ahem...]
Wow, it's like the first day, so awkward.

2875
02:01:25,082 --> 02:01:28,490
[Feeling awkward, Antonio tries a little joke]

2876
02:01:28,490 --> 02:01:30,122
Now that Chef Kwon's identity is out,

2877
02:01:30,122 --> 02:01:32,362
there's not much difference between him and me.

2878
02:01:32,362 --> 02:01:34,618
[Introverted Sam Sam]
Being all awkward.

2879
02:01:34,618 --> 02:01:37,290
So embarrassing.

2880
02:01:37,290 --> 02:01:40,154
Tonight, everyone should say, "Yes, Chef."

2881
02:01:40,154 --> 02:01:42,378
Yes, Chef!

2882
02:01:42,378 --> 02:01:44,828
[Ehehe, no way]

2883
02:01:44,828 --> 02:01:45,962
No way.

2884
02:01:45,962 --> 02:01:48,042
[Kwon. Soon. Chi. (Chef)]
Kwon Soon Chi.

2885
02:01:48,042 --> 02:01:49,178
"Kwon Soon Chi."

2886
02:01:49,178 --> 02:01:52,746
[Chef Kwon Soon Chi, Napoli Matfia]
Napoli Matfia.

2887
02:01:52,746 --> 02:01:57,088
[To Paolo, this whole situation
is just amusing]

2888
02:01:57,088 --> 02:01:58,634
[While our very own Napoli Matfia
steps away for a moment]

2889
02:01:58,634 --> 02:02:01,333
Watching this the whole time...

2890
02:02:01,333 --> 02:02:02,378
What?

2891
02:02:02,378 --> 02:02:05,082
Did Antonio maybe already know?

2892
02:02:08,025 --> 02:02:11,522
They say Napoli Matfia started following me.

2893
02:02:11,522 --> 02:02:14,128
[What an honor]
They say he started following me.

2894
02:02:14,128 --> 02:02:15,366
So adorable.

2895
02:02:15,366 --> 02:02:17,607
[Jealous?]

2896
02:02:18,330 --> 02:02:19,850
[Sneaking a peek]

2897
02:02:19,850 --> 02:02:21,402
He went to check for himself

2898
02:02:21,402 --> 02:02:23,825
[Did Kwon follow me back too? Awkward]
whether you followed him.

2899
02:02:23,825 --> 02:02:25,160
He's worried that he didn't get a follow.

2900
02:02:25,160 --> 02:02:27,450
[@napolimatfia started following you]

2901
02:02:27,450 --> 02:02:30,074
[Follow back accepted]

2902
02:02:30,074 --> 02:02:31,442
[8:00 PM]

2903
02:02:31,442 --> 02:02:34,072
[Dinner service begins, right on schedule]

2904
02:02:34,072 --> 02:02:36,232
Work is work.

2905
02:02:36,232 --> 02:02:37,862
[Order ticket comes in]

2906
02:02:37,862 --> 02:02:39,562
[Another order ticket]

2907
02:02:39,562 --> 02:02:41,706
Well, time to get to work either way.

2908
02:02:41,706 --> 02:02:43,770
- That's that.
- Gotta finish strong.

2909
02:02:43,770 --> 02:02:45,402
Right to the end.

2910
02:02:45,402 --> 02:02:47,130
[An honor, fixing his chef's hat for him]

2911
02:02:47,130 --> 02:02:50,090
[Oddly polite behavior]
Sam, I have a favor to ask.

2912
02:02:50,090 --> 02:02:53,782
[Order: 4 appetizer platters,
2 cheese & salumi platters, 3 potato flans]

2913
02:02:53,782 --> 02:02:56,858
[All right, let's get started!]
Let's go.

2914
02:02:56,858 --> 02:02:58,122
[Antonio's task]

2915
02:02:58,122 --> 02:02:59,994
[Whoosh]

2916
02:03:00,922 --> 02:03:03,482
I brought over another cutting board.

2917
02:03:03,482 --> 02:03:06,682
- He brought another one over.
- I'll do the cheese platter here.

2918
02:03:06,682 --> 02:03:10,858
[Antonio hands his own station over to Kwon]
Great, go ahead and use this.

2919
02:03:10,858 --> 02:03:13,194
If Kwon plates it, I'll drizzle the oil.

2920
02:03:13,194 --> 02:03:16,314
Two, four, six, eight...

2921
02:03:16,314 --> 02:03:19,162
[5 minutes earlier]
Even if he's a top chef, nothing changes.

2922
02:03:19,162 --> 02:03:22,506
[But face-to-face with Kwon,
he's all sweetness]

2923
02:03:22,506 --> 02:03:26,314
[I'll be the one assisting from now on!]
He's determined to give full assistance.

2924
02:03:28,090 --> 02:03:31,530
[Meanwhile, Paolo, working in the back]

2925
02:03:31,530 --> 02:03:32,826
Emergency, emergency.

2926
02:03:32,826 --> 02:03:34,986
- Emergency, emergency.
- Emergency, emergency.

2927
02:03:34,986 --> 02:03:37,338
"Emergency, emergency" will stay

2928
02:03:37,338 --> 02:03:39,568
- in my heart.
- Emergency.

2929
02:03:39,568 --> 02:03:41,626
Sure.

2930
02:03:41,626 --> 02:03:44,618
Once Kwon leaves, Paolo will

2931
02:03:44,618 --> 02:03:46,874
sometimes...

2932
02:03:46,874 --> 02:03:49,498
["Emergency, emergency" every single day]
"Emergency, emergency."

2933
02:03:49,498 --> 02:03:51,338
[No Kwon, emergency, emergency]
I can hear it already.

2934
02:03:51,338 --> 02:03:53,018
I know it.

2935
02:03:53,018 --> 02:03:57,272
[Kwon's a little sad about it too, deep down]

2936
02:03:57,272 --> 02:04:00,102
[The dining room, once bustling with guests]

2937
02:04:00,102 --> 02:04:02,712
[gradually grows quiet]

2938
02:04:02,712 --> 02:04:05,002
[In a brief moment to catch their breath]

2939
02:04:05,002 --> 02:04:08,138
[There are things that must be done]

2940
02:04:08,138 --> 02:04:10,202
[Can't skip a selfie...]
- Gotta get a selfie too. - Oh, a selfie too.

2941
02:04:10,202 --> 02:04:12,922
[Hats off!]
Gotta post it.

2942
02:04:12,922 --> 02:04:15,818
[Even combs his hair...]

2943
02:04:15,818 --> 02:04:16,938
[Side-eye]

2944
02:04:16,938 --> 02:04:18,887
Why am I being so self-conscious?

2945
02:04:20,549 --> 02:04:22,938
[Now the real photo shoot begins]

2946
02:04:22,938 --> 02:04:24,426
[Bye... Napoli]

2947
02:04:24,426 --> 02:04:25,770
[#LastOne #WellDone #ServiceOver #Myself]
Selfie.

2948
02:04:25,770 --> 02:04:26,922
- Great job, myself.
- Selfie.

2949
02:04:26,922 --> 02:04:29,178
- Myself.
- Looks good on you.

2950
02:04:32,378 --> 02:04:34,810
[Pretending to not have done anything]
They saw it for sure.

2951
02:04:35,930 --> 02:04:39,127
- What's this?
- Please leave me a message.

2952
02:04:39,127 --> 02:04:40,266
A rolling paper.

2953
02:04:40,266 --> 02:04:41,482
Asking them to write something for me.

2954
02:04:41,482 --> 02:04:44,202
He even asked for this himself, personally.

2955
02:04:44,202 --> 02:04:45,994
[Requesting his own rolling paper] [Proud]
Man, this is really...

2956
02:04:45,994 --> 02:04:47,306
Usually, though...

2957
02:04:47,306 --> 02:04:50,378
[Note] [Copy-paste]
Someone else does it, and gives you the gift.

2958
02:04:50,378 --> 02:04:54,170
[A self-appreciated rolling paper]
You don't usually ask for it yourself, though.

2959
02:04:54,170 --> 02:04:57,034
[Q. You prepared
this rolling paper... yourself?]

2960
02:04:57,034 --> 02:04:58,792
Weren't you really touched?

2961
02:04:58,792 --> 02:05:00,314
Isn't it really nice? Really?

2962
02:05:00,314 --> 02:05:01,402
What's the point of it?

2963
02:05:01,402 --> 02:05:03,594
[The romantic Matfia]
- Truly touching. - Right?

2964
02:05:03,594 --> 02:05:05,362
Right?

2965
02:05:05,362 --> 02:05:06,483
Bro.

2966
02:05:06,483 --> 02:05:09,832
Kwon asked us to leave him messages.

2967
02:05:09,832 --> 02:05:12,650
When chefs leave, they often
get signatures on their jacket.

2968
02:05:12,650 --> 02:05:15,270
[What should I write?]
I'm getting it from all the staff.

2969
02:05:16,330 --> 02:05:19,610
[Paolo too, better get a photo]

2970
02:05:19,610 --> 02:05:21,290
[Cute]

2971
02:05:21,290 --> 02:05:23,930
[#Naples_SBN #Paolo #Antonio]

2972
02:05:24,634 --> 02:05:26,618
[Korean and Naples love: We're Napoletanos]
Napoletano.

2973
02:05:26,618 --> 02:05:28,730
Napoletano.

2974
02:05:28,730 --> 02:05:30,482
[Kwon! You're one of us now]

2975
02:05:30,482 --> 02:05:32,858
Paolo really likes you.

2976
02:05:32,858 --> 02:05:37,258
[Thanks for everything, "emergency emergency!"]
"Emergency, emergency," nice handwriting.

2977
02:05:37,258 --> 02:05:40,234
We met by chance

2978
02:05:40,234 --> 02:05:44,282
and by chance
ended up working together every day.

2979
02:05:44,282 --> 02:05:47,114
Sam, you're a special person.

2980
02:05:47,787 --> 02:05:51,578
I was happy to share our cooking with you.

2981
02:05:51,578 --> 02:05:53,338
It really is a memory now.

2982
02:05:53,338 --> 02:05:55,066
[My heart, all warm and fuzzy]
The truth is

2983
02:05:55,066 --> 02:05:56,538
this is how they really feel.

2984
02:05:56,538 --> 02:05:59,258
Those two really mean it.

2985
02:05:59,258 --> 02:06:02,058
[And the last person remaining...]

2986
02:06:02,058 --> 02:06:03,802
[Our Antonio]
- Antonio. - What will Antonio write?

2987
02:06:03,802 --> 02:06:05,642
I'm most curious what Antonio will write.

2988
02:06:05,642 --> 02:06:09,898
[Antonio agonizes over it for a long while]

2989
02:06:09,898 --> 02:06:13,642
[Crowding around]
He's still writing his message.

2990
02:06:13,642 --> 02:06:16,378
[Ooh]

2991
02:06:16,378 --> 02:06:17,818
[All eyes on him]

2992
02:06:17,818 --> 02:06:19,082
How long are you going to write?

2993
02:06:19,082 --> 02:06:21,242
- I haven't written anything yet.
- Nothing yet.

2994
02:06:21,242 --> 02:06:22,858
Wait, hold on.

2995
02:06:22,858 --> 02:06:25,418
[Makes a quick run]
I need some alone time.

2996
02:06:25,418 --> 02:06:27,802
I need some alone time.

2997
02:06:27,802 --> 02:06:31,242
[Cute]
Antonio's getting all sentimental.

2998
02:06:32,010 --> 02:06:35,818
[Antonio left alone,]

2999
02:06:35,818 --> 02:06:41,578
[writes what he wanted to say to Kwon]

3000
02:06:42,234 --> 02:06:45,146
[These past few days were really busy,]

3001
02:06:45,146 --> 02:06:48,730
[but the time flew by in the blink of an eye]
Man, this is basically a love letter.

3002
02:06:48,730 --> 02:06:51,642
[You're such a good person,]
Right, Antonio means it.

3003
02:06:51,642 --> 02:06:54,538
[Kwon, I'm so glad I got to know you!]
He's just a little clumsy with words.

3004
02:06:56,826 --> 02:07:00,682
I don't like the word "last."

3005
02:07:00,682 --> 02:07:02,762
Kwon, we'll always be here.

3006
02:07:02,762 --> 02:07:04,538
Thanks for everything.

3007
02:07:04,538 --> 02:07:06,634
This isn't goodbye,
it's a promise that we'll meet again.

3008
02:07:06,634 --> 02:07:07,738
Man, as expected.

3009
02:07:07,738 --> 02:07:10,082
I especially think Antonio...

3010
02:07:10,082 --> 02:07:13,770
he does joke around a lot,
going "you fooled me" and all that,

3011
02:07:13,770 --> 02:07:15,514
but Antonio's expression

3012
02:07:15,514 --> 02:07:18,618
was really something, that

3013
02:07:18,618 --> 02:07:22,218
not-knowing-what-face-to-make
face, what that meant was

3014
02:07:22,218 --> 02:07:24,298
he really gave it his whole heart.

3015
02:07:24,298 --> 02:07:28,090
Someone he'd truly given his whole heart to,

3016
02:07:28,090 --> 02:07:29,994
but it's like that person just vanished.

3017
02:07:29,994 --> 02:07:31,818
- That kind of feeling.
- I get it.

3018
02:07:31,818 --> 02:07:33,722
I think that's what he felt.

3019
02:07:33,722 --> 02:07:36,842
He nagged and taught me so much,
with total sincerity.

3020
02:07:36,842 --> 02:07:38,814
- Exactly.
- He tried so hard to teach me.

3021
02:07:38,814 --> 02:07:39,866
And that, somehow...

3022
02:07:39,866 --> 02:07:41,882
That just made me tear up watching it.

3023
02:07:41,882 --> 02:07:44,602
Yeah, I think I know what you mean.

3024
02:07:45,338 --> 02:07:50,426
People sort of get why I kept
going on and on about Naples, but...

3025
02:07:50,426 --> 02:07:53,850
since they've never actually seen it,
they can't really understand it fully.

3026
02:07:53,850 --> 02:07:55,802
Why I love Naples so much,

3027
02:07:55,802 --> 02:07:58,330
why I had no choice
but to become the Napoli Matfia.

3028
02:07:58,330 --> 02:08:00,122
[Miss you so much]
I miss you.

3029
02:08:00,122 --> 02:08:02,154
Kwon, I miss you.

3030
02:08:02,154 --> 02:08:04,058
[Eyes teary...]
Hey, no!

3031
02:08:04,058 --> 02:08:06,194
Gosh!

3032
02:08:07,032 --> 02:08:08,794
Oh no, she's crying.

3033
02:08:08,794 --> 02:08:10,362
The time I spent with Kwon was so good.

3034
02:08:10,362 --> 02:08:13,306
- I really grew attached to him.
- Me too.

3035
02:08:13,306 --> 02:08:14,970
I really grew attached, for real.

3036
02:08:14,970 --> 02:08:17,922
[Getting teary too...]
- I got so attached. - Yeah.

3037
02:08:17,922 --> 02:08:20,390
She's crying, oh my.

3038
02:08:20,390 --> 02:08:24,602
[In Naples, Kwon's Undercover journey ends]
It's impossible not to love this place.

3039
02:08:24,602 --> 02:08:26,472
I knew it all along, I'm telling you.

3040
02:08:26,472 --> 02:08:29,354
[Napoli cocky mode: ON]
I think he's a Korean restaurant owner.

3041
02:08:29,354 --> 02:08:31,546
[Sneaking a glance for no reason]
- Ah, right now. - No, why is he

3042
02:08:31,546 --> 02:08:33,290
[Amazed]
being so awkward like this?

3043
02:08:33,290 --> 02:08:35,466
[Me, rolling beef with a celebrity like this?]

3044
02:08:35,466 --> 02:08:37,902
Aren't you coming?

3045
02:08:37,902 --> 02:08:39,282
[Scurrying over]

3046
02:08:39,282 --> 02:08:41,306
Give me your phone, I'll take the photo!

3047
02:08:41,306 --> 02:08:42,746
[One shot]

3048
02:08:42,746 --> 02:08:47,133
Gotta take a bunch!
So we can pick the best one!

3049
02:08:47,133 --> 02:08:50,342
[Chengdu's cutie, MZ Kai]
Xu Jian Kai is adorable.

3050
02:08:50,342 --> 02:08:52,458
[Beaming]
Nice to see.

3051
02:08:52,458 --> 02:08:55,002
Lu! Do you have any plans to study English?

3052
02:08:55,002 --> 02:08:57,594
In my head.

3053
02:08:57,594 --> 02:08:59,387
What's your English name again?

3054
02:08:59,387 --> 02:09:00,341
Sam...

3055
02:09:00,341 --> 02:09:01,806
No, don't change it.

3056
02:09:01,806 --> 02:09:03,658
[Your name's confiscated, Hee Tae!]
No, don't change it.

3057
02:09:03,658 --> 02:09:04,922
We've gotta have a showdown at least once.

3058
02:09:04,922 --> 02:09:07,786
[Let's do Parma vs. Naples!]
- A showdown. - Has to be Naples versus Parma.

3059
02:09:07,786 --> 02:09:09,018
No, wait, that's not written right.

3060
02:09:09,018 --> 02:09:10,887
[Squeeze]
Hold on, no, it's this way.

3061
02:09:10,887 --> 02:09:13,233
- My circulation's cut off!
- No, it's like this, this way.

3062
02:09:13,233 --> 02:09:14,538
- Suits you well.
- Kind of looks like a painter.

3063
02:09:14,538 --> 02:09:15,811
A painter.

3064
02:09:15,811 --> 02:09:17,884
Do it like this, you're a painter,
or you're a cook.

3065
02:09:17,884 --> 02:09:19,189
Wait, suddenly, uh-oh...

3066
02:09:19,189 --> 02:09:22,366
Seems like she's gonna
make the staff meal again.

3067
02:09:22,366 --> 02:09:25,219
I'll make the staff meal today.
